er Tech (Oct 12-16): Big Banks Reports Earnings, Anthropic Revenue Jumps 45% & More - Benzinga", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi0AFBVV95cUxQRlZnaWpsUGZjaTQzbUV5Y2M0UnpYMU1EVUZENW13bS0yZV9obG1GSDhUZDBZZzEzbTV5bGxzeE9jbVVDc0xDbnJsYXFZVzVqMVVXdGpXdHFJMU1hUTJvOWNGSzROUHZPaXFXa0tqbVYySnlueXRLeUpHVzVPNV9MRWZXUFhIY3RpQTVhX0pLcDExaXlBSlRJU2RNZXdnLWFqTm4zajdGMW9vOHUtRnJkbWx5aXpOYTJEU182TGQyQUx", "source": "lane_print_vs_priced", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:51:02+00:00", "text": "Consumer Tech (Oct 12-16): Big Banks Reports Earnings, Anthropic Revenue Jumps 45% & More - Benzinga\nConsumer Tech (Oct 12-16): Big Banks Reports Earnings, Anthropic Revenue Jumps 45% & More Benzinga", "truncated": false}, {"id": "e0177956ea86438862a144ba", "title": "Somali Senate Passes National Meteorological Agency Bill - Somali National News Agency", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxQMnVvdTRCbWZ6N1RpUnpOMGpiOUY5c2tEcG1sVXNhRG1NSlI0eEJ4eVlpWnNxVU5lQnFFNzdiaHJwa2lobUdUUXFja25Yb0RmNXNIUHRYUkVVTHVPSTdlZmJyRk1TbjN6N1YySFptZVV5S2pVdGxXZU9YaWxJNnFadjVENEU1VEgyZ096aA?oc=5", "source": "topic_legislation", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:50:17+00:00", "text": "Somali Senate Passes National Meteorological Agency Bill - Somali National News Agency\nSomali Senate Passes National Meteorological Agency Bill Somali National News Agency", "truncated": false}, {"id": "297499b6b343491accac4c27", "title": "From fuel subsidies to gas investment: a shared opportunity for Iraq - 964media", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiREFVX3lxTFBNcHZtZkNBUnJpRlFjaUpRX3BBbmFSWS1GNnVyVFJidEttdXlfRmo1dGxoUklyMmZ5UjhCdkg1Y2xJR1d2?oc=5", "source": "lane_subsidy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:49:36+00:00", "text": "From fuel subsidies to gas investment: a shared opportunity for Iraq - 964media\nFrom fuel subsidies to gas investment: a shared opportunity for Iraq 964media", "truncated": false}, {"id": "4e7fbd2db9fa27e500c0e2cc", "title": "Child, four women among Palestinians injured in West Bank pogroms", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/17/several-palestinians-injured-detained-in-ongoing-west-bank-pogrom?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:48:03+00:00", "text": "Child, four women among Palestinians injured in West Bank pogroms\nShare Israeli settlers attack European diplomats during West Bank olive harvest on social media\nAn Israeli soldier fires a tear gas grenade towards Palestinian olive pickers during the olive harvest on October 17, 2026, in Abu Falah, West Bank [Faiz Abu Rmeleh/Getty Images]\nIsraeli settlers have attacked European diplomats, including a French mayor, near the Palestinian village of Taybeh in the occupied West Bank.\nThe delegation was visiting Palestinian olive harvesters on Saturday when the Israeli attackers confronted the group. The attack comes a day after settlers\nIn Saturday’s incident, the settlers targeted Belgium’s consul general, French and Polish diplomats, and Catholic representatives, Belgian Minister of Foreign Affairs Maxime Prevot said.\n“A French mayor was assaulted and a Belgian vehicle damaged,” Prevot said, linking the attack to Israel’s “illegal settlement policy” and pledging to push for further European Union sanctions.\nBernard Baudoux, the French mayor who was assaulted, told the AFP news agency the attack suggests that “there is a tolerance on the part of the Israeli government” towards settler violence.\nVideo shared by an activist at the scene, Amit Orfali, shows Baudoux leaning against a vehicle while sitting on the dusty ground. Other clips showed young masked men knocking insistently on a driver’s side window and asking for identification, while other masked men carrying sticks advanced in the distance. Orfali said the masked men “threatened to kill us”.\nFrance’s foreign minister, Jean-Noel Barrot, called on Israel to arrest the “extremist settlers” who “violently assaulted” Baudoux, and bring them to justice. “They must urgently halt this criminal violence and guarantee the safety of civilian populations, as they are compelled to do under international law,” he said in a post on X.\nAl Jazeera’s Nour Odeh, reporting from Ramallah, said the settlers had surrounded the diplomats’ vehicles before pelting them with stones and smashing their windows.\nThe assault has prompted an Israeli police investigation and condemnation from Belgium, as settler pogroms disrupt the Palestinian harvest across the occupied territory.\nIsraeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s office, however, appeared to question the reports of the attack on the Europeans, saying on X that they are “alleged” and require “compelling evidence”, despite acknowledging that published footage of the incident exists.\nEarlier on Saturday, several Palestinians were injured by Israeli settlers, as Israeli forces arrested farmers during\nFour women and a child were among six people injured when Israeli settlers attacked residents in Ma’in village in the Masafer Yatta area, south of Hebron, according to the Palestine Red Crescent Society (PRCS).\nIn the town of Deir Ammar, west of Ramallah, Israeli forces opened fire on farmers picking olives, forcing them to leave their land, according to the Palestinian news agency Wafa. In the same area, Israeli settlers shot and injured two Palestinians.\nIn the village of Tuqu, southeast of Bethlehem, Israeli forces fired on a Palestinian civilian vehicle.\nIn the village of Kafr Malek, northeast of Ramallah, settlers raided a farm at dawn and killed about 20 sheep, Mayor Najeh Rustum told Al Jazeera.\nAl Jazeera’s Odeh said settlers also destroyed olive trees across the Beit Furik plain, east of Nablus, in the northern West Bank, while Israeli forces arrested landowners and olive pickers.\nIn the village of Deir Jarir, east of Ramallah, she said settlers under army protection fired live ammunition at farmers in the al-Hariq area to prevent them from completing the harvest, forcing them off their land.\nSettlers also smashed the vehicle of international activist Jonathan Budlak in the village and threw stones at a farmer’s vehicle.\nIn the village of Burqa near Ramallah, Israeli forces and settlers prevented farmers from picking olives, Odeh said, adding that settlers attacked farmers in the Wadi al-Sha’er area, southeast of Salfit.\nA settler throws a stone towards Palestinians in Abu Falah near Ramallah on October 16, 2026, during pogroms against Palestinians trying to harvest olives [Ammar Awad/Reuters]\n“What we see, whether it’s in Beit Furik, Kafr Malek, Deir Jarir or elsewhere in the occupied West Bank, is part of a campaign,” Odeh said.\nShe said settlers have become increasingly emboldened, publicly advertising attack campaigns on social media platforms.\n“There have been 300 documented attacks since the beginning of October, and that has had a devastating impact on a very important season for Palestinian farmers,” she said, adding that danger comes from soldiers and settlers alike, as military forces routinely intervene to protect settlers and attack Palestinians defending their land.\n, a prominent rabbi for Israel’s National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvir’s Jewish Power party and a leading authority among the\n, a religious Zionist group devoted to seizing Palestinian land in the occupied West Bank.\nIn the edict, Lior stated that harvesting olives in the “Holy Land” is entirely permitted for Jews and carries an added virtue, given security dangers.\nHe wrote that Jews are permitted to harvest olives even in areas far from Israeli communities to publicly display ownership of the land and fulfil God’s commandment of conquering it. He claimed the land belongs to the Jewish people, and Palestinians did not buy or rent it.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "61c61c518c9fa60c44f785ef", "title": "Davidovich Fokina stuns top seed Zverev to reach Shanghai Masters final", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/17/davidovich-fokina-stuns-top-seed-zverev-to-reach-shanghai-masters-final?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:46:48+00:00", "text": "Davidovich Fokina stuns top seed Zverev to reach Shanghai Masters final\nShare Davidovich Fokina stuns top seed Zverev to reach Shanghai Masters final on social media\nSpain's Alejandro Davidovich Fokina celebrates his victory against Germany's Alexander Zverev during their men's singles semifinal at the Shanghai Masters tennis tournament [AFP]\nAlejandro ‌Davidovich Fokina produced a major upset by defeating top seed\n5-7 ⁠6-4 6-3 to reach the Shanghai Masters final, where he will face either former world number one Daniil Medvedev or fellow Spaniard Rafael Jodar.\nThe 25th seed fired ⁠36 winners in the two-hour, two-minute contest on Saturday to secure only his second victory over Zverev in eight meetings. His previous win against the German came in the round of ⁠32 at the Canadian Open in 2023.\nDavidovich Fokina earned his first break of the match to take the second set, forcing a decider with a stunning backhand passing shot on the run that capped a bruising baseline exchange and brought the crowd to their feet.\nCarrying that momentum into ‌the final set, Davidovich Fokina broke Zverev for a 2-0 lead and never relinquished control, booking a place in the second ATP Masters 1000 final of his career after finishing runner-up in Monte Carlo in 2022.\nLanding 82 percent of his first serves and repeatedly exposing Zverev on the forehand side, he secured one of the biggest victories of his career.\n“I knew that if I stayed there all match, I could get at least ⁠one chance and I took it there in the second set,” ⁠Davidovich Fokina said.\n“Then in the third set, I think I was better physically. The early break in the third set gave me a lot of power.\n“I focused on just playing, not mattering about the result but enjoying.”\nZverev said fatigue had caught up with him.\n“I think a break is quite necessary now,” the 29-year-old told reporters, saying he would monitor his fitness before a tournament in Vienna that begins October 24.\n“I carried a little bit of injury, I carried fatigue into the tournament, and I’m OK to lose to a player like this today,” said Zverev, who had felt his ankle at times in Shanghai.\nDavidovich ⁠Fokina, who missed the North American hard-court swing in August because of injury, has now won nine consecutive matches in China after ⁠lifting his second tour-level title at the ATP 250 ⁠event in Chengdu last month.\nIt was a disappointing end to the week for Zverev, a seven-time ATP Masters 1000 champion whose best result in Shanghai remains his runner-up finish to Medvedev in 2019.\nThe 29-year-old has otherwise enjoyed a ‌fine season, ending his Grand Slam drought at the French Open before claiming a second major title at the US Open and securing the ATP year-end\n‌after ‌Jannik Sinner was sidelined for the remainder of the season with a knee injury.\nFifth-seeded Russian Medvedev was playing 12th-seeded Jodar, 20, in the second semifinal.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "886830dbdac951203f4c38e0", "title": "Fujifilm plans $18 million Mesa expansion to boost semiconductor materials production - KTAR News 92.3 FM", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTFBuaTJhSGFWQkdBMDllTTRWTnV4QUVzMVZBR21kZTRxVWNPX2praUdwTHpmeHBlc3dCb3ZaYy0tOG9rNlZTRE9YVFVrN0pGMVFKckdPUjBpWFBobFRRV3FYbUdMbm5aSVlGRHpzOHdRODltdmdBZzBTMDdJSzZLSEE?oc=5", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:46:47+00:00", "text": "Fujifilm plans $18 million Mesa expansion to boost semiconductor materials production - KTAR News 92.3 FM\nFujifilm plans $18 million Mesa expansion to boost semiconductor materials production KTAR News 92.3 FM", "truncated": false}, {"id": "2b0863b802374b43bac4925e", "title": "GTCR Leads $200 Million Second Lien Term Loan For Sophos Refinancing - Pulse 2.0", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss