12:38:00+00:00", "text": "Russia celebrates Trump's sanctions waiver while Ukraine warns it will encourage attacks - WVTM Channel 13\nRussia celebrates Trump's sanctions waiver while Ukraine warns it will encourage attacks WVTM Channel 13", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8e2aa409f0824ff1d73c66ca", "title": "Pope to be discharged days after lung cancer surgery", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5x2vkddrkrko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:37:26+00:00", "text": "Pope to be discharged days after lung cancer surgery\nSouthern and Eastern Europe correspondent\nPope Leo XIV has been discharged from Rome's Gemelli Hospital, just four days after an operation to remove a cancerous growth from his lung.\nThe 71-year-old walked unaided to his waiting car, stopping to speak to well-wishers.\nThe Vatican said the Pope will give the traditional Angelus prayer and blessing to a crowd in St Peter's Square on Sunday, as he did last week when he surprised the world by announcing the surgery.\nOn Friday, photographs were released of the Pope celebrating Mass and distributing communion in hospital for staff.\nA statement from his doctors said blood tests and a chest X-ray showed \"steady improvement\" following his operation.\nThe surgery on Tuesday, which lasted for 90 minutes, included the removal of the lower lobe of the Pope's right lung. The results of further tests to check for any sign that the cancer has spread have not yet been announced.\nThe Pope also spoke to Russian President Vladimir Putin on Friday, in their first call since June 2025. The Vatican said the call was to urge \"dialogue and peace\".\nIt came as Russia's bombardment of cities across Ukraine intensifies, with a growing number of civilian casualties and no sign of Putin being ready to halt the invasion.\nThe Pope also called for a humanitarian ceasefire in the Ukrainian city of Oleshkiy, occupied by Russia and under constant shelling, to allow people to be evacuated and for the urgent delivery of food and medicine. The BBC recently reported on residents there\nbeing forced to eat garden weeds to survive.\nThe Pope's schedule has been cleared completely until 20 October, so his reappearance in public so soon is a surprise and will be some relief for Catholics around the world.\nThose close to the Pope said he was keen not to delay a trip to Latin America, planned for early November and which includes a visit to Peru, where he was a missionary for many years.\nIt is not yet clear whether he might be fit to travel or require further treatment.\nPope pictured for first time since surgery and cancer diagnosis\nPope diagnosed with lung cancer but had successful surgery, Vatican says\nPope's health should not be taken 'for granted', says top Vatican diplomat", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "f43a52e32a087533029e45a2", "title": "Safe Havens, Dwindling Assets: What SSR’s Roxmore Acquisition Means for Gold M&A - Crux Investor", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxNb2tXVUplelpCRExhSGIwamt1bmltZFJMbnNSVXpEZFp6R1h6SkVaeENOQ3NKTTJ6Yk1HQUxZMG4tX29nM2pPd0txd0NlRzVsazB6LTF2dHdvRm1ERlJPMml6eVFDU3BacFBybndaazZlRHExcDVvb1R6Nm12eTlQQThwQ0E4RjgxMVBOb2JKbWlaenhjVkxYMzA1dTczQXZhZEFmQ3lWa0pvYlhiMURyVDZ3?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-17T12:37:25+00:00", "text": "Safe Havens, Dwindling Assets: What SSR’s Roxmore Acquisition Means for Gold M&A - Crux Investor\nSafe Havens, Dwindling Assets: What SSR’s Roxmore Acquisition Means for Gold M&A Crux Investor", "truncated": false}, {"id": "50093982cd9a9b787d023c46", "title": "Estuary Biotherapeutics Launches With $103 Million To Develop Gene Therapies For Kidney Disease - Pulse 2.0", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxNVU1vOGtsOFhJbnRoRXVOaVVEVUt2VDJ4UVZ1anFOZlV3WkhCWmlmazVSMHlKalRNYkY4aDBIM2VyZHM0Z2JienNNSmQ2SWN4T0xCMkZGQUlvWm9qaXZ4bHNhcExibmFMNVBFT0ZMbDluQloyajFER3dRVVYtOHY2Y2NuZno