FBZ3BkYmw0dGE4MjJkTnY1LU0zZUtHN1hlOXhQanZ0UXVpMHhQMWJLbGNybElJTThxMEE?oc=5", "source": "lane_factor_impulse", "published_at": "2026-10-17T11:35:00+00:00", "text": "Gold Faces Year-End Downward Pressure...\"90% Odds of Fed Rate Hike in December\" - BigGo Finance\nGold Faces Year-End Downward Pressure...\"90% Odds of Fed Rate Hike in December\" BigGo Finance", "truncated": false}, {"id": "dea4b835be153c7270925bd8", "title": "Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-rdf", "source": "rss_dw_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T11:34:00+00:00", "text": "Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy\nZaporizhzia in eastern Ukraine came under renewed attack overnight\nis stepping up its attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure in a bid to cut electricity and heating in the country as winter approaches, Ukraine's President\nHis remarks come as Moscow intensifies its attacks on civilian targets in the capital, Kyiv, and elsewhere, with\nkey observers saying its objective is to render the country virtually unlivable.\nOvernight strikes on Zaporizhzhia killed a 64-year-old man\nIn a post on social media platform X, Zelenskyy said Russia had just carried out one of its biggest attacks on\nfull-scale invasion of its neighbor in February 2022.\n\"More than 15 critical power generation and transmission facilities were targeted across different regions of Ukraine,\" he wrote.\n\"Restoration work is ongoing, with all necessary services and all available resources of Ukrainian energy companies involved,\" he added.\nZelenskyy said that Russia was planning to leave Ukrainian citizens in the cold this winter.\n\"Russia is trying to cause a blackout in Ukraine — right before winter. Russia is trying to leave millions of our people without electricity and heating,\" he wrote, calling on allies to put pressure on Moscow to stop this happening.\nHe said Russia had \"expanded ‌its campaign ​against the energy system\" and was trying \"to stretch ⁠Ukraine's ​reserves ​and repair ​capacity as ‌thinly as possible.\" ​\nRussia claims multiple infrastructure attacks\nThe Russian Defense Ministry, for its part, said on Saturday that its forces had attacked several infrastructure targets in Ukraine overnight.\nAmong those named was an electricity substation in the northwestern city of Zhytomyr.\nHowever, it also said Ukraine's largest steelworks, in the city of Kryvyi Rih, had been hit, saying the facility supplied steel products to the Ukrainian military-industrial complex.\nIt said another steel plant in ​Zaporizhzhia, a city near the front ​line, had also been struck.\nUkrainian authorities have also said that one person — an ambulance driver — was killed ​and ‌19 others injured, including a child, in a Russian airstrike on Kherson in southern Ukraine.\nRussian state news ​agency TASS has also reported the death of one woman as a result of Ukrainian drone strikes in Russia's Belgorod region that also injured a man.\nRussia's overnight attacks hit numerous civilian sites\nTrump's sanctions waiver a boost for Putin: Zelenskyy\nUS President Donald Trump's decision to waive a package of new sanctions on Moscow,\nsaying the move would only encourage Russian leader\n\"A US sanctions blackout, easing pressure on the aggressor, financial rewards for Putin — all of this only encourages him to keep attacking,\" Zelenskyy said.\nOn Friday, Trump signed an executive order that waived sweeping US sanctions and tariffs targeting Russia's energy revenues, two days before they were due to take effect.\nThe waiver has been hailed by a Russian presidential envoy as a \"historic moment.\"\n\"The Trump administration's suspension of the [Lindsey] Graham Act is an important and truly historic moment,\" Kirill Dmitriev said on social media.\n, \"would have caused \"serious damage first and foremost to the US economy and global markets.\"\nfueling speculation that the US leader is siding with Moscow in the conflict.\nIf you rely on our team for trusted reporting, please take a moment to select us as your\n, so you'll always see our verified news first.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "ba91e92cf67de25fe1231a4e", "title": "Open Text (OTEX) Could Be 9% Below Fair Value On Its $1b Refinancing Move - Simply Wall Street", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizAFBVV95cUxObmxGQ3BDeVgwQUJERW9nRU1DYU9JcEZEYTB1U1psaXlWcjY5c2k0TzJ3WWVITUVrSDd3bl9WN04zZFhIRm5odzRKS1BxVW5weDdQOEc5RUZHcXNtaU1LbTh2NjlXWk54YlZDbFc4eGxhUE1xWFRwdkxlMmxtei1WaGJ0LUMzUExJZUxVRENlbHFsdTFBY1lmZWZBV0RXemtVTGM1cFV5dDM2R0FRUUFvU1R6dDZtbFlBY1k5NmE0WmV", "source": "lane_credit_funding", "published_at": "2026-10-17T11:33:58+00:00", "text": "Open Text (OTEX) Could Be 9% Below Fair Value On Its $1b Refinancing Move - Simply Wall Street\nOpen Text (OTEX) Could Be 9% Below Fair Value On Its $1b Refinancing Move Simply Wall Street", "truncated": false}, {"id": "23fb99b42ac36e13d4673da2", "title": "How Strong Demand And Higher Earnings Estimates Will Impact Cintas Stock - Simply Wall Street", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi0AFBVV95cUxPeDVmR0ptY3RZRkFwRHVCeHhDa0J0Sy0tWXRrbUdPTUhldjgzRlFLYS04S1Rld3VFVDQ0djk3SWgzYzhuTjh2N2FWY204TzJKdVBFLTRsY2libUQ0bTd0NTgzYnE0c1BSYklndHNyTmlUcTMwc3p3ak5nU2VVVDlTVkQyMk5OU09IZVlTb1p0VjlFV2NCN0VaQ2dnaDZvdVJrSGtNNG92QVRLVXVNLUhWZy1WMXlPdnYzR3RxVUh3SHd", "source": "rss_google_markets", "published_at": "2026-10-17T11:33:57+00:00", "text": "How Strong Demand And Higher Earnings Estimates Will Impact Cintas Stock - Simply Wall Street\nHow Strong Demand And Higher Earnings Estimates Will Impact Cintas Stock Simply Wall Street", "truncated": false}, {"id": "9af3c504088eb21100da1f00", "title": "Oyedele: Nigeria won’t return to petrol subsidy, forex distortions as reversal could trigger investor flight - TheCable", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiy