at it means for Amgen stock ad-hoc-news.de", "truncated": false}, {"id": "131b1f0cf30c0dc5a9d3f03d", "title": "Wildfire prompts thousands of evacuation orders in Orange County", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/10/17/wildfire-prompts-thousands-of-evacuation-orders-in-orange-county?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:03:26+00:00", "text": "Wildfire prompts thousands of evacuation orders in Orange County\nWildfire prompts thousands of evacuation orders in Orange County | Wildlife | Al Jazeera\nWildfire prompts thousands of evacuation orders in Orange County\nFirefighters are battling fast-moving wildfires in California’s southern Orange County as strong Santa Ana winds fan the flames. At least six homes have burned as thousands have been ordered to evacuate.\nShare Wildfire prompts thousands of evacuation orders in Orange County on social media", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "ca032d311672b3951822e883", "title": "More than $1.3 million in government subsidies lured Breeze Airways to Arnold Palmer Regional Airport - TribLIVE.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi2AFBVV95cUxQT0ZwTy1JTWlmdTF0RjFnNW9RLWkxV3JGOVNrUEN0S0RUZXVXVW80MWNkSUtQY0VXMWZET3Vqc2psWEZxYWpodHBGSEw4TTBUNkFCRDZLSE8wX1E0V1FWUzlydWtYYXhlMnI0OGpIT1U4TC1OVVAxSWZKQjJBSU5qYkJzbThKODQ0WF8wOENkWXRDS1ZObmt0aGh3WHplMUR6UmhvSTN2VUJ5RHVrTzFVQTNXSVFweTNtVXh3ZXFLUjV", "source": "lane_subsidy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:03:23+00:00", "text": "More than $1.3 million in government subsidies lured Breeze Airways to Arnold Palmer Regional Airport - TribLIVE.com\nMore than $1.3 million in government subsidies lured Breeze Airways to Arnold Palmer Regional Airport TribLIVE.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d833f71f7ecc9ff93ba8ced7", "title": "U.S. News: Top U.S. News Today - AP News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiP0FVX3lxTFBlSV95cW15dzRMN3BweVV5a2ZVclpfUE5TYWRCWGtHX1VOX1JuNklpQVZ0NnQ1Q3diNDlUbmNPYw?oc=5", "source": "rss_ap_topnews:google_fallback", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:02:02+00:00", "text": "U.S. News: Top U.S. News Today - AP News\nU.S. News: Top U.S. News Today AP News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "0ea9f57b23a6d55c3b05394a", "title": "France braces for nationwide protests", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/france-braces-for-nationwide-protests/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-rdf", "source": "rss_dw_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:02:00+00:00", "text": "France braces for nationwide protests\nFirefighters had a busy day and night across France\nPolice and protesters clashed amid mass rallies across\non Saturday, over high prices and social inequalities and the state of the education system.\nFrance's Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said some 1,200 people had been arrested across the country and that 150 police officers had been injured.\n\"It's a miracle the toll wasn't higher,\" Lecornu said while visiting officers deployed in Paris on Saturday evening.\nSaturday's rallies follow weeks of protests by France's youth\nInterior Minister Laurent Nunez said 110,000 people took part in the demonstrations in Paris alone, while 110 marches had taken place across the country.\nHundreds of thousands turn out across France\nThe Interior Ministry said some 550,000 people turned out for the nationwide demonstrations.\nThe ministry said the arrests were made following violent incidents in Paris, Marseilles, Rennes, Toulouse, Angers and other cities across the country.\n\"Such actions include attempted looting, confrontations with law enforcement, the setting of fires to street furniture and the targeting of seats of power and media outlets,\" the ministry said, blaming the unrest on what it described ​as the \"hard-left.\"\nHundreds of people were arrested, including over 800 in Paris\nIn Paris and Marseille, police fired tear gas at protesters as violent clashes took place.\nAFP reported that dozens of shops were looted in Paris, Marseille, Nice, Bordeaux and Lille.\nThe windows of the offices of French broadcasters CNews and Europe 1 in western Paris were also broken by protesters, and AFP journalists reported seeing several parked cars torched.\ncondemned the violence in a post on X and warned: \"Those who have broken, attacked the prefectures as well as businesses, looted even our town halls, will be prosecuted and punished.\"\nIn Lyon, situated in central France, the city's tourism office was set alight with flames and black smoke seen billowing from the building.\nLyon's tourism office was set alight during chaotic scenes\nIn the city of Limoges, the town hall was set alight as unrest broke out. The blaze spread from a wing of the building and eventually reached the roof, where it continued burning as crowds stood watching.\nThe historic building was largely destroyed by the blaze, despite attempts by firefighters to douse the flames.\nMeanwhile, in the northern city of Lille, protesters smashed their way into the city hall and vandalized the premises before leaving, according to an AFP photographer.\nThe 19th-century town hall building was largely destroyed by fire after unrest erupted in Limoges\nRiot police within minutes confirmed that all the protesters had left.\ninitial wave of demonstrations that began last month over the situation at schools in the country\n, with pupils complaining about teacher absences and run-down facilities.\nTo view this video please enable JavaScript, and consider upgrading to a web browser that\nIn the French capital, police had banned rallies around the Elysee presidential palace, the prime minister's office and the Champs-Elysees avenue, along with other key locations.\nA march through the center of the city was also banned.\nReports began emerging late on Saturday morning of riot police clashing with protesters in the Saint-Denis area on the outskirts of the capital, as well as near the Gare du Nord train station, among other areas.\nFrench police were out in force near the Place de la Republique in Paris\nScenes of unrest 'don't paint full picture'\nIn Paris, DW correspondent Jack Parrock said unrest was playing out in small pockets of the city.\n\"The videos circulating on social media of the violence in France don’t paint the full picture,\" Parrock said.\n\"The significant percentage of the people we met out on the streets of Paris were teachers, nurses, students, and workers, who want no part in the unrest, but do also seem to understand why the outbreaks are happening,\" Parrock explained.\n\"Amongst those people, we did still witness a collective rage against a government they don’t feel is listening to them,\" said Parrock.\nOn the matter of how police were responding, Parrock said they had seen police \"seemingly try to show some restraint — clearly intending to de-escalate some of the recent tension.\"\nFrance protests escalate as unrest spreads across cities\nTo view this video please enable JavaScript, and consider upgrading to a web browser that\nStudents have been joined by trade unionists and remnants of the\n(\"Gilets jaunes\") movement, which staged mass weekly protests from November 2018 to June 2020, initially against rising fuel prices. They later morphed into protests against the high cost of living and economic inequality in general.\nThe student protests over the past weeks have been backed by Jean-Luc Melenchon, the leader of the hard-left France Unbowed (\"La France insoumise\", or LFI), who marched in one demonstration on Tuesday.\nThe government has blamed the LFI for pouring fuel on the fire of widespread public discontent, an allegation the party has denied.\nEdited by: Karl Sexton, Jenipher Camino, Sean Sinico\nIf you rely on our team for trusted reporting, please take a moment to\nselect us as your Preferred Source on Google\n, so you'll always see our verified news first.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "6210d64050830308bb5d5ab5", "title": "Magnitude 5.6 earthquake strikes Pakistan's Balochistan province - Gulf News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxNY1luelVrS2pDbEZUWVNUQmZFVWNZalU3ampoel9Gc1h6ci1rdng2bkV4bWxZWVE5bzJDMk43dm5pOENuZ1ZRSzBESGoycGtSMFBMajFhbXFDVWdOQno0V2lRT1ZvUXJDemZFSjEtLWpDMU1pVFFQdU5aT1huVFpndkduOE1BOFh5cHZlT2dGME5SOUl4XzlTWjFGLUFsZFBGVDNnS2UwdTViSGo5Y05YWnROS3otdw?oc=5", "source": "lane_cat_weather", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:01:49+00:00", "text": "Magnitude 5.6 earthquake strikes Pakistan's Balochistan province - Gulf News\nMagnitude 5.6 earthquake strikes Pakistan's Balochistan province Gulf News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "0f8d660869c992e79e03b543", "title": "ECB's Lagarde says bond selloff will slow inflation - Reuters", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxORnNpbWFQTVJFZTQ1NDEzNVA1QlMyNThGdl8tR19Bd0UtQTAyVnBGRFBldDVOMFFnRHR0WkRHaS1CODVMSUFvSTZJdzN5a2NSbHFLbHA2bnZ0ZVBXYUprYS1oeGN6eF9lakVpVmRTSVB6VkpwUzlOVXZCME5ldGVmNmZPTUtuSGVnRTZzbENrQ1pGcFlScVZ1Sl9rQ1pHWUo1c1l4VUJn?oc=5", "source": "publisher_reuters", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:01:43+00:00", "text": "ECB's Lagarde says bond selloff will slow inflation - Reuters\nECB's Lagarde says bond selloff will slow inflation Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "c51bb4fbcb9fb0e3546891a6", "title": "China Plans AI Export Controls Covering Advanced Models, Agents and Chip Designs - International Business Times, Singapore Edition", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxPRGFTVVBUaFdrRU5zbEh4bzVRZlZVT29kQjB3NzRBVk81MWtWajNJMzhfTER1WjVHbkZaelpXWGxCSkVGZlpVajNfVWVudW50SUlvRTlxQWZwdU1qc2lfODZ4R1hSbnk0ZnNQMDJGR2tHWTFNc3VTOEdKOENadXRvRU5VcG96Q1JxM3I1MUlGeTNzdlRFb2Vfdk42TE5QLW8td0xWRm9udw?oc=5", "source": "lane_access_control", "published_at": "2026-10-17T08:01:01+00:00", "text": "China Plans AI Export Controls Covering Advanced Models, Agents and Chip Designs - International Business Times, Singapore Edition\nChina Plans AI Export Controls Covering Advanced Models, Agents and Chip Designs International B