published_at": "2026-10-17T06:18:37+00:00", "text": "Brent crude oil prices hit $110 for first time since May as Iran attacks continue, Ukraine eyes Russia ene - The Economic Times\nBrent crude oil prices hit $110 for first time since May as Iran attacks continue, Ukraine eyes Russia ene The Economic Times", "truncated": false}, {"id": "17853736d8c7c434feeb8386", "title": "Brentcrude oil prices hit $110 for first time since May as Iran attacks continue, Ukraine eyes Russia energy infra - The Economic Times", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwJBVV95cUxNc2JkbEdCZWlVdnpieDd0a25kdTdWU0xENVdpeE1kQUdpLTNCQlJBYktaVGk5VjNremY3eFQ1akZTWjA0MHdzM2VhZDhWYmRaTUtodWhPdDdybWpReGhVMDZoLVF6SHRiaUJ5Q0FXUWRCT3VPYUgybVlXbG5LcmJENmpBaC05clViaTY2SVJianlFd3kxeTh3X0hLUnZ1X2Q4TG5OS2FERGM0aTM3ajRudUJsM3Q1dlZydXhreWE4Z0U", "source": "lane_regime_state", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:18:37+00:00", "text": "Brentcrude oil prices hit $110 for first time since May as Iran attacks continue, Ukraine eyes Russia energy infra - The Economic Times\nBrentcrude oil prices hit $110 for first time since May as Iran attacks continue, Ukraine eyes Russia energy infra The Economic Times", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8980f89c0231959facfaec71", "title": "Call for more food funding due to high living cost", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqde8zk6d916o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_business", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:18:16+00:00", "text": "Call for more food funding due to high living cost\nDeputy Louise Doublet said she thought the cost of living was not taken into consideration in the decision\nA Jersey politician said she thought cost-of-living pressures were not considered by the government when it chose to\nSince 2024 children in four primary schools have been able to get apples, bananas and other fruit as part of the pilot scheme.\nDeputy Louise Doublet said: \"To have that taken away at a time when the cost of living is still increasing I think has been quite hard for some families\".\nThe education minister ended the trial because not enough children were eating the fruit and it was leading to a lot of wastage. The Government of Jersey has been approached for a comment.\nfresh fruit would be included in a school food programme that provides hot school meals for government primary schools.\nMinister for Education and Lifelong Learning Catherine Curtis previously said the free fruit scheme was leading to \"a lot of wastage\" and parents \"actually asked\" for fruit to be incorporated into the school food programme instead.\nDoublet said the minister had responded to her questions in the assembly \"centred around the evidence and she informed the assembly that it hadn't resulted in much of an increase in children actually consuming fruit and vegetables and I do accept that\".\nBut she added she did not think benefits in terms of cost of living were measured by the scheme.\n\"Personally I would like to see more investment in healthy food especially if it's locally grown food to help families with the cost of living,\" she said.\nWhen asked about the contract with UK company Apetito Limited to provide hot school meals for government primary schools across Jersey she said it was the \"best available option\".\nShe added she understood people's concerns around the freshness of the food but her \"understanding is that the meals are actually frozen rather than artificially preserved\".\n\"I would like to see these funded meals extended further because it hits the cost of living for parents and... provides healthy meals for children,\" she said.\nFree fruit scheme for pupils axed due to wastage\nConcerns raised over island's food security\nHot school meals to be supplied by UK company", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "29e2941da13f6147de66939d", "title": "Citizens Financial Group (CFG) Lifts Dividend 13% After Strong Q3 And Bigger Buyback - Yahoo Finance", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/C