ham Act, citing national interest CNBC", "truncated": false}, {"id": "25c532bca48ac28ba9e9c404", "title": "Hackers Use Compromised ConnectWise Credential to Sign In to 173 Microsoft 365 Tenants - The Hacker News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTE9LLVo4bDAtYTNoMmpoeFIwdFpheVNIQVJMaXZqOUtaZXZ4TjE4M2E3T0Z4SlA0aVJtNGh3N2dBSXg2SWZiQ0EtcVRKNnhrU1E3RVN5ejJ1V0h4Y2U1SG5nMmtGV2xWckV6NkJWaVJ2VEZDWGVVVTdRLUI1YzgxUUU?oc=5", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:16:00+00:00", "text": "Hackers Use Compromised ConnectWise Credential to Sign In to 173 Microsoft 365 Tenants - The Hacker News\nHackers Use Compromised ConnectWise Credential to Sign In to 173 Microsoft 365 Tenants The Hacker News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "f08ab38721d012a1c548dbcd", "title": "Magnitude 5.6 earthquake strikes Pakistan's Balochistan province - Sharjah24", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTE0zZ0F4YXdNaHFFMFFKeURKZ1dkWXN3blhNaU9zSmw3N1dnWlBidklQMnpLSUhHNkxLOGE2VnozZHBaaUVpN3p3Y2k3RlpSdmxkbUZZN1Y3ZXlhZDQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_cat_weather", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:14:57+00:00", "text": "Magnitude 5.6 earthquake strikes Pakistan's Balochistan province - Sharjah24\nMagnitude 5.6 earthquake strikes Pakistan's Balochistan province Sharjah24", "truncated": false}, {"id": "59872c19d164989d234bc8c5", "title": "Exclusive: Watchdog lists ships carrying Russian gas, blasts Trump sanctions waiver - The Kyiv Independent", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxOWXFvdkVkZTFBWTIyYy05ODhUcmwyTUZYTEJZLWRSaGZsSE9SS2hlVGh1ZVk5bUQ0d3pTcG9zVnNpRmxac3lfejBTSldEN0pMRTA3UlVQbHBKV25Lc0FsbklnM3NseFFiR3JZd1FaLWpFWGRVUVhJNExNclFKUlNnVEx2czM1Q21ieDFtaWVnUG1QNFB3cDJ3OEhNamtXMUhRY01jR2FYMm1na0hJMXZr?oc=5", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:13:18+00:00", "text": "Exclusive: Watchdog lists ships carrying Russian gas, blasts Trump sanctions waiver - The Kyiv Independent\nExclusive: Watchdog lists ships carrying Russian gas, blasts Trump sanctions waiver The Kyiv Independent", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d765b53804e9392260f39046", "title": "How Investors May Respond To P&G Stock Before Quarterly Results - Yahoo Finance", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilAFBVV95cUxPQldOMmJLVklNTm9hX2hVRldVUmZSMDNkTnBmMHJiOXZiaC1MZnBwUVJWUmE0TVNLbVFPeGNLSnp5ZHZjYmVXZkVjZU04bkZwVkJST1RDc3AwbVRzdHg0R0RpSkFJRGN0QUQtc3plN20yV2VicXNjT0N6TDdfX2w5NXh5dVRpS29jX2RRaVJId2EzdXRN?oc=5", "source": "lane_print_vs_priced", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:13:00+00:00", "text": "How Investors May Respond To P&G Stock Before Quarterly Results - Yahoo Finance\nHow Investors May Respond To P&G Stock Before Quarterly Results Yahoo Finance", "truncated": false}, {"id": "10c82a1ab9a7ad060fd0c3e3", "title": "Amit Shah praises ABVP for Odisha student union election victories - The News Mill", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxPYm5oSHhwNDF2OFlPQVJXNk1TckhfNDZVdWRHRHFuU1JoM2RQWVh2aTNsMXlyUldfSkY1S1pVMlEyZ193OER5V1A4a3V6NC1CRklvQXBsSFU2Qm93bkJiNDFGRlJIclY4Z0JyMng5VjNYOUNzWEJmRGVWdVdQUGgxd0YtaW4tUzVWZHZRcXFKdzNkQmZvQnBkTk9SenhGTzRZ?oc=5", "source": "lane_labor_organize", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:12:23+00:00", "text": "Amit Shah praises ABVP for Odisha student union election victories - The News Mill\nAmit Shah praises ABVP for Odisha student union election victories The News Mill", "truncated": false}, {"id": "78f0a0f7bd83305013c1e49c", "title": "5.8 magnitude earthquake hits Pakistan - Greater Kashmir", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxOTWRFRjJUT1hMVmFRT3Q0cjdPOVRXSE51dGNiVFFVcy14TkNtaWx6TEtuZEFmWnJxZU1IX1M4UDNFcGxPMjN4MTVVd3VnZkN0OXRfRV81a0hTU0tSTVp3T3VMVzN6QVpHMU0yQ00xaGsxLWhtUHZGRXU5Wjl3Q2thVENfcVVWZkRhM0pwZ2JfbVfSAZABQVVfeXFMTk1kRUYyVE9YTFZhUU90NHI3TzlUV0hOdXRjYlRRVXMteE5DbWl", "source": "lane_cat_weather", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:11:56+00:00", "text": "5.8 magnitude earthquake hits Pakistan - Greater Kashmir\n5.8 magnitude earthquake hits Pakistan Greater Kashmir", "truncated": false}, {"id": "76c8f83c4111c5af4542eaa6", "title": "Charity reflects on changing needs over 25 years", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c615jnxv7n45o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_business", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:11:54+00:00", "text": "Charity reflects on changing needs over 25 years\nHelp a Guernsey Child says it works through professional referrers who know the children\nA charity that raises funds to provide children with \"essential items\" has said families are facing \"changing pressures\" as celebrates its 25th anniversary.\nHelp a Guernsey Child said since it was created in 2001 it has provided more than Â£1.2m worth of essential items, equipment, services and support to local children and young people.\nThe charity said in its early years it gave financial support to a number of larger community projects benefiting children but there was now an increasing focus on helping individual children and families.\nAlex Jenner, from Help a Guernsey Child, said: \"Over the past 25 years, we have seen significant changes in the types of support families require.\"\nJenner said despite changes in needs the charity's \"purpose has remained the same, to ensure that children in the Bailiwick are not disadvantaged because they lack the essentials that every child deserves\".\nThe charity said it works through professional referrers who know the children and families involved.\nApplications for grants come in from social workers, health visitors, teachers, doctors, nurses and other frontline professionals and are considered individually by the charity's Directors.\nThe charity said the increasing focus on helping in individual cases meant providing something as \"fundamental as a bed, flooring, white goods, clothing, safety equipment or a heating appliance, as well as specialist disability equipment and educational opportunities\".\nIt added the nature of their work reflected the \"changing pressures\" faced by local families.\nThese included the rising cost of living and increased demand for essential household items and practical support, it said.\nJenner said: \"A relatively small grant at exactly the right time can make a profound difference to a child's safety, wellbeing, education or independence.\"\nNew grant scheme supports charities faster\nAutism Guernsey secures Â£100,000 funding boost\nStudents get financial help to 'reach potential'", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "29a94ed5c6b05f91e59167ba", "title": "SAZEW Company Announcements - Sazgar Engineering Works Ltd - Investify", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiYkFVX3lxTE9XU21KR0VSSU9QU2hwaGpUbmowcG9VYm9LWW82bmIxX0FxREdITkRCaTY0MVZDaF9zVlE2Yms3TGx4MnU3bnBTUHdDR1JSLWY4ZldLcDlfWUtoWmkzS3ptMHhB?oc=5", "source": "topic_business", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:08:10+00:00", "text": "SAZEW Company Announcements - Sazgar Engineering Works Ltd - Investify\nSAZEW Company Announcements - Sazgar Engineering Works Ltd Investify", "truncated": false}, {"id": "855c25beb01ee010d07fb1fd", "title": "Sundelin Scores Overtime Winner as No. 10/9 St. Cloud State Women’s Hockey Completes Road Comeback Over (RV) St. Thomas - St. Cloud State University Athletics", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-wFBVV95cUxNaFd3YkV0MnNGa2RBdzdSQkxTR3VtUGFQSWd1T25jMzg0SGNhaFRsRnZkakNCOTh5RE1BUXdjYkI0RHFWT2poVjQ5X3ZmeWZDUG8yV01xV1pFTEV2YkNycGlQdE9iUDNIVFZud0M5MWpIV1BLY1h2ZTVTN2lJd1d3RHdmMHRneERLTVNrbEhQdzBFT2gtNkZMQW12WEFLX0VJWVZfSndwNnVIeW8xU0o1bl9KSm5feFpwdkNGV1Z6U3d", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:04:35+00:00", "text": "Sundelin Scores Overtime Winner as No. 10/9 St. Cloud State Women’s Hockey Completes Road Comeback Over (RV) St. Thomas - St. Cloud State University Athletics\nSundelin Scores Overtime Winner as No. 10/9 St. Cloud State Women’s Hockey Completes Road Comeback Over (RV) St. Thomas St. Cloud State University Athletics", "truncated": false}, {"id": "1aad6eba7b5d44acf4095f26", "title": "weight loss: fda approves highly effective drug treatment for obesity - www.polskieradio.pl", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxNUXB1X195Rjg5eU84UWdKcDB0NXluWUpfd1I2M19tOWdERFY1cmFGSmluQ243Z1dNOTlnOFIwUGxTODRnWXhvMHF5MjA1N1ZyZ2JVbzUzYkZzaHFtTHEwZmgzblAyV0FyMzgtaTR5OTM0NFd5R0xWa3BSYmV6WUtSS3dweEFmc0NhQW9uSG5mLUs5Vl9tUkFtelZCYmZaM0J3WnFRYTNVRWZCMTRsTndiMnVWMW5RUDN0?oc=5", "source": "lane_gate", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:04:25+00:00", "text": "weight loss: fda approves highly effective drug treatment for obesity - www.polskieradio.pl\nweight loss: fda approves highly effective drug treatment for obesity www.polskieradio.pl", "truncated": false}, {"id": "da640b361787b73225f4f42d", "title": "fda approves diabetes drug for weight loss - Philstar Life", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxOMU5SNkpxNDU1S2FNajJMNGNZQ0x3UVRyRlFWdWdoT255X3Z4MTd0R3BtNDJiRzE4cXBDQUY2Z3ZxOHBrVUZVZXVZd0RmWkNjMjdhVWVJa1I2aGh4elpaMC1mWkNYQVpsdXNXalFfWlJqekw1YWdXd2psekUwaGJvRFp6MWRIdmszNWkwejFOdw?oc=5", "source": "lane_gate", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:04:19+00:00", "text": "fda approves diabetes drug for weight loss - Philstar Life\nfda approves diabetes drug for weight loss Philstar Life", "truncated": false}, {"id": "964780588ea34ab388269a65", "title": "Oregon school shooting: Police praise 'heroism' of those who intervened to stop more killing", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-rdf", "source": "rss_dw_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:04:00+00:00", "text": "Oregon school shooting: Police praise 'heroism' of those who intervened to stop more killing\nThe shooting occurred at the Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon\nImage: Joe Kline/AP Photo/picture alliance\nstate of Oregon have identified a teenage gunman\nas a former special needs student there, while praising people who stepped in to stop more killings.\nThree children aged 5, 8 and 11 lost their lives in Thursday's rampage, along with a 25-year-old female teacher, before the shooter was shot dead by a father of two pupils at the school, located in the town of Bend.\nAnother young child and a teacher were also injured in the attack.\nWho intervened to prevent more deaths in Oregon?\nA man in a vehicle outside the school who was shot at and missed by the 16-year-old gunman was the first to alert police to the danger.\nBefore they arrived, however, a female teacher tackled the shooter after he had already killed the victims with a pump-action 12-gauge shotgun in the school's special needs classroom.\nWhile the two wrestled with each other, a man identified by family as Kaylub Giamanco, a 36-year-old father of two girls at the school, rushed in with his legally held weapon and shot the gunman dead.\n\"He heard shooting and saw a teacher involved in a physical altercation with the suspect ... and fired his weapon, striking the suspect multiple times,\" Bend Police Chief Mike Krantz told reporters.\n\"When someone is willing to risk their own life for others, we recognize that. The teacher who is willing to stand and fight for her children ... incredible. That is true heroism, and we don't see that a lot in society,\" he said.\nThe shooting has shocked the Bend community\nImage: ABC affiliate KOHD/Handout/REUTERS\nPraise from Trump as gun control debate revived\nGiamanco's mother told the local branch of Fox News that she was \"very proud\" and that her son was \"an absolute hero.\"\n\"It's a terrible thing, but thank goodness for a man that had a gun and knew how to use it,\" he told reporters.\nThe shooting in Bend has triggered the usual responses from both sides in the everlasting debate about gun control laws in the US.\nThe National Rifle Association (NRA), one of the main and most powerful opponents of tighter laws on the possession of weapons by civilians, hailed the actions of the armed bystander.\n\"Yesterday's terrible act of violence in Oregon serves as another reminder of the importance of a law-abiding armed citizenry,\" the NRA said in a post on X.\nGun control advocates, however, once more condemned the relative ease with which firearms can be procured in the US, which they see as the main factor in the country's high rate of gun-related deaths compared with most other developed countries.\n\"America's gun violence crisis is killing our babies. Enough is enough,\"\nAccording to an analysis by the education information portal Education Week, there have been 26 shootings at US schools so far this year that have resulted in injuries or deaths.\nMore than 360 mass shootings have been recorded across the country this year, according to the Gun Violence Archive.\nIt defines mass shootings as incidents in which at least four people are shot, excluding the shooter.\nIf you rely on our team for trusted reporting, please take a moment to select us as your\n, so you'll always see our verified news first.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "56fcc685ac2dfe168991d965", "title": "Nightclubs are disappearing - and it's affecting young people", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5yngn0pl2ro?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_business", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:01:55+00:00", "text": "Nightclubs are disappearing - and it's affecting young people\nOne under 30 told the BBC they preferred to live somewhere relaxed\nUnder-30s have described missing out on being able to \"let loose and mess around\" because of a \"bleak\" lack of nightlife where they live.\nHenry Gannon said that growing up in Woking he had seen places for young people to gather and socialise \"die away\".\n\"Communal areas just seem to have vanished,\" he added.\nWoking once had multiple late-night venues - now it does not have any traditional dedicated nightclubs left in the town centre.\nGannon blamed the situation on the cost of living crisis, which he said was \"pricing out\" those in their 20s from enjoying themselves.\n\"There isn't really anything to do for younger people who often don't have much expendable income,\" he said.\nAlternative options, the 23-year-old added, were \"Wetherspoons, sitting in the park or getting a prohibitively expensive taxi back from another town or city\".\n\"I feel like I am missing out on a crucial part of being my age, which is being able to let loose, mess around and enjoy life.\nA quarter of UK towns have lost all their nightclubs, the Night Time Industries Association (NTIA) said in 2025.\nIt added that one in six towns have no late-night venues left.\n\"These figures are a stark warning of the systematic erosion of Britain's nightlife infrastructure,\" said NTIA CEO Michael Kill.\n\"We are facing a national cultural crisis.\n\"The damage, as we see it, is increasingly irreversible. Once these venues disappear, they rarely return.\"\nAdam said the nightlife situation in Tonbridge - where the last club closed several years ago - was \"pretty minimal\".\n\"There are some nice pubs and small bars, though most things close around midnight,\" he said.\nBut the 29-year-old, originally from the US, said he was drawn to Kent town as it was \"quieter and more relaxed\".\nStill, Adam said, the lack of nightlife forced younger people to go elsewhere for a night out, which impacted the local economy.\n\"It is definitely a missed opportunity,\" he added.\nWhile he recognised nightclubs were spaces for meeting others, Adam said there was also a trend of younger people going out and drinking less - which was good for their health.\nThe twenty-somethings going out - in the gym\nThe BBC previously heard from under-30s that were opting out of drinking culture and\nThey said that alcohol-free socialising was empowering, avoided hangovers and let them meet like-minded people.\nOthers have also pointed to a cultural shift with more\npeople skipping clubs for sober social events\nFinn Ashcroft, from Chichester in West Sussex, said after Covid \"people were finding it harder to get out and socialise\".\nHowever, he said it was important to emphasise that many under-30s were \"making do\" without clubs and instead creating their own events.\nAshcroft urged people to speak up if they wanted more nightlife where they live\nWhile its traditional nightclubs had closed, Ashcroft said Chichester had plenty of spaces that could be used for music and dancing.\nHe told the BBC he had set up the event companies C-Side Sounds and Strictly Grooves to \"push music locally\" in these spaces.\n\"Students were champing at the bit for somewhere to go,\" he said.\n\"We've definitely helped nurture nightlife within the city.\"\nThe 22-year-old said the \"most important thing\" people looking for more nightlife where they live could do was \"be vocal about it\".\n\"They have the power to [get] local councils and governing bodies to make sure there are spaces for people... to make memories together.\"\n'Nightlife culture isn't dying but it is evolving'\nEnd of hedonism? Why Britain turned its back on clubbing", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "e963d8ddb60a21f92892b8f3", "title": "Loyola-Sacred Heart Girls JV Basketball @ Powell County - MaxPreps", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi8AFBVV95cUxNcXFRU3UzcUV2WExuLS1kV0pCVHhkVEYtT3JmUWdJNDJSaVF5YTM0VEROVnliZGhhbW15dy0ydjc3UFcxZW1UUkd1R1pPLXp3aFJWallFSjNaUFltc0hBeVktN0wtYkdYOGplaF9DS0JsSFY2MldzUGhVYmg1VVVCX1lGTkZSdnZtUzJlZ0F5Rnc1ek1kcDRkbEN1RDdyMjE5SHFxbUd3X3JFUmZMUXFDRWRSeDV5SzJGczlEcEtQWWx", "source": "topic_fed", "published_at": "2026-10-17T06:01:50+00:00", "text": "Loyola-Sacred Heart Girls JV Basketball @ Powell County - MaxPreps\nLoyola-Sacred Heart Girls JV Basketball @ Powell County MaxPreps", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d8f9c34a85136bc12f7f31bb", "title": "China cuts US Treasury holdings to 18-year low in August as debt fears mount - South China Morning Post"