Z3ZMTU5aWjF3VkNqM2kyMU5R0gGuAUFVX3lxTE9WelZFTGtCMzhXTmZZT1Z", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-17T04:45:59+00:00", "text": "Trump's AI Task Force To Commission Report On Technology's Risks - NDTV\nTrump's AI Task Force To Commission Report On Technology's Risks NDTV", "truncated": false}, {"id": "47466cafbf4adfdbf362382e", "title": "Trump puts Russia sanctions package on hold, says pause is in national interest - New York Post", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi1wFBVV95cUxNTmdqelFfdEhueFNsYklTTnp2aFpsZDN0UjRUeW0wOW5sMlZNcEk1c1lEa2Rha0FOaDBzdmMwUXF1LXRjUHR2d1UyU0dQazF0aGVrc0pFZ3I1Sko5QjNnZkdOUW5xNkg0WHlnV09pcDFQV3ZDMDhtNE9HaDJoc19hcExFUFA1LXRtWS1DeDh1a0k5OFM3Y3p2UnNqemNIMGhYc0ZhcXF5dGZXUDZYT1RZNXRzelM5SGR0dFM2a0RRMGt", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-17T04:45:04+00:00", "text": "Trump puts Russia sanctions package on hold, says pause is in national interest - New York Post\nTrump puts Russia sanctions package on hold, says pause is in national interest New York Post", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8eafef662a0761fd664c68f7", "title": "Trump puts on hold new Russia sanctions he signed into law", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/17/trump-puts-on-hold-new-russia-sanctions-he-signed-into-law?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T04:45:03+00:00", "text": "Trump puts on hold new Russia sanctions he signed into law\nShare Trump puts on hold new Russia sanctions he signed into law on social media\nUS President Donald Trump, right, meets Russian President Vladimir Putin for a summit at Joint Base Elmendorf-Richardson, a US military base in Anchorage, Alaska, on August 15, 2025 [Kevin Lamarque/Reuters]\nUnited States President Donald Trump has put on hold a sweeping package of sanctions on Russia that he signed into law last month, telling Congress the pause is in the national interest.\nTrump signed an executive order on Friday, two days before a deadline in the law that would put the sanctions into effect.\nRepublican senator says Trump diesel agreement with Russia may be illegal\n‘Energy ceasefire’: What’s behind Trump’s love-hate ties to Russian oil?\nTrump insists energy ceasefire holds as Ukraine reports new Russian strikes\nThe law – named after Lindsey Graham, the Republican senator who died unexpectedly in July after returning from Ukraine – passed in the House of Representatives and the Senate by large margins. The bipartisan legislation was drafted by Graham and Democratic Senator Richard Blumenthal.\nfor its war on Ukraine by sanctioning Russian officials, banks and a shadow fleet of tankers carrying its energy exports.\nIt also directed Trump to impose tariffs of up to 100 percent on the five biggest importers of Russian oil or gas with an exception for countries that import less than 15 percent of Russia’s natural gas exports and are taking steps to cut them.\nKirill Dmitriev, special envoy for Russian President Vladimir Putin, said on social media that Trump’s move was “an important and truly historic moment”.\n“The US-Russia economic dialogue and peacemaking efforts will continue,” he added.\nThe decision to suspend the sanctions came a week after Trump said the US signed a deal to buy diesel from Russia to try to lower global fuel prices.\n, saying it would help Russia’s war effort without affecting fuel prices.\nDemocratic Representative Don Beyer said he and other politicians had “warned” that Trump might do this, referring to Trump’s deal with Moscow.\nBeyer called on Congress to “fix this flawed law to stop Trump from capitulating to Putin and ensure that it truly supports Ukraine”.\nTrump recently has also increasingly criticised Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy for failing to reach a deal with Russia.\nIn an interview with Al Jazeera, Oleksandr Merezhko, the chairman of the Ukrainian parliament’s Committee on Foreign Policy and Interparliamentary Cooperation, linked Trump’s latest moves, which put Ukraine at a disadvantage, to next month’s midterm elections in the US and predicted an improvement in relations after the voting.\n“President Trump is a difficult partner, but we are dependent on the United States, and we need to have constructive, respectful relations even with Trump, no matter how difficult it might be,” he said.\n“I believe that after the midterm elections, the situation will be better, the emotions will subside and we will be able to return to constructive dialogue with President Trump,” Merezhko added.\nPolls have suggested that Trump’s Republican Party will have a hard time keeping its majorities in Congress in the November 3 elections due to voters disapproving of Trump’s handling of the US-Israel war on Iran and blaming him for higher prices.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "20f031cc175d630dbec8f509", "title": "Nurses say technology is making their jobs and patient care worse - ABC17NEWS", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxNTThxVkJkd09kT3duRk1OejhxODFFeGJOd3RJdWEtV1Y0X01pWmJpaTdhU21LeEY3LXpjZXdRWktXdDNrUExhRWNFZ3dOWDNaZ2FlUmJaSjJGNkV3TkhmLUpHXzZYRG9MZ0h2bk1YcVp3aVZCN2NQdUhHUDZsVXVSNXFBZ0ZPUWNkWFZQOW1JdnJzVUp5eVRuZnY0aTIzaWdrY0ZJWm1lazNFWEJtSFpXX1F3?oc=5", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-17T04:44:44+00:00", "text": "Nurses say technology is making their jobs and patient care worse - ABC17NEWS\nNurses say technology is making their jobs and patient care worse ABC17NEWS", "truncated": false}, {"id": "a4f8bd8be62dd5659781ea9d", "title": "ASU launches mentorship program to grow more organic farmers - AZ Family", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxQSVJhcDF3N3hrS1FJYnY3ZGdUU1FWOGZEX1lBam1oVDBxUzBDa1h5aEY1M2JNd1JzcDlCYXhyQ3JCMkdadEVIN2xmRll0ZWVzWWtkWmN4bE1XWDRLaE9rUVFnYWdxeDEzRjdwUEMtYnZxMnR1ZTY5SXRGd1RGV0dBZTJrN3QzTkdtOEFXcHVDTmVoZjZhbXF0VHZ30gGuAUFVX3lxTE14cWUxTVpQM3puOTVuTzdUdXVDM1ExellpaVJ", "source": "topic_products", "published_at": "2026-10-17T