lWjRORW8xakFQZktINGxOcG8zOGhhR253cy1CeU9HeU0zdVZLOGFZRWNoQ0xLY2RCVm1lOVI1Q1lnLWlJeWdkTGRJMmpqSF94cHExWFpDZVl5QWw0TTBOalB", "source": "lane_distress_restruct", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:30:38+00:00", "text": "US federal bankruptcy court operations disrupted by cybersecurity incident | Business Information & News | FE - Westlaw Today\nUS federal bankruptcy court operations disrupted by cybersecurity incident | Business Information & News | FE Westlaw Today", "truncated": false}, {"id": "dfdd7bf4e912dc61929a7617", "title": "Southern California wildfire engulfs homes, prompts evacuation orders", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/17/southern-california-wildfire-engulfs-homes-prompts-evacuation-orders?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:30:36+00:00", "text": "Southern California wildfire engulfs homes, prompts evacuation orders\nShare Southern California wildfire engulfs homes, prompts evacuation orders on social media\nA firefighter battles the Norte Fire in San Juan Capistrano, California, on October 16, 2026 [AFP]\nA fast-spreading wildfire in Orange County, in Southern California, has engulfed several coastal properties and prompted widespread evacuation orders.\nThe Orange County Fire Authority said on Friday that the Norte Fire had scorched about 188 hectares (465 acres), with the state’s Cal Fire agency putting it at about 231 hectares (570 acres) by the evening, and that at least six homes had been damaged or destroyed in the San Juan Capistrano area.\nOregon school shooter was former special needs student, police say\nAI deepfake ads grow more popular in US midterm campaigns, blurring truth\nFIFA set for rule change after Balogun red card row at the World Cup: reports\nThe fire authority said firefighters were “aggressively attacking the fire from the ground and air” and issued pleas for people to stay clear of the area.\nUnseasonably high temperatures and low humidity are fuelling the rapid growth of the fire, the AFP news agency reported.\nThe Norte Fire started in the coastal city of San Clemente on Friday and moved to the city of San Juan Capistrano, with some 6,000 homes and 16,000 residents under evacuation orders by the evening. An evacuation shelter has opened in each city while helicopters attempt to douse the flames.\nThe Norte Fire is one of several in the region driven by Santa Ana winds, intense warm gusts that blow from the southwest US interior towards the California coast.\nThe Santa Ana winds typically arrive in the autumn, right when Southern California’s vegetation is at its driest after a long, rainless summer, according to The Weather Channel.\nForecasters said winds blew at between 55km/h and 90km/h (35mph and 55mph) within coastal areas.\nThe strongest winds were expected through Friday, but the high heat and low humidity conditions that contribute to the growth of the fire are expected to last through Saturday night.\nTens of thousands of people in Los Angeles County were left without power as authorities attempted to lessen the possibility of electrical sparks that the heavy wind gusts could carry.\nCalifornia firefighters were also busy battling the Bryson Fire, which broke out on the outskirts of the Malibu beach community in Los Angeles County on Thursday. As of Friday, the fire had burned about 59 hectares (147 acres) and was 17 percent contained, according to Cal Fire.\nThe Henderson Fire was 20 percent contained and had burned 842 hectares (2,080 acres) in San Diego County by Friday, Cal Fire said. The blaze impacted Marine Corps Base Camp Pendleton and prompted freeway closures.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "c7b9387268c9a97184a7c313", "title": "Jio’s $3.2 billion IPO tests investor appetite as Ambani legacy faces scrutiny - Yahoo Finance", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxOOVJIVUNyYkZrcVBWREJSaDBqVHBLV1JveW9fakYxZmdQelRyaUZkM2FLS1F5cHV2TmNTUXplVVp6cmxrWVlIVVlpVFBidld4MDlfNEk3d2x