210S1BpR21OVWxleDNVdU9jdkxSMlZyZ2FlQ0FSbUpkbW1jRlpDa2dsdFdvSXhnREdKcDhBUnlVUncxcUxoWnpES3lGa1BKVUFPVktaVTdoeGViVzVIQ3oxa1h3TFpnQ0N1YlNCODZaQzhMYjBfcjdKVUlieXczRUZGNnAtZWhjSEFLTldQcFBjNEo2NjhIZW9LV1p3?oc=5", "source": "topic_government", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:11:14+00:00", "text": "Trump signs executive order waiving new Russia sanctions, tariffs - Arab News\nTrump signs executive order waiving new Russia sanctions, tariffs Arab News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "5afaca8d9f920155031fe5f7", "title": "Three men jailed for 158 years each for murdering Australian and US surfers in Mexico - BBC", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTE1Td2ZsbFdISWxWS2JJcWMxUjhBUVdqb1RzWXRIeUxubjhnMUhQTVpCcnMtd1YwU3ZoZjJ3UkYxTlhVUDEyMVg3Vmo2T2ZNNHVJOHZxMGpXUHNHRlE?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:11:10+00:00", "text": "Three men jailed for 158 years each for murdering Australian and US surfers in Mexico - BBC\nThree men jailed for 158 years each for murdering Australian and US surfers in Mexico BBC Three men sentenced to more than 158 years for the killings of Australian, US surfers in Mexico CNN Mexican judge sentences three men to 158 years in prison for murders of Australian and US surfers​ The Guardian Three sentenced to 158 years in Mexico for murder of Australian, US surfers Reuters 3 Men Are Found Guilty in Murders of Tourists on Surfing Trip to Mexico The New York Times", "truncated": false}, {"id": "244ffc3b821d4ad760d149a5", "title": "Three men jailed for 158 years each for murdering Australian and US surfers in Mexico", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3kgqjkzw29wo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:11:10+00:00", "text": "Three men jailed for 158 years each for murdering Australian and US surfers in Mexico\nHow a harrowing trial of two murdered Australian surfers ended in a guilty verdict\nA Mexican judge has sentenced three men convicted of murdering Australian brothers Jake and Callum Robinson and their US friend Carter Rhoad to 158 years and nine months in jail each.\nThe Robinsons and Rhoad were killed in an apparent botched robbery of their truck on a secluded beach in Baja California in 2024 while they were on a surfing trip, the court heard during the trial.\nThe murders sent shockwaves around the world, particularly in Australia, as the area is usually safe from the violence seen in other parts of Mexico.\nThe guilty verdict was handed down last week. Debra Robinson, the brothers' mother, told the courtroom that her sons' murders had taken \"the future we had imagined with them\".\nThe convicted killers' full names were not given for legal reasons, meaning they were only identified as JesÃºs Gerardo, Irineo Francisco and Ãngel JesÃºs.\nIn November last year, the girlfriend of the alleged ringleader, JesÃºs Gerardo (alias \"El Kekas\"), was\nto 20 years in prison. She had admitted to involvement in the robbery.\nThe court heard that the bodies of the victims were found dumped down a well with gunshot wounds to their heads.\nAt the time, the murders shocked locals and tourists in the beach town of Ensenada who were disturbed at the apparent ease and sheer pointlessness of the killings.\nEnsenada has a reputation as a welcoming spot for surfers, but the chilling murders revealed how commonplace such extreme violence remains in Mexico.\nThe only explanation the authorities were able to give was that the surfers - all in their early 30s - had ultimately been murdered for being in the wrong place at the wrong time.\nTheir killings happened barely 36 hours after they crossed into Mexico from the US. Their bodies, however, were not found for another week, when their families were able to identify them.\nLocal surfers also called for greater security for residents and visiting tourists, citing other recent examples of violence in the state. Tourism is a key part of the regional economy in Baja California.\nTrial over killing of Australian surfer brothers and US friend starts in Mexico\n'Shattered' - Tributes to surfers killed in Mexico", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "d67b5810570e4539db59cff0", "title": "Trump puts new Russia sanctions that he recently signed into law on hold, citing national interest - Castanet", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi1wFBVV95cUxNNkVXLWF1QjYzWGRvb0poUjRaTDZrTFFDaW04dHdpM2w4cG91dXFzNHBEc3NfS2U0cngyZlFiLW16bTZwcUVlVnZwWWt1TWdGengzLUdKODRhZGxYVm54eHBjUUdKbXV0M1BPRkZiaHBXVmpYY0pETWQxMXNyYm94Y1dUMHJEUmJibWhSdGpCWDk3X05vQUdXNFdfb3BhM0VCbjAySG55cFVFdG1QUU5mNUdmeGVYOVZFUzE4QmtYTGR", "source": "lane_tax_fiscal", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:09:00+00:00", "text": "Trump puts new Russia sanctions that he recently signed into law on hold, citing national interest - Castanet\nTrump puts new Russia sanctions that he recently signed into law on hold, citing national interest Castanet", "truncated": false}, {"id": "66ac420d60eccd803264c859", "title": "Trump waives Russia sanctions ordered by law named for Lindsey Graham - Washington Examiner", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxQNk9MTDI3WWVZX3RvazdyRW9INGJabkd1NTNKbGVyZTRLQTdhTVQ1Q1l1WnlVajd1cjEtU1BldWpXUGluT2hFOTl0VmtrSldjQnlYRkhSQWhHeWdIRUVTc0pKSjl2bndIRlhVT21mU1M5NHlYcDFCWURpQW9DdnVMdzZmVFpQUGNEQm9lQXlnV1B5UjFJcUEyNWJVOW1PZHgzWGpEQjVfcFh1d3pNWk9RdXBmUEtYSnVwOFV3N0JhUlI", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-17T03:09:00+00:00", "text": "Trump waives Russia sanctions ordered by law named for Lindsey Graham - Washington Examiner\nTrump waives Russia sanctions ordered by law named for Lindsey Graham Washington Examiner", "truncated": false}, {"id": "5e2a542212715ca351b6c4e6", "title": "Trump Signs Order Exempting Russia From Sanctions Law - The New York Times", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxNbjBtZHJzaWs1Q0M1VEQ3LVg3VTRvdkdwTFNKY2xwbG82X0ZYZGR1X3ZYZk1uOGRqWFdhcl90YUNTVlQ5dWNjV0Y1bmpYcWo4TENqdnhTMy1VQVV6