7T02:34:00+00:00", "text": "India’s ‘Cockroach’ Protest Leader Faces Court in Voter-List Row - Bloomberg.com\nIndia’s ‘Cockroach’ Protest Leader Faces Court in Voter-List Row Bloomberg.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "9463019bead5292d59a26af6", "title": "Trump puts new Russia sanctions that he recently signed into law on hold, citing national interest - Goshen News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikgJBVV95cUxNSElFZjhQbU9BS05TQkVYcFFsTXNHY2VwQVAxbWs2S3FQeVJEc3BwNXN3bkZObHNWQ0N2cGowNWNtbkxXRmRZMnJreFI5TUlma2E3QURwcHluc0pjUDZIbTRCeXlQVTZHdlJ4N0ppMTlYN1cyWlUydWEzTkkwaGhtakswcFI2QWJkY3lNUWhZVl81QkNyUkF5Q25aMFZlc0txeTBiYWlSN29IOXVtVnZqYzFnak1PQjhjUlZYdkNTQTh", "source": "topic_legislation", "published_at": "2026-10-17T02:33:56+00:00", "text": "Trump puts new Russia sanctions that he recently signed into law on hold, citing national interest - Goshen News\nTrump puts new Russia sanctions that he recently signed into law on hold, citing national interest Goshen News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "abcf49ea3266fb5856af8339", "title": "Two of MLB's smallest spenders will meet in the World Series for first time since 1991 - ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxNMFA3X0M0OXVqQ3kxVHVjNTkyQmpmMzJPdTQ0WVNyb0w2VlpUdmpxVGNxZ2hadHVaUTFnN2lLc1Ixenk1UlA0a05NVGZaV0dMbXBGbDlNakUtSDJtTlRDWm9veDExV1NERnE1WElaSEtqc1A0b01hcTl2WkVKWjBFSHNoNW1rWUJWRVNuWFFSV3c0cGNtT0wtSXVZWXRqd9IBowFBVV95cUxNRDNndEFVcDQtNUJnX0pVbVRuQUtVNkw", "source": "lane_factor_impulse", "published_at": "2026-10-17T02:33:21+00:00", "text": "Two of MLB's smallest spenders will meet in the World Series for first time since 1991 - ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos\nTwo of MLB's smallest spenders will meet in the World Series for first time since 1991 ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos", "truncated": false}, {"id": "a1365c50f71f1cd7c301b03d", "title": "Brazil sees record fall in Amazon deforestation as key election looms", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqe8rzg6zl00o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T02:33:09+00:00", "text": "Brazil sees record fall in Amazon deforestation as key election looms\nBrazil's government says deforestation rates in the country's Amazon and savanna regions have fallen to record lows ahead of a presidential election run-off in which the rainforest's future is a key issue.\nLeft-wing President Luiz InÃ¡cio Lula da Silva, when he assumed office three years ago, pledged to end deforestation by 2030 in the Amazon. It had surged under his right-wing predecessor, Jair Bolsonaro.\nLula will face Bolsonaro's son Flavio in the run-off on 25 October, with polls suggesting a neck-and-neck race. Flavio is expected to continue his father's policies if he wins, though he has pledged to fight organised crime in the Amazon.\nSatellite data shows that in the year to July 2026, the deforestation rate fell by 41.8% in the Amazon - the biggest drop since records began in 1988. The fall in the Cerrado, Brazil's savanna region, was 23.8%.\nThe Amazon rainforest - the world's largest - is a crucial buffer in the global fight against climate change and 60% of it is located in Brazil.\nWhy the Amazon rainforest is so important\nJair Bolsonaro promoted mining in indigenous lands in the Amazon and forest clearances soared at the same time as resources to protect the forest were cut.\nDuring Bolsonaro's presidency from 2019 to 2022, the Amazon lost nearly 60% more in forest lands compared to the previous four years, news agency AFP reported, citing official data.\nLula reversed his policies and oversaw deforestation rates\nduring his first year in office. Lula tightened up environmental monitoring and penalties for illegal logging.\n\"Our goal is to achieve zero illegal deforestation by 2030,\" he said in a post on X on Friday.\nTropical rainforests like the Amazon are home to millions of species. In a healthy state, they absorb vast quantities of planet-warming carbon dioxide, helping to keep the Earth cool.\nBut they have come under increasing pressure from decades of deliberate land clearance for agriculture and logging, as well as climate change, which scientists warn can create conditions for wildfires.\nBrazil's Environment Minister Joao Paulo Capobianco described the decline in Amazon deforestation as \"absolutely stratospheric\".\nIt was an \"historic achievement\" for Brazil, said Marcio Astrini, executive secretary at climate advocacy group Observatorio do Clima.\nIt showed that \"with political will, it is possible to curb deforestation and greenhouse gas emissions\", Astrini said.\nTropical forests destroyed at fastest recorded rate last year\nWhat was agreed on climate change at COP30 in Brazil?\nBrazil's Amazon sees sharp decline in size of area burned in 2025\nBrazil's Amazon rainforest at risk as key protection under threat", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "18f95355ec331e06bd84ebca", "title": "Trump Puts New Russia Sanctions That He Recently Signed Into Law on Hold - NTD News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQUHVwTnVqM1FaYWh6RF9BcDI2TE5teExZTTBZODV3cmFhdWNhU0hMZkp2QWZpdXFJSjZ0T2kxZjRZVnk3eC11Qlpuak9sdThNQVB1Z2dSTWhWWUJRaE9Vd3FHMXBzZkN6XzF5NnNVNDM4U0xrcTBadTctM2JGU3FMZ0F4ZmNfb0VCRE1kMDByVUExQU41Y0UxMWlUcVFWeF9ZdEhzLVBTeEk?oc=5", "source": "topic_legislation", "published_at": "2026-10-17T02:33:09+00:00", "text": "Trump Puts New Russia Sanctions That He Recently Signed Into Law on Hold - NTD News\nTrump Puts New Russia Sanctions That He Recently Signed Into Law on Hold NTD News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "1aedd18c8dd87b261a2cd3ba", "title": "Trump puts new Russia tariffs and sanctions on hold - Yahoo", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxPSmExaHRSNW1aOWJoVm4zckJLc1VlQlZMLWk5cnJTQUxVVjVOU0g4QmEtd0JNUjFFNzY2ZkpWUzZ6YUgzYlhRc2xkaU9XeGJMckg1RkU1V283b0l6cDdJNE1Wb19ZR1F3SUoydi0wUFVxcGdfSGFYN