ource": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-17T01:55:45+00:00", "text": "Actress Selma Blair says she 'did not intend to harm anyone' in plane altercation\nUS actress Selma Blair has spoken out after being accused of assaulting multiple people on a flight to New York.\nA publicist for the Legally Blonde star said she \"did not intend to harm anyone\" and that there was \"much more to this story\". Blair \"experienced a medical emergency on the flight\" and is still fighting âmultiple sclerosis (MS), a statement read.\nBlair's publicist said that the 54-year-old had a neurological disorder that \"bears directly on how a medical episode presents to people who do not know her\".\nto charges that she assaulted an officer and a nurse after being removed from the flight. She was also accused of assaulting two flight attendants on board.\nwhat happened to her aboard a Delta Airlines flight\nto New York had been \"built almost entirely on a police statement and\nThey also denied media reports that she had attempted to open the door of the aircraft.\nThe publicist noted Blair's fight against multiple sclerosis (MS),\npublicly in 2018. She announced in 2021 that she was in remission for the disease, but the statement noted that the Hellboy and Cruel Intentions star \"still has bad days\".\nIt added that she also has pseudobulbar affect (PBA) - a disorder that develops in the context of a brain injury or underlying neurological dysfunction, according to the US National Institutes of Health.\nThe disorder affects emotional expression that can result in sudden involuntary and out-of-control episodes of laughing, crying or anger that do not match how a person actually feels.\nWatch: Selma Blair is seen leaving court after plane incident\nBlair's publicist described the actress's physical achievements since her MS diagnosis as \"nothing short of a miracle\" and said she still lives with pain daily.\n\"Selma had never been arrested before Sunday night,\" she said. \"There is much more to this story than has been reported and we ask to consider the entirety of the facts before rushing to judgement, whether in the courtroom or in the court of public opinion.\"\nThe incident happened on a flight travelling from Los Angeles to New York on Sunday evening. New York airport officials responded to a call about \"a physically abusive passenger\" on a Delta Airlines flight. Two flight attendants were hurt and one was taken to hospital, the New York Port Authority said.\nA pilot asked for medical help, describing \"a bloody nose\" and \"some bite marks\", according to audio recorded on air traffic control obtained by CBS News, the BBC's US partner.\nBlair was arrested and taken to hospital. She was issued a federal summons by the FBI for a charge of assault within the special maritime and territorial jurisdiction of the US that relates to the on-board altercation.\nThe two additional charges of assault were filed in state court after she was taken off the plane. She has pleaded not guilty to those charges and was released on bail.\nActress Selma Blair faces charges for kicking nurse and officer after plane incident\nUS actress Selma Blair accused of assault after incident with flight attendants\nSelma Blair: 'Multiple sclerosis took my career down'", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "106ced4c2ce42274f9757715", "title": "Trump waives Russia energy tariffs and sanctions under Graham law - Business Standard", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiygFBVV95cUxPdGk5RmtMSlJ4cUE3Z3Qta2VRcktxRDA0YTIzQUs3TzJCVERZMG8zQ3JxaHlDSTBlbnRuRE1vU25WV3BHUTdSQ2hvMXhxZmRnb3FDVE02T3YtRldYWjl4eVVISWhSNnU3bGtKbk16NkZ0czVrLXk0V2FyRnNMcU1oWjlDblQyYUVJbFlCMFU0dnFITEV0ZFFIbDYxbjh6aFhRaWZkblBhUFdkeE1Bay1jMHlDcmNwS2RCNmpZYXp3Tnk", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-17T01:55:43+00:00", "text": "Trump waives Russia energy tariffs and sanctions under Graham law - Business Standard\nTrump waives Russia energy tariffs and sanctions und