-prediction-lineups?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T22:53:26+00:00", "text": "Leeds vs Manchester United: Premier League – teams, prediction, lineups\nShare Old rivalry has new twist as Man United head to Leeds – all to know on social media\nBryan Mbeumo is set to continue in attack for Manchester United at Leeds [Cathal Mcnaughton/Reuters]\nto follow our live coverage of Leeds against Manchester United.\nSunday, October 18, at 2pm local time (13:00 GMT)\nAl Jazeera Sport will have all the build-up from 9:00 GMT ahead of our live text commentary stream\nReal Madrid demand resignation of La Liga chief after Goebbels comparison\nPro-Nazi chants before Ajax match slammed by Croatia leaders\nAsian Cup in Saudi Arabia still on, organisers say, but golf tour postponed\nFIFA set for rule change after Balogun red card row at the World Cup: reports\nManchester United against Leeds United has long been one of the fiercest rivalries in football.\nThe former’s closest shot to ending their wait since 1967 for an English top flight title came in 1993 when Sir Alex Ferguson’s side were pipped to the title by the latter.\nThe following year United’s wait was over as Ferguson’s side – buoyed by the arrival of Eric Cantona from Leeds – lifted the inaugural Premier League crown.\nThe rest for United and Ferguson was history, but since the most successful manager in English football retired the Old Trafford club have been in decline.\nThe fortunes of Leeds, who have won three league titles, dipped dramatically after that last piece of domestic silverware. Ten years later, they were relegated and three years were even spent in League One, the third tier of English football.\nNow the Elland Road club are back in the top flight, having won the Championship two seasons ago, and have an eye on the top four this weekend.\nAl Jazeera Sport takes a look at the match that for Leeds marks the arrival of their fiercest rivals, who have lurched to a 40-year low.\nLeeds have lost only one of their six league games this season, a 2-1 reverse at Arsenal in their last match when the Premier League holders were second best for much of the match and were forced to come from behind.\nTwo wins and two draws in their first five league matches saw Leeds holding onto the coat-tails of Arsenal and City.\nThat run culminated with a stunning 4-1 home win against Newcastle United.\nA disappointing home draw with Crystal Palace sat in between the\nA 6-3 defeat at Chelsea ended their League Cup hopes, but the home side needed two goals in the last ten minutes to pull clear in the thrilling encounter.\nHow have Manchester United fared this season?\nUnited’s season – and Michael Carrick’s start as permanent manager – couldn’t have got off to a worse start with\nWhen the Red Devils fell a goal behind against another promoted side, Ipswich Town, at Old Trafford in their next match, the warning signs were there.\n– and that remains United’s only league win of the season.\nby Manchester City – in which a controversial VAR decision separated the sides – has been one of United’s better performances with deflating draws against\nby Brighton, who overcame the home side’s early 2-0 first-half lead to the disbelief of Old Trafford.\nWhat is the latest on Lisandro Martinez’s Manchester United criticism?\nDefender Lisandro ‌‌Martinez will be available for Sunday’s game after ⁠⁠United accepted ⁠⁠his apology for criticising its transfer policy,\nMartinez met Carrick and senior club officials on Thursday, two days after suggesting United ⁠⁠needed greater investment to compete at the highest level following their 2-0 Champions League defeat by Atletico Madrid.\nThe centre back later apologised for his remarks and Carrick ⁠⁠sought to downplay the episode when he spoke to reporters on Friday.\n“We’ve moved on from that. It was one of those things. It’s really not a drama for the group,” Carrick said.\n“The squad have trained really well and they are in good spirits. There is ‌‌a freshness about the group…\nWhat happened the last time Leeds played Manchester United?\nLeeds were 2-1 winners at Old Trafford when the sides met in the Premier League in April.\nNoah Okafor scored both goals for Leeds to inflict the only defeat of Carrick’s interim tenure, having replaced Ruben Amorim as manager.\nMartinez was sent off early in the second half, but Casemiro offered United some hope just after the hour mark.\nWhat happened in the corresponding Leeds-Man Utd game last season?\nThe teams shared a 1-1 draw in the Premier League match at Elland Road last season. Leeds’ Brenden Aaronson opened the scoring in the 62nd minute with Matheus Cunha levelling three minutes later.\nWhen did Manchester United last beat Leeds?\nUnited were 2-0 winners when the sides met at Elland Road in Leeds’ relegation season in 2022-23.\nMarcus Rashford and Alejandro Garnacho netted the goals.\nWhen did Leeds last beat Manchester United at home?\nLeeds haven’t beaten United at home since Harry Kewell scored the only goal of the game in a Premier League match in 2002.\nThere have been seven matches between the sides at Leeds since then, with United winning five of those.\nThe Opta supercomputer has given Leeds a 42 percent chance of victory, while offering United a 32 percent chance of winning.\nHead-to-head – Leeds vs Manchester United\nThis will be the 116th meeting between the sides, with United winning 50 and Leeds claiming the spoils on 27 occasions. Another 38 matches were draws.\nJoe Rodon and Mateo Joseph will both miss the game due to injury, while former United winger Daniel James is a doubt with a back problem.\nTrafford, Justin, Elvedi, Muharemovic; Bogle, Ampadu, Tanaka, Gudmundsson; Stach, Okafor, Calvert-Lewin\nPatrick Dorgu, Manuel Ugarte and Benjamin Sesko all remain sidelined by injury, while Luke Shaw and Kobbie Mainoo face late fitness tests. Matthijs de Ligt is nearing a return to action following his long-term back injury.\nPredicted Manchester United starting lineup\nLammens; Dalot, Martinez, Maguire, Shaw; Baleba, Mainoo; Mbeumo, Fernandes, Diallo; Cunha", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "f64df85c41d749938f6fd6c1", "title": "El Paso launches prehospital whole blood program to treat trauma patients en route - KFOX", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPclQ4S3ZsS2ZLSUNKLV8xMy1rUXl3N3lTdkU5LVR4dFQ1NzNoNUtkWlhablhNaUU0WEo4aGdzV0hZQk9sTWNHVHJsaFhldDZINGlDUXFYdUVQSlR1TVpBNE9LeGM1X0NYVFNIeGdSTi1NdVRJYTFLSk9BTU9pUEdhdXRvTl92djQzQWJ0WGhZS0F0dVlmT2xsME0xTjJ3cmF5Tmdfb243N3ZlT1ZkV0lWZmFR?oc=5", "source": "topic_products", "published_at": "2026-10-16T22:52:58+00:00", "text": "El Paso launches prehospital whole blood program to treat trauma patients en route - KFOX\nEl Paso launches prehospital whole blood program to treat trauma patients en route KFOX", "truncated": false}, {"id": "7f041cf2e100570bb0a6055f", "title": "Nicor Gas rate hike - CIProud.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifEFVX3lxTFA1ZkRuWnU2VHFOZ0o1STBmemJlLTAzRzZLb0dodDJ3V05yWVZORG91eHVDOF9GSDRaWC1EX0RsWnNYV3czVFRzajc1X245TVd4RzNvTGx5NzA2eGlHOTNTT2t4bWFWSlBSU0FJWkpQa1V2ek5kTFVpRUthUkw?oc=5", "source": "lane_factor_impulse", "published_at": "2026-10-16T22:52:36+00:00", "text": "Nicor Gas rate hike - CIProud.com\nNicor Gas rate hike CIProud.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "11dcf2448ecb3e47b4e67064", "title": "No shares were issued as Suzano (SUZ) VP settled 56,290 performance awards in cash. - Stock Titan", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxNSzVWdm9vV2hRR3YzYVUtS09seUFRaTNSWEJnRG9SV1VmWGJabHp6TmtHQ3FTbXU0U2ROQWwwcllhRXJwdUNxd0tlcmwzTWl6TktvelJVOE1hVGhCNW1lTjV3S0tvMWQ3c29pd3htZmR6a2s1MjlQWUwtc191c1FnVEVWS0MzNjZDMS0tSGtOSEdSQTdMQzVJdHItV1lsMl9pNWtkNmZ3?oc=5", "source": "sec_4:google_fallback", "published_at": "2026-10-16T22:52:36+00:00", "text": "No shares were issued as Suzano (SUZ) VP settled 56,290 performance awards in cash. - Stock Titan\nNo 