gnore new eligibility rule - Ottumwa Courier\nNCAA sues Ohio governor over his executive order allowing schools to ignore new eligibility rule Ottumwa Courier", "truncated": false}, {"id": "dd667635370546ce97be8e61", "title": "Ag commissioner candidates tackle tariffs, farm crisis, data centers during debate - North Dakota Monitor", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxNQVJ1YUcya2xiaG1mLVR0d1RraWNMUjM0VGdYUTJRRV9JODRtS1ZMYjFZLTRDUURpR2QxbXo4QXdPRjdxUjk3SldYelE2YlpyVzNFT28ySlpxWk5iUnBlN3JMOVVSNi03RWF2aVRCLUMxNkJpR2Q1ZWQxR29OanNvMUNGUGZDOEVqc1haV1FtelZqbUZnMHlTTFE4M3FBYTJaWjc0TGFORmV2eWVNaXRMb3NwdXRSUHk4NFMyRTNWN3I", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-16T21:09:31+00:00", "text": "Ag commissioner candidates tackle tariffs, farm crisis, data centers during debate - North Dakota Monitor\nAg commissioner candidates tackle tariffs, farm crisis, data centers during debate North Dakota Monitor", "truncated": false}, {"id": "953ead3546c442a0c9f916a1", "title": "Meta employees say Lula’s accounts restricted in Brazil election: Report", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/10/16/meta-employees-say-lulas-accounts-restricted-in-brazil-election-report?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T21:08:50+00:00", "text": "Meta employees say Lula’s accounts restricted in Brazil election: Report\nShare Meta employees say Lula’s accounts restricted in Brazil election: Report on social media\nBrazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will face challenger Senator Flavio Bolsonaro in a presidential election runoff on October 25 [File: Evaristo Sa/AFP]\nEmployees at Meta have acknowledged in internal communications that the Instagram accounts of Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva were negatively affected by restrictions during the country’s election, media reports say.\nThe messages, reported on Friday by Brazilian daily Folha de S Paulo, also acknowledged the platform recommended the profile of Lula challenger Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, as well as his WhatsApp channel. Folha, the Sao Paulo-based paper, cited messages it had reviewed.\nUS records 4,410 measles cases as outbreak grows\nHow Iran messaging highlights cost of war ahead of US midterm elections\nWhite House press secretary Katie Zacharia fired after five days on the job\nAOC transfers $1m to Michigan candidate El-Sayed in progressive push\nMeta told the Reuters news agency that the technical issues cited in the report were already public and the conversations it referenced related solely to the severity of the issues, not political interference.\n“Any suggestion that Meta favors one side is false,” it added in a statement.\nLula, the left-wing incumbent, will face right-wing challenger Bolsonaro in a\non October 25, following a stronger-than-expected performance by the senator in the first-round vote earlier this month.\nFriday’s report came on the heels of a Brazilian court ruling on Thursday that ordered Meta to immediately adopt measures to provide equal treatment of the two candidates ahead of the runoff.\nThe ruling by a judge in Brazil’s top electoral court was made shortly after Lula filed a complaint that accused the tech giant – which owns Instagram, Facebook and WhatsApp – of using biased algorithms and AI restrictions to favour opposition candidate Bolsonaro ahead of the election.\nJustice Marco Aurelio Bellizze ruled that Meta cannot reduce the distribution of political content, restrict searches or remove posts in a way that creates an imbalance between Lula and Bolsonaro. His ruling also orders the company to ensure its artificial intelligence tool applies identical criteria to both candidacies.\nBellizze said in his ruling that Meta must pay a fine of 500,000 reais ($98,700) per day if it fails to comply.\nAccording to Lula’s party, some of his posts appeared without a share button and had reduced reach. Options for reactions, sharing, audio or accelerated speed were also missing.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "0d3d759ebed2aefb816e94ff", "title": "Livworx Launches Meet EveryBODY to Unite Communities Around Health - markets.businessinsider.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxQejN6eldodF9xRlh2UzI5NFlmaVU0NnhuT0JPXzF0dmt2RVhTVm1jR3l0WWpoWi03QUZDMlZaRGFCWlpNMHF5dlZWLUZUMDJyZmVDaW1tSVNubU12U1dtSmZUOFlOcXVRVjNFRTBDaktubUxRNjlPeEk0Z0hQM0NqWTE1Q3JXdmdBWGRhdFpyVG5iSzZPYTByOGFSSHpONWFod3hkbnVTakxLN3VwWk9WQ2VmVS1nbF96MWxrZDJDUEw", "source": "topic_products", "published_at": "2026-10-16T21:08:48+00:00", "text": "Livworx Launches Meet EveryBODY to Unite Communities Around Health - markets.businessinsider.com\nLivworx Launches Meet EveryBODY to Unite Communities Around Health markets.businessinsider.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "2b13623641a8946be5155ca6", "title": "How Israeli spyware used ‘zero click’ hack on Al Jazeera staff", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/10/16/how-israeli-spyware-used-zero-click-hack-on-al-jazeera-staff?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T21:08:44+00:00", "text": "How Israeli spyware used ‘zero click’ hack on Al Jazeera staff\nHow Israeli spyware used ‘zero click’ hack on Al Jazeera staff | Al Jazeera | Al Jazeera\nHow Israeli spyware used ‘zero click’ hack on Al Jazeera staff\nAn explosive investigation reveals how Israeli spyware firms hacked into Al Jazeera devices in 2024 using a new ‘adfection’ method previously unknown to the public.\nThe ‘zero click’ hacks can infiltrate your phone or computer simply by scrolling past an ad online.\nShare How Israeli spyware used ‘zero click’ hack on Al Jazeera staff on social media", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "dbdb0a09d7e2953b3fc1b40f", "title": "Solventum Corp. stock falls Friday, underperforms market - MarketWatch", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizAFBVV95cUxQdnQzMDE5UWUzbFpGUjBVaWVpWXRGSWNaVEhsTUE4ZjNQRHl4LWFNZ2VIb1M2Q