R200Rl9iWTdJWEFuNEJVeW5rRzVnSQ?oc=5", "source": "topic_fed", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:59:00+00:00", "text": "Page: An unlikely city facing an uncertain future - Detroit Free Press\nPage: An unlikely city facing an uncertain future Detroit Free Press", "truncated": false}, {"id": "44411b5d007526ad83e69898", "title": "Big Tech stocks head for biggest weekly drop since ‘liberation day’", "url": "https://www.ft.com/content/4c4f03f4-f878-4bd6-8128-5be7e3bb8ca1?syn-25a6b1a6=1", "source": "rss_ft_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:58:24+00:00", "text": "Big Tech stocks head for biggest weekly drop since ‘liberation day’\nAI trade jitters send investors scrambling for government debt in a move that halts a months-long Treasury sell-off", "truncated": false}, {"id": "376ddddc2f6ac6ff68fe6f33", "title": "White House press secretary Katie Zacharia fired after five days on the job", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/white-house-press-secretary-katie-zacharia-fired-after-five-days-on-the-job?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:58:06+00:00", "text": "White House press secretary Katie Zacharia fired after five days on the job\nShare White House press secretary Katie Zacharia fired after five days on the job on social media\nNewly-appointed White House Press Secretary Katie Zacharia is \"transitioning out\" after five days on the job [File: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters]\nWhite House press secretary Katie Zacharia is “transitioning out” of her role just one week after United States President Donald Trump tapped her for the job, Al Jazeera has confirmed.\nFox News on Friday reported that Trump said there was no rush to hire Zacharia’s replacement.\nKatie Zacharia selected to be next White House press secretary\nUS ambassador to Greece Kimberley Guilfoyle resigns amid misconduct claims\nNew White House press secretary Katie Zacharia holds first briefing\nWhite House spokesperson Katie Zacharia’s law career faces scrutiny\nEarlier Friday, Trump told reporters he told Zacharia to “reconsider” staying in the job.\n“I don’t think Katie should be made to suffer like she’s suffering at the hands of the press,” Trump said as he departed the White House. “I said to her, ‘Honestly, if I were you, I’d reconsider. You think about it.’”\nZacharia said she had received a call about the role last week. She succeeded Karoline Leavitt.\nTrump later announced her appointment and described her as “an attorney”. However, over the last week, the question of whether Zacharia, a graduate of California’s Pepperdine University law school, had actually passed the bar exam to work as an attorney came under fire.\nIn an interview, she told Fox News on Thursday that she did not pass the bar exam.\nShe lasted five days on the job, half the length of Anthony Scaramucci’s tenure as director of communications, who served for 10 days during Trump’s first administration.\nAl Jazeera correspondent Kimberly Halkett explained that the appointment and subsequent reversal could create further problems for Trump as Republicans prepare for a pivotal midterm election.\n“The fact that there was that major credibility issue as well as a shaky performance is what sealed her fate,” said Halkett. “This makes the president look impulsive at a time when he’s already being criticised for not having a campaign that is really on track to win in November.”", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "d0921f257d15251200914b20", "title": "Police assess Palestine Action post by national security adviser's wife - BBC", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTE9BTUxjckpFTG1WTWVDbFo5N01pSl9yUkRpbF8zZWU5MEhrbFZMNTVmQWRtakdXd0RscHVleGhIQXozZWxqSFZ5ek9faG0yR3VtMDZKVVdDYzFFd3M?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:58:05+00:00", "text": "Police assess Palestine Action post by national security adviser's wife - BBC\nPolice assess Palestine Action post by national security adviser's wife 