ctor acquired 3,000 shares through options at $6.63 a share at Capital Bancorp (CBNK). - Stock Titan\nA director acquired 3,000 shares through options at $6.63 a share at Capital Bancorp (CBNK). Stock Titan", "truncated": false}, {"id": "7b103580a31fb2e3f01ed319", "title": "‘Well-known individual’ tries to secure permanent injunction against Guardian and ITN - The Guardian", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxPeW9JX2RfMXBIM0x3bkItMTVzUlplalcxQmhUYzZnZFE2S1lQSDJSWWV6Ql96RjJIcVBESDdZRlV3ZDYyNHhnd2Ffei1YYkFvSkNMWlQzU0cwVVBjZDBQM3hZZnBSVVhweGl3elNNaUwtMWl4SXl1UElRekFJajNEOHRSbmFQSUx0TkNCTGhlX2tuSmZ2SUo2c19rNlY4MzQ1VGw5UWZzaFZxZ250NUV4RlF6TlFUMFlJQWo4LW1CRFF", "source": "lane_blast_legal", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:22:00+00:00", "text": "‘Well-known individual’ tries to secure permanent injunction against Guardian and ITN - The Guardian\n‘Well-known individual’ tries to secure permanent injunction against Guardian and ITN The Guardian", "truncated": false}, {"id": "c82017ce7fbd09cd3ddf5941", "title": "How Iran messaging highlights cost of war ahead of US midterm elections", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/how-iran-messaging-highlights-cost-of-war-ahead-of-us-midterm-elections?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:21:43+00:00", "text": "How Iran messaging highlights cost of war ahead of US midterm elections\nShare How Iran messaging highlights cost of war ahead of US midterm elections on social media\nGas prices are seen at a gas station in Deerfield, Ill., Wednesday, Oct. 14, 2026. [Nam Huh/AP]\nIn messages that appear to be directed at the American public, Iran has been highlighting the cost of the war that the United States and Israel launched against the country ahead of the United States midterm elections.\nIranian officials have published articles in state-affiliated outlets stressing the disastrous impact of the war on oil prices and the US economy, while Iran’s chief negotiator and Parliament Speaker\nhas actively targeted US officials about rising costs and military spending.\nDozens of aircraft, hundreds of buildings: US loss to Iran attacks revealed\nIran war has cost the US $38bn: How will it impact US economy, politics?\nWhat’s behind reports that the Israeli army is low on troops, equipment?\nSina Toossi, a senior non-resident fellow at the Center for International Policy, said Tehran is looking to increase the political cost of the war for Trump by trying to talk directly to the American public.\n“It’s not necessarily that they’re trying to get Democrats in power or manipulate US politics in a certain direction, other than just overall increasing the costs on this issue of the Iran war, and just playing that game of information warfare and getting out their own narrative and propaganda as well,” Toossi told Al Jazeera.\nTrump’s Republican Party is looking to retain control of the Senate and House of Representatives in next month’s midterm vote. But the Democratic Party, which largely opposes the war with Iran, is mounting a strong challenge across the congressional electoral map, including in areas that have been conservative strongholds for decades,\nOn Wednesday, Ghalibaf shared a news story on\nto 3.7 percent last month along with a collage of negative headlines on the US economy.\nThe social media post also featured a comic strip from the Road Runner cartoon showing Wile E Coyote building a catapult that misfires and launches a boulder at him.\n“Let’s ‘play the percentages’. Not in odds, but in the % increases,” Ghalibaf wrote in a message to US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent, who has been leading the sanctions campaign against Iran.\nBessent said last month that he represents “the house”, likening the economy to a casino while addressing the national debt and bond market.\nIranian Parliament Speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf arrives at Zurich Airport in Switzerland, June 20, 2026 [Handout/Iranian Parliament Speaker Office/West Asia News Agency via Reuters]\nGhalibaf’s remark referred to the increase in inflation, underscoring that the cost of living keeps rising due to the war despite Bessent’s assertions.\nDays earlier, he shared an image of a ghost shaped like a bell curve, with diesel prices rising and housing affordability and consumer confidence falling.\nSince the start of the war on February 28, Iran has disrupted shipping in the Strait of Hormuz, sending energy prices soaring. In the US, the price of diesel is at an all-time record of $6.33 per gallon (3.8 litres), according to the American Automobile Association, and gas is $4.33, up from less than $3 before the war.\non vessels around the strait in recent days after Trump and his aides repeatedly stressed that the waterway is under US control.\nThe uptick in energy prices has fuelled overall inflation in the economy, leading the US Federal Reserve to\nlast month at a time when Trump has been calling for them to be cut to stimulate economic activity.\nIn a letter to the American public on September 29, Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) accused Trump of lying about the cost of the war and the state of the US economy, dismissing the president’s claims that oil prices would soon nosedive.\n“Countries around the world have lost their faith in the US economy. Demand for American bonds has plummeted. In fact, countries are starting to offload their US bonds. Soon, the dam will break, and the economy will implode, causing, unfortunately, great pain for Americans for many many years,” the IRGC said.\n“Americans need to wake up. They need to wrest control back from corrupt politicians. Now is the time, as the American political system is at its weakest.”\nThe US midterm elections are seen as a turning point in the conflict – not because of their potential outcome, but because of what Trump might do after the vote.\nTrump has suggested that he would either strike a deal with Iran or return to a full-scale war after the November 3 legislative elections. He has also dismissed the idea that the vote will have any impact on his Iran policy.\n“They’re waiting to see how I do in the midterm election. What they don’t realise is that I’m not running,” Trump said at the\n“I gave absolutely no credence and will not give credence to the election. When it comes to Iran, it doesn’t even enter my mind. The only thing that does is that Iran will never have a nuclear weapon.”\nIf the Democrats gain control of Congress, they can push for measures to curb Trump’s ability to continue the war, including through withholding funding for the military campaign.\nBut Toossi said there is a debate within Iran on the potential impact of a Democratic victory in November.\nWhile some point to foreign policy hawks among the Democrats to argue that little would change, others say a midterm defeat would make him politically vulnerable and\n“I don’t think they’re hedging their bets either way, and I don’t think it necessarily affects their overall strategy of increasing the costs [of war] regardless of whatever happens in November,” Toossi told Al Jazeera.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "f16dbeebb0bd3f18a3f48812", "title": "2026 fda approved weight loss drug retatrutide approval status - www.polskieradio.pl", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxPN0FUOEdKQjRuUFhIU3BQekdRZjdfcHM2YlBJRkhiekhaUnBBeTgtVHZvSFV6UWlNZkxtSGhBaFh2djJWV2dhOGJpWk9YMGExekwtY2V5SFZERklod0p5VGZRWk4tTnFkQVVzN3pDUnNZOVVKdjluMHNrak1NclZjRnpIdTF3ZU5mT0N6RU8zTVVWeUltSmFnZGp0WTFfWTN5cThmaXZHZnFnRmxCNnc?oc=5", "source": "topic_fda", "published_at": "2026-10-16T18:21:14+00:00", "text": "2026 fda approved weight loss drug retatrutide approval status - www.polskieradio.pl\n2026 fda approved weight loss drug retatrutide approval status www.polskieradio.pl", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d32e2b4eccb15d3e79129028", "title": "Great Alaska ShakeOut teaches Anchorage students earthquake safety - dailydispatch.com",