+00:00", "text": "Beyond Immerse adds three flavors alongside its energy spin-off - Stack3d\nBeyond Immerse adds three flavors alongside its energy spin-off Stack3d", "truncated": false}, {"id": "4f5b4595e396a1457042e291", "title": "Beyond Immerse adds three flavors alongside its energy spin-off - Stack3d", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTE9PbElUVWpkMzdJOVNHd2JGd0pndV9xQloyZHV4c0dvZ085VlZFRmdqLVNSNmhRWENyUFI3OTFfTEhxMlpRMWxaRQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_spinoff", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:41:00+00:00", "text": "Beyond Immerse adds three flavors alongside its energy spin-off - Stack3d\nBeyond Immerse adds three flavors alongside its energy spin-off Stack3d", "truncated": false}, {"id": "9b7d5647d59a7afdd2698ce6", "title": "US records 4,410 measles cases as outbreak grows", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/us-records-4410-measles-cases-as-outbreak-grows?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:40:18+00:00", "text": "US records 4,410 measles cases as outbreak grows\nShare US records 4,410 measles cases as outbreak grows on social media\nThe United States Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) reports that children and teenagers make up the majority of new measles cases [File: Megan Varner/Reuters]\nThe United States Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) has recorded 4,410 measles cases so far in 2026, an increase of 330 in a week, and has dispatched an investigator to the state of Pennsylvania to help contain the country’s largest outbreak.\nCDC figures also show 451 measles-related hospitalisations nationwide this year. Children and teenagers aged five to 19 account for 42 percent of cases, followed by adults aged 20 and older, who make up 41 percent. Seventeen percent of cases were among children under the age of five.\nCDC reports two measles deaths in US as cases hit 35-year high\nPennsylvania confirms fifth measles-associated death as US outbreak grows\nNew York state declares measles disaster amid resurgence of disease in US\nPennsylvania reported 1,222 cases across 42 counties as of Wednesday, including 86 new infections since October 9, according to the state health department. The outbreak has led to 225 hospitalisations and\nmeasles-associated deaths. State officials are actively investigating a sixth reported death.\nThe CDC is sending a so-called “disease detective” from its Epidemic Intelligence Service to work with state health officials on the Pennsylvania outbreak. The deployment follows Pennsylvania’s request for federal assistance, known as an\nPennsylvania has expanded vaccination efforts in affected communities. State health centre staff have administered more than 5,900 measles, mumps and rubella (MMR) vaccine doses at 202 pop-up clinics since the outbreak began in late April.\na statewide disaster emergency on October 5 as measles cases rose in nearby Pennsylvania. The order is effective until November 4 and expands the number of healthcare professionals authorised to administer vaccines and allows nurses greater flexibility to order measles testing.\nMeasles vaccination coverage among US kindergarteners fell from 95.2 percent in the 2019–2020 school year to 92.4 percent in 2025–2026, according to data from the CDC. The agency estimates that about 280,000 kindergarteners are at risk because of gaps in vaccination coverage.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "320ca73ba6546be9d8c0c3b6", "title": "Former New Orleans Personal Injury Attorney Sentenced in Connection with Staged Accident Probe - Department of Justice (.gov)", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxPeDlYTDZBX3BrZldVbC0zT0ZrRlVWUXVIaEgwQnJiUW1vc2tLVlRDMzdXOWF3dFB5UDBGUWdfTXpUZDFsaFdsTk9kU3N4X1JIcTYybkNhLW9hTjIyMHZJVURIZFUxcnZrT19xeWhXZlhpc3YtNGlockFYdWVRNXlXbS1jSHgzV1JLZzkxZDZyUjF5ekotWTZOUXFMd3ZwbmxrVzBXMmtKUWVYd2VIbUVWZFlFYnhEZzZGQ25qTlhNaFA", "source": "official_doj_search", "published_