art With Just 3 Companies - Yahoo Finance\nThe Next Stock Market Crash Could Start With Just 3 Companies Yahoo Finance", "truncated": false}, {"id": "0ab421ec54faea7bd92a7ac9", "title": "S&P 500 dragged down by AI stocks as chip shares head for worst week since July: Live updates - CNBC", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE93d3pqaDdoN1RiVVZKZnIyYl9SZ05PdXNGc3JIMjFqbmF4Um96Z1prZVJVcHBrV3g1YmR6X1ZJNEhINUUtRm5ESXVtTTFMdGUwbUs4N3BjUjNZQzhDX3pjRmhmMlY1YzVjbkFtM2RkWUZZQzhtYURJ?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_business", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:06:00+00:00", "text": "S&P 500 dragged down by AI stocks as chip shares head for worst week since July: Live updates - CNBC\nS&P 500 dragged down by AI stocks as chip shares head for worst week since July: Live updates CNBC Stock Market Today: Tech Stocks Slump as Nasdaq Faces Weekly Loss WSJ Nasdaq falls over 1% as AI trade extends decline, set for worst week since June Investing.com S&P 500 subdued as gains in banks offset AI jitters; Dow at one-month high Reuters Chipmaker sell-off sends investors to other stocks and bonds for safety CNN", "truncated": false}, {"id": "275d9c7ea882378544515709", "title": "Real Madrid demand resignation of La Liga chief after Goebbels comparison", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/16/real-madrid-demand-resignation-of-laliga-chief-after-goebbels-comparison?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:05:31+00:00", "text": "Real Madrid demand resignation of La Liga chief after Goebbels comparison\nShare Real Madrid demand resignation of La Liga chief after Goebbels comparison on social media\nLa Liga President Javier Tebas has been in position since 2013 [Isabel Infantes/Reuters]\nReal Madrid are demanding the ‌‌resignation of La Liga President Javier Tebas after he compared rhetoric from ⁠⁠the club’s management ⁠⁠to the propaganda methods used by the Nazi Party in Germany.\nTebas wrote earlier on Friday on social media that “Real Madrid’s management directs an orchestra of ⁠⁠mouthpieces and Real Madrid TV leads the singing”.\nManchester Utd have ‘moved on’ from Martinez outburst, says Carrick\nInfantino apologises to FIFA council but critics remain unhappy\nWhat led Manchester United’s Martinez to meltdown in Madrid – all to know\nFrench football body urges fans and students to keep politics out of stadiums\nThe LaLiga president was responding to articles by two journalists saying he and LaLiga were acting against Real’s interests.\nTebas added that the authors ⁠⁠in El Debate newspaper were amplifying a message on behalf of Real’s management.\nReal Madrid’s demand for Tebas to immediately resign deepens a feud between the club and La Liga’s chief.\nLast month, Real called for a new LaLiga president in response ‌‌to Tebas calling their complaints about refereeing decisions ‘a smokescreen’ for their shortcomings on the pitch.\nTebas on Friday criticised Real Madrid TV’s coverage of officiating at their matches.\n“Their score is always the same: select the plays that suit them, repeat the grievance, feed the suspicion and point fingers at the enemies,” he wrote.\n“That method recalls propaganda mechanisms used by Goebbels, Nazi Germany’s Minister of Propaganda.\n“The comparison is with those propaganda techniques, not with ⁠⁠an ideology or, of course, with the Madridista fanbase,” added ⁠⁠LaLiga’s president.\nReal Madrid demand Tebas’s resignation as La Liga chief\nReal Madrid released a statement later on Friday demanding that Tebas resign from his positions as LaLiga chief and vice-president of the Royal Spanish Football Federation.\nThe statement called it “intolerable and extraordinarily serious” that ⁠⁠Tebas used “a comparison with the propaganda methods of the Nazi regime to discredit our club, its management and its television.\n“Tebas’ repeated conduct ⁠⁠demonstrates a lack of neutrality, respect and impartiality incompatible with ⁠⁠his institutional responsibilities,” said Real.\n“It is unacceptable that he even takes advantage of questions, information or opinions from journalists unrelated to the club to direct his accusations at us, attributing to us actions of third parties for which ‌‌we bear no responsibility.”\nThe 64-year-old, who is elected by the 42 professional clubs in Spain’s top two tiers, has been La Liga president since 2013. In 2023, he was ‌‌re-elected ‌‌unopposed until 2027.\nReal Madrid’s statement came hours after La Liga confirmed that they are one of the six clubs that will sit on the league’s Executive Committee this season.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "28e0cc9cac95bf7c9f9f17e4", "title": "Kinder Morgan to Report Q3 Earnings: What's in Store for the Stock? - Yahoo Finance", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxNM1FCWjQ0Mk5tZUJJaE56VTJ0Z3ZrUmN4U09LWndtWk5XOWEwd2dZeXdaeWxYTHpXRUs2UkFGVjE1bkhGSW9XNVBIWlJCcGJYdWIzMGEzMjgtRnJsTnYxTUxSaVJhODI0aVN2cFVLdmtqdzdHU1d2dHFWQUtERllwR1NBazd1WmNlcmtTZDlZendMWjFvOXBlYllYQlRFQQ?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_markets", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:05:00+00:00", "text": "Kinder Morgan to Report Q3 Earnings: What's in Store for the Stock? - Yahoo Finance\nKinder Morgan to Report Q3 Earnings: What's in Store for the Stock? Yahoo Finance", "truncated": false}, {"id": "42b4065e014dfa4e3c5c03bb", "title": "Want Anthropic exposure before its IPO? Here’s how - Yahoo Finance", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTFB3eVIwcVdCaUJLQ0JlLURLNElkanJrcGxKMi12M2dnTnNXSVlHUmpUbDRoMEpuQVMwanFZZThISV9mTHFTXzJwTW05bkJGaHNxN1Z6VmdiUDJybGk3bnUyamgxUGxydHk2SUFsZ25TaUZtcTJfc0U1MG1xWkJBbTA?oc=5", "source": "lane_listing_flow", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:04:26+00:00", "text": "Want Anthropic exposure before its IPO? Here’s how - Yahoo Finance\nWant Anthropic exposure before its IPO? Here’s how Yahoo Finance", "truncated": false}, {"id": "05ab2ad33b35e6ca2bd39b65", "title": "Felton Power Plant Shutdown Deepens Cuba's Energy Crisis - Cuba