e Motley Fool", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxQRXgtQllsVkVMdHpZTWc4SFJJV21WZXJBcFFMY19TZlZHWmlNQ1psWXBIV05xQlVJOEdwbC01RElWVDhORjhjVFQ3R1FNQnpZclV0ZmRQV0x6RVl4a0o0dE9reUY2XzE4N0ZaRHZudmE4Um5SZWNuS3FORjlidlpBWmlEdTc1WW5vV0N6MTFncE0yYjVBYlQ2REpR?oc=5", "source": "lane_tax_fiscal", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:04:13+00:00", "text": "RMDs Don't Have to Bring a Higher Tax Bill. Here's the Legal Loophole. - The Motley Fool\nRMDs Don't Have to Bring a Higher Tax Bill. Here's the Legal Loophole. The Motley Fool", "truncated": false}, {"id": "1894b8d1462b7b85ee09083b", "title": "Pope Calls on Putin for a Ceasefire to Deliver Aid to Temporarily Occupied Oleshky - UNITED24 Media", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxQSWxEdm1zUF96MWJZUDZJQnUyNWRuYkhndHh5UkFRZDZYQkFMMldnRXloZm9QRGh1OVl1c1FGb2pZYzZzTGs1eUJjcU54Qy1oTERXZlZXUG8yWGx1WmVuLXZTZlNCV1hfQnlnWWRva0lJeVFYSTYyMUdUUy1nUDdvejJYV2gzRTYzUWNna2c4ajRjbXp1ZWgxeHJwTTBXYUY2Q3dPVXpReUZiNFM3Z29uMTloX2JwZm5Pc3B0RA?oc=5", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:04:09+00:00", "text": "Pope Calls on Putin for a Ceasefire to Deliver Aid to Temporarily Occupied Oleshky - UNITED24 Media\nPope Calls on Putin for a Ceasefire to Deliver Aid to Temporarily Occupied Oleshky UNITED24 Media", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8ab5580417042f40b792864f", "title": "Visitors flock to see tiger that mauled ex-child actor to death as enclosure finally reopens - New York Post", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizwFBVV95cUxNTlVUdVpXZTR5VWQzTUpUR0RETVNpZ3ctMEhENGJDTnloNzlDb25xTDhNRzljanI2dG5CU2dLVkRYWUhBSzFabnRXOE5TN0ZSaEJSd3hqQ0tKY1Vybm5HUk1ndWMxc3d4U2RJcEtPMTh5Xy1yR2hsYWEwQTBTclE4SWw1ZkZfMS1wWkJQMXJIWFdMUmM5S0otX3hKUFB6anpPUUV4VzM5eHhWRnpVNEhSMFZwd2Vab0hWU3VWaDZTaVd", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:04:00+00:00", "text": "Visitors flock to see tiger that mauled ex-child actor to death as enclosure finally reopens - New York Post\nVisitors flock to see tiger that mauled ex-child actor to death as enclosure finally reopens New York Post NHS staff may have breached tiger attack victim's medical records BBC Trump Shares Bizarre AI Tiger Video In Late-Night Spree After Posting Fatal Attack Footage Forbes What we know about wildlife park tiger attack Yahoo ‘Take the phone away’: Luke Russert and Symone Sanders Townsend slam Trump’s ‘weird’ late-night posts MS NOW", "truncated": false}, {"id": "02f608463a27880de9ae89b4", "title": "Pope Leo to make public appearance Sunday, first since cancer surgery", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/pope-leo-to-make-public-appearance-sunday-first-since-cancer-surgery?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:03:52+00:00", "text": "Pope Leo to make public appearance Sunday, first since cancer surgery\nShare Pope Leo to make public appearance Sunday, first since cancer surgery on social media\nPope Leo XIV celebrates mass at the Agostino Gemelli Polyclinic in Rome, Italy, in the first photos released after he underwent cancer surgery [Vatican Media via AP Photo]\nPope Leo XIV is making steady progress at the hospital after undergoing lung surgery earlier this week, according to his doctors, as the Vatican says he plans to appear before the public on Sunday.\nThe 71-year-old Catholic leader, who has been\nunderwent an operation to remove part of his right lung on Tuesday.\nPope says death penalty ‘inadmissible’ as US plans to livestream execution\nUS archbishop says Catholics in army should not participate in firing squad\nVatican confirms Pope Leo’s surgery was successful\nHe is now able to “carry out normal daily activities with full independence”, his doctors said in a medical update on Friday.\nA blood test and chest X-ray earlier in the day confirmed his “steady improvement”, added the medical bulletin.\nThe update came as the Vatican shared the first images of Leo since his surgery, showing him celebrating mass and standing unaided in the Rome hospital where he is recovering.\nThe Vatican said Leo will deliver a traditional noontime prayer on Sunday, marking his first public appearance since the operation.\nPreparations are also going ahead for his planned trip to South America in November, The Holy See added.\nfor a pope known to be energetic and who was elected only in May 2025 caused shock and raised questions about the future shape of his papacy.\nThe Vatican did ⁠not say on Friday when the pontiff might be discharged from hospital, but previously indicated his recovery would take about a week.\nPope Leo XIV leads mass at the Gemelli University Hospital in Rome, Italy, where he is recovering after undergoing lung cancer surgery [Handout/Vatican Media/AFP]\nThe pope’s doctors have said his surgery was completed successfully, without complications. They have not yet disclosed the size of the tumour or whether the disease had spread to nearby lymph nodes, key factors in determining prognosis.\nChicago Cardinal Blase Cupich, seen as a close ally of ‌Leo, said he had been shocked by news of the cancer diagnosis.\nHe told Catholic magazine America he thought Leo had “downplayed” his health issue on Sunday, when the pope announced he needed surgery for a small, well-contained growth on his lung.\n“When I heard they took ‌out ‌part of the lobe of the lung and that it was malignant, that was more shocking and more concerning,” said Cupich. “I think people are very concerned and even worried about this but hoping for the best.”\ndue to ⁠visit Uruguay, Argentina and Peru\nfrom November 6 to 17. Peruvian President Keiko Fujimori had speculated that the trip might have to be delayed, ‌but in a sign that preparations were carrying on as normal, the Vatican released a list of journalists admitted to ‌cover ‌the visit.\nWork on the trip is “going forward”, said a Vatican spokesman.\nLeo also continued to work from the hospital on Friday, including speaking by phone with Russian President Vladimir Putin. During the call, the pope pushed for a ceasefire to allow aid and food into the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky, the Vatican said.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "f725db2b62f1031145a35f79", "title": "Nvidia’s Huang and Broadcom’s Tan Debate the AI Boom - Bloomberg.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizwFBVV95cUxQNlRLUzZMcHBMOTZKdVZJcmFKUnlYNkFLdlYydV9WbFBvVHFLSXphLXVFck5aMUxzX3NaSzBHNkVodTVpeHBvTTM2ck9jTkJ0RkVoUzlURzJ3dEY1SjRuMHFMVE1zbDB5MUptVC1FRVkwNElMREFaaGk1MTFYUEMtMFZPSll4clZVNzQtVHZoWm5STUNfaGZ4YlVudUE3Y1NvWTAyRDZTZzlnbTV5RlBDQ3U4Tk9UTzVMT1AzcVUxa3J", "source": "publisher_bloomberg", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:03:51+00:00", "text": "Nvidia’s Huang and Broadcom’s Tan Debate the AI Boom - Bloomberg.com\nNvidia’s Huang and Broadcom’s Tan Debate the AI Boom Bloomberg.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "c658f8cdee05ccb8c0a179cb", "title": "Is Crane NXT (CXT) Undervalued On Its Board Appointment And Recent Rally? - Simply Wall Street", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxNOGYtRzdRVEthaTgzRzVNc2tRQWFEdkpWcTJORDJYRnFJU0VqcDRrelRsUmdDWHRkcnB3eDRLVFFkOENSUzZrQTEwcGFscnprcl9BbFRtbUMweUp6bi0zam00V3dwVzZqZjU4ZTlTOHNyTld6cmhXdnhaaEI1WjJqODNSeHNhMWl5T1pPT3NKeW52Zy1VdlJnaFdtcUNRNEtEaDlfbVJ5MHhrN2t0cWdTbzFlLXV1ejl5Nm8xZG9n0gH", "source": "lane_key_person", "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:03:24+00:00", "text": "Is Crane NXT (CXT) Undervalued On Its Board Appointment And Recent Rally? - Simply Wall Street\nIs Crane NXT (CXT) Undervalued On Its Board Appointment And Recent Rally? Simply Wall Street", "truncated": false}, {"id": "6795ea6f5c6884cea1897fab", "title": "U.S. embargo, sanctions on Cuba impacting power supplies, access to medicine - CBS News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiekFVX3lxTE9taHhZdkUxTjBJSFhvd1ZtcENOUlVoVzI0STVhZzdMaDdBWW5IeFhxQUVHMFd5dlRBVVdfY1lBSG1Na3M3TW81YkhGSXlZRnNaSEFsVTNUbk1fcGd6TE9WU1hoMDg4NVJJbnBtLXNESC14ZmdiNXUtRDNn?oc=5", "source": "topic