VYwUzNVdUt0TDluRHY4OGpDcWl5Y25la3pRazVaSXRIM1o1cjhyY1dDM09zT2diYnI4S2lycXlIS2hnN1cyYXppc1JfYXQ1YVNIc0U1b2kxaEtKWnc?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_markets", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:35:43+00:00", "text": "Stock Market Midday, Oct. 16: Tech Stocks Slide as Investors Rotate Into Defensive Sectors - Yahoo Finance\nStock Market Midday, Oct. 16: Tech Stocks Slide as Investors Rotate Into Defensive Sectors Yahoo Finance", "truncated": false}, {"id": "b9f781437e4bc1b28c07a0b6", "title": "Former Detroit USPS employee sentenced for unemployment benefits fraud - CBS News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxNS0VMWnIzS3M3SHMtZWJNUjFrMENyTjdSeEluODdiS3dsMHFzTlV2a0pjaVhXc1hSa0dMTnIwOUN3SE5vbjBXQnhJZXNhaGlYM1FZeEZoNGpqTUhRd25ocnJzQllwV3FjZkNHOUp1TEdBTlhlWnpVY3QwaGJsN0FINE8xSUxjMlh6eGdMLXM2TXU5NV90azNhMS0xdw?oc=5", "source": "topic_fed", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:35:34+00:00", "text": "Former Detroit USPS employee sentenced for unemployment benefits fraud - CBS News\nFormer Detroit USPS employee sentenced for unemployment benefits fraud CBS News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "237622c0f5cc031fa096258f", "title": "Spain to appeal to CAS after FIFA penalty for Islamophobic chants", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/16/spain-to-appeal-to-cas-after-fifa-penalty-for-islamophobic-chants?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:35:32+00:00", "text": "Spain to appeal to CAS after FIFA penalty for Islamophobic chants\nShare Spain to appeal to CAS after FIFA penalty for Islamophobic chants on social media\nEgypt players at the end of their match with Spain in March [Albert Gea/Reuters]\nSpain’s football federation is taking its case to ⁠the Court of Arbitration for Sport after FIFA rejected an appeal against sanctions imposed for Islamophobic chants by supporters during a match against Egypt in March.\nFIFA fined the ⁠federation (RFEF) $20,000 and ordered it to close at least 15% of the available seats for Spain’s next home friendly.\nManchester Utd have ‘moved on’ from Martinez outburst, says Carrick\nPro-Nazi chants before Ajax match slammed by Croatia leaders\nAsian Cup in Saudi Arabia still on, organisers say, but golf tour postponed\nDR Congo protests Formula 1’s ‘indefensible’ decision to race in Rwanda\nfollow incidents at the RCDE Stadium near Barcelona, home of LaLiga club Espanyol, where ⁠\n, “If you don’t jump, you’re a Muslim” during the goalless World Cup warm-up match.\nAfter the second occurrence of the chant, the stadium announcer issued a warning and the scoreboard displayed a message against discriminatory behaviour.\nSpain winger Lamine Yamal, who is Muslim,\nat ‌the time, describing them as disrespectful and intolerable and calling those responsible “ignorant and racist”.\nthe following day while world governing body FIFA later started disciplinary proceedings against the RFEF.\nThe RFEF argued that the word ‘Muslim’ was “neither insulting nor pejorative”, adding the fans’ conduct should be assessed under FIFA’s Article 17, which covers political, ideological, religious or offensive messages, rather than Article 15, which deals with discrimination and racist abuse.\nFIFA’s disciplinary committee rejected that argument, saying Article 15 ⁠does not require the explicit use of a slur and that a ⁠term can be discriminatory when used in context as “an insult, taunt, or marker of inferiority”.\nThe RFEF appealed the sanction, but a FIFA spokesperson told Reuters that it was dismissed last week, prompting the Spanish federation to take the ⁠case to CAS, the highest authority in sports disputes.\n“Throughout the proceedings, the RFEF has maintained that it acted immediately, diligently and effectively from the moment ⁠it became aware of the incidents,” a high-ranking official in the ⁠RFEF told Reuters.\n“Furthermore, the measures taken ensured that the chants were not repeated and that the spectators present in the stadium themselves expressed their disapproval of such behaviour.”\nThe official said the federation considered the sanctions particularly severe, arguing that comparable capacity restrictions ‌had not been imposed automatically in more serious cases or those involving previous disciplinary offences.\nThe chants were detected by the RFEF’s monitoring systems and immediately reported to the match ‌officials, ‌the official said, adding that security was reinforced in the affected section of the stadium.\n“The federation cooperated fully with the relevant authorities to identify those responsible.”", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "949f410956cd1434346fff24", "title": "Billionaires Ready Legal Attack If California Wealth Tax Passes - Bloomberg.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxOMmp5NEVGTE81MDNaNWVmT2tiLUtBQjE5VnRCQm9Yc1A5Wkp6b29EMjJVSHM4bkVheHlaWk5PaDJGTloxRTdIeC1mZ0VwanUxc0w4QzFaNElGbnFTX2Z0ZFdOWU9OZy1Dd0dpVlNHXzN1Vkpkcnh0RlVicjVkaEJrYnhNUXdrTjNCRU0zeGFyb1ZJejZKMVpMRFVGNXk0eUk1Z2k0VGUyeFprMEctYzFaYkRod1Q?oc=5", "source": "publisher_bloomberg", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:35:13+00:00", "text": "Billionaires Ready Legal Attack If California Wealth Tax Passes - Bloomberg.com\nBillionaires Ready Legal Attack If California Wealth Tax Passes Bloomberg.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "fa00e74e7934db378677ac66", "title": "Court injunction blocks PNP bid to take control of Clarendon Municipal Corporation - Jamaica Observer", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxQeUpxemVPaHViMzBkZHBra21tUEt3MThtLVV3MV9Ga2tucmhDS0xvVndDUllIRTNmSFF6X2ZYU1VNX05SZEF4eV9YMWxwWGE2WWRlRDVTQmU3ZzlXTFpIcFZSVzVzYmgzYWI4U1NzU1ZBdkpMWlBJUmxlTFVCZjlWRklUczFfOVQ4VW1aRGhiekpJTU16d1F3cFVuaDA2TmxteVljTktBYVJpUlFONlN2aEpYTk9jc3VqX2JEb1dn?oc", "source": "lane_blast_legal", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:34:49+00:00", "text": "Court injunction blocks PNP bid to take control of Clarendon Municipal Corporation - Jamaica Observer\nCourt injunction blocks PNP bid to take control of Clarendon Municipal Corporation Jamaica Observer", "truncated": false}, {"id": "aa4ff6b8cb3df8f6febc02d1", "title": "AI tool receives FDA clearance to predict breast cancer recurrence - WFTV", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixgFBVV95cUxPb09aeERaYzRvM1gzb2RINHI0ekxmUUdXOEhfc1Z1S1ZzeUFZQktLT0tNdGFSLWptWHlBTklHdFQ4UkpVNlFKRXVCd1FfQ1J3d2JJRVNwYnphanVFVElXYjJBc0d3cjRkNW1wRlRrb0tONWZNNWtlWWVMLU5jMHlzSDZiYkdSTTNIbGVFdXpIYTVHa3JnWEhsbzBtb2I2cUJKbFpVUnFvTE9QSHF6dUUwbjVFN1NJdGsyUWk5bkR0d2N", "source": "lane_gate", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:34:47+00:00", "text": "AI tool receives FDA clearance to predict breast cancer recurrence - WFTV\nAI tool receives FDA clearance to predict breast cancer recurrence WFTV", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d73de03455bfb55072282d25", "title": "International Seaways in $370M Bruton acquisition - Marine Log", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxOWGVEa0JqeXdUVUxwczFndWd6aGlXZW1SbGlvZkRNaUNGaHhvZDM4YWxfR2oxOXpUcXZrWjJRVmdLRGh6VXBndHIzcVA4XzI1ZlNHUTdtd2dvcF9hQ0FXZ2JRUV9rLTQ0aUV3QmVITG5NVFJDSWlBTlAxYVZ5MmYzRW1Ld1M1YUE?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:34:36+00:00", "text": "International Seaways in $370M Bruton acquisition - Marine Log\nInternational Seaways in $370M Bruton acquisition Marine Log", "truncated": false}, {"id": "a5b978af7737e0da698b7fb6", "title": "Latest poll shows Bolsonaro maintaining edge over Lula in Brazil run-off", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/latest-poll-shows-bolsonaro-maintaining-edge-over-lula-in-brazil-run-off?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:34:26+00:00", "text": "Latest poll shows Bolsonaro maintaining edge over Lula in Brazil run-off\nShare Latest poll shows Bolsonaro maintaining edge over Lula in Brazil run-off on social media\nSupporters of Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva are seen in Minas Gerais, Brazil [EPA]\nAnother poll has shown leftist Brazilian President\ntrailing behind right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro in the October 25 run-off election.\nThe survey, released by CNT/MDA on Friday, showed Bolsonaro taking 46.8 percent of the vote, compared with 45.9 percent for Lula.\nThe media battle behind Brazil’s election\nA political dynasty? Why the Bolsonaro family dominates Brazil’s right wing\nBrazilian government calls for probe into US funding of far-right causes\nThe latest projection comes a day after a Quaest poll found Bolsonaro carrying 46 percent of the vote, compared with Lula’s 44 percent. A separate Datafolha poll found Bolsonaro taking 47 percent of the vote against Lula’s 45, down from 49 percent a week earlier.\nAll three polls currently fall within a 2 percent margin of error, meaning the race is still considered by many experts to be a toss-up. Still, they underscore an uncomfortable political climate for Lula, who had a month ago been projected to easily sail to victory at the ballot box.\nThat was before Bolsonaro, the son of former President Jair Bolsonaro, took\nin the first round of voting on October 4.\nBolsonaro won 56,104,503 votes compared with Lula’s 53,879,538.\nThe senator has hewed closely to the political persona of his father, who has been barred from running for re-election until 2030 after an electoral court ruled he abused his authority to cast doubt on the 2022 presidential election.\nThe elder Bolsonaro has remained under house arrest while serving a 27-year sentence connected to efforts to overturn the 2022 vote, which he lost to Lula.\nFlavio Bolsonaro, 42, has pledged a crackdown on crime and drug trafficking and to cleave taxes used to pay for government programmes. A win would make him the latest conservative leader closely aligned with US President Donald Trump to take power in the region.\nLula, meanwhile, has been holding regular rallies hoping to energise his supporters. The 80-year-old politician is seeking a fourth, non-consecutive term after a\nOn Wednesday, the country’s Congress approved an amendment to give workers two paid days off a week, as opposed to one.\nThe move gives Lula a major victory on one of his top social reform promises just days before the vote.\nThe election comes at a pivotal time for Latin America’s largest economy. Brazilians are grappling with concerns over crime and the cost of living, while the country faces an increasingly tense relationship with the United States. The vote is also being closely watched across a region that has shifted sharply to the right in a series of recent elections.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "b4b1d8b0f4e225b453d43c25", "title": "Tesla Launches Roadster at SpaceX Site in Latest Merger Hint - Claims Journal", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMic0FVX3lxTFAyS2IwOEY4bkNMcDVfaVo1aHU5aGVfeWRIV3hNamduU0Nldm5qNGFXR0xWczkyWTFaQ3lJMnVmekRpMEhBbWZzZkpfY1pyejlKcUNiUzJVbmp1bXhNMnBkQk9YZGNvWUd4MHlGS1ZTLXhOSUE?oc=5", "source": "topic_products", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:34:00+00:00", "text": "Tesla Launches Roadster at SpaceX Site in Latest Merger Hint - Claims Journal\nTesla Launches Roadster at SpaceX Site in Latest Merger Hint Claims Journal", "truncated": false}, {"id": "dad44741b518708d806783c9", "title": "NL-ix acquires Swedish internet exchange STHIX - Techzine Global", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxNRTZlSG9zWlVDM3liSlR6Wkw2QlJPYnVuNlVRaTZzdFVNVS15dHZWTnd2WUMtVFJ1ZzJtLUFyMTRMenQ5Vjl5bkVyTFRPTTB3NzFEZnViSUZscENTTmJ5V3RvNzRmSWJDWGlxNWRTcXdndTZFYUh5NEFsc1BEWURjeVpadVdzdUdRNzd0cDk2bWVPWFpxRjFsUUFLR2dIUWc?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-16T16:33:50+00:00", "text": "NL-ix acquires Swedish internet exchange STHIX - Techzine Global\nNL-ix acquires Swedish internet exchange STHIX Techzine Global", "truncated": false}, {"id": "c9d5d11a9e619b828ff7d781", "title": "US federal bankruptcy court operations disrupted by cybersecurity incident - Reuters", "url": "https://news.goo