andon Feldman - Yahoo", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxPcTVBeVI0N0F0c3hvTUowRnJwamZxM0pyNVlKdFZSRHU0bzlzRlVVTlU4WW9nakxnZThUbHZjZUE5cS0zUndEbHlfSU8xR2Fod3dCb1lVRV9QMUVabnJzQVYweGJOUnBaZEFMbU5fV0pvX01rYU9OQkMwZkRKUEJWc3hITTJmY0k2d2ZHbm5NbG12b1pObkdGYlA0ZWVMNFVBYmdXQmZVWUpieE0?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-16T15:52:22+00:00", "text": "Netflix Acquires ‘Canopy’ Creature Feature Spec From Brandon Feldman - Yahoo\nNetflix Acquires ‘Canopy’ Creature Feature Spec From Brandon Feldman Yahoo", "truncated": false}, {"id": "f075e1a0555ce68b9d40e37f", "title": "Manchester Utd have ‘moved on’ from Martinez outburst, says Carrick", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/16/manchester-utd-have-moved-on-from-martinez-outburst-says-carrick?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T15:52:18+00:00", "text": "Manchester Utd have ‘moved on’ from Martinez outburst, says Carrick\nShare Manchester Utd have ‘moved on’ from Martinez outburst, says Carrick on social media\nManchester United manager Michael Carrick looks on as Lisandro Martinez, right, trains [Jason Cairnduff/Reuters]\nto follow our live coverage of Leeds vs Manchester United.\nMichael Carrick said Manchester United had “moved on” from Lisandro Martinez’s outburst aimed at the club’s hierarchy this week, saying it was “really not a drama for us as a group”.\nSpain punished by FIFA for Islamophobic chants during Egypt friendly\nPro-Nazi chants before Ajax match slammed by Croatia leaders\nAsian Cup in Saudi Arabia still on, organisers say, but golf tour postponed\nDR Congo protests Formula 1’s ‘indefensible’ decision to race in Rwanda\nArgentina defender Martinez took aim at the hierarchy of the struggling club following United’s\nto Atletico Madrid on Tuesday, saying Carrick had been left with an under-strength squad.\ncriticised technical director Jason Wilcox\n, saying he had “100 percent” expected more investment during the summer transfer window after United finished third in the Premier League last season.\nIt is understood Martinez has been fined for his outburst, but Carrick said he would be in United’s squad for the Premier League match at Leeds on Sunday.\n“It’s done, really,” Carrick said at his pre-match news conference on Friday when asked about Martinez’s comments and his\n“We’ve moved on from that,” he said. “It was one of those things. He has come out and acknowledged the situation, and as a group we’ve moved on.\n“It is really not a drama for us as a group. The boys have trained really well; there was a really good feeling around training this morning.”\nMartinez issues apology, but Keane calls Man Utd a ‘circus’\nMartinez, 28, issued an apology on Thursday, saying he had held positive talks with the club’s leadership and Carrick.\n“Everyone knows that I am a passionate person and that I live football with great intensity,” he said in a post on Instagram.\n“The frustration of the defeat led me to express how I felt at a time and place that perhaps were not the right ones, and for that I want to apologise.”\nFormer United captain Roy Keane branded the situation at his former club as “a bit of a circus”.\nUnited travel to Elland Road, the home of one of their fiercest rivals, with just two wins from nine games in all competitions this season.\nThey are 13th in the Premier League, with just one win from six matches and", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "2312d9dfb65f6000456feb1d", "title": "Michigan engineer who helped expose Flint Water Crisis files for injunction to block EPA policy - Yahoo", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPRUw0MHBsRnhQeGMyUV9fbGZyZjAtRVVlVl9wZDFqVl9qb1dOS2tyNW5tb2RGV3UzeldMbWs1bHhJWWMtOUMzQ0RNdDlmRU9qdWNCYW0yYTlYNHJmMzRwNGdjM21FVmlfVDVRdjdRVTZPbU5kS0NEeFhkSEQ5ekVnYUk0a1dQRzJDOHVOMzF4V3R1aGE5R3VYZnVWeTNmUQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_blast_legal", "published_at": "2026-10-16T15:52:13+00:00", "text":