: "Security firm Proofpoint acquires Varonis for $6.3bn - www.thestack.technology\nSecurity firm Proofpoint acquires Varonis for $6.3bn www.thestack.technology", "truncated": false}, {"id": "1c887f3fada5581f95a84aef", "title": "Canada’s Inflation Data, Business Survey on Tap ahead of BoC Decision - Action Forex", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi0wFBVV95cUxQQ1dBMUxwTnRKRjZoUnl3WC1mVnBaWW5CVHYzSVdJM1dqWFV3dmNEdFhVdTZudjNaSHgzTDI5akk5TnMwMnIzOFd4cC1kTm9BSllyc2hjV0FkdUwwRjU0c09CM1I3R0FfVlppU3laZDRLWlZVMzFVYklkUXRScnNnZkhlR2djZ1FBeC1MNFRiaXZRRDF3dUZKbWMxX2JrVlJTaEhYNWhnb1RZZk5sTlZ3WWE2ZHBodVNxallqZkdOSEx", "source": "lane_factor_impulse", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:58:04+00:00", "text": "Canada’s Inflation Data, Business Survey on Tap ahead of BoC Decision - Action Forex\nCanada’s Inflation Data, Business Survey on Tap ahead of BoC Decision Action Forex", "truncated": false}, {"id": "64cd8626a4f88dd3e05f2545", "title": "Patients in chains rescued from suspected illegal rehab centre in South Africa", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmwyvxj49gpwo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:57:51+00:00", "text": "Patients in chains rescued from suspected illegal rehab centre in South Africa\nOfficials uncovered \"gross inhuman conditions\" when they raided the centre\nA pastor and his wife have been arrested in South Africa after 200 people, some in chains, were found held at a suspected illegal rehabilitation centre in the north-eastern part of the country.\nThe facility, operated from a church in Mpumalanga province, was discovered during an operation by officials in the area on Thursday.\nAuthorities said they uncovered \"gross inhumane conditions\" when they raided the facility, with some patients found with \"sores all over their bodies\" and \"others chained to each other\".\nPolice have since charged the couple, who were running the facility, with kidnapping but could add more charges. They have not yet commented.\nIllegal rehabilitation centres have mushroomed in South Africa in recent years as drug use spirals in the country.\nLast year, the department of social development said it had uncovered over 100 unlawful facilities operating across the country, mostly in Gauteng province, home to the country's largest city, Johannesburg.\nA girl of 16 and a boy of 11 were found being kept in the same room as adults in the Mpumalanga centre.\nTwo minors were among the 200 people found living in crowded rooms at the facility\nThe couple running it told officials they were housing 60 people, but upon inspection, more than three times that number were found, including more than 30 women.\nThe group, mostly believed to be drug addicts, were found in crowded rooms and without access to functioning bathrooms or running water.\n\"Some [of them had] been at the alleged illegal centre for a while,\" the department said.\nGift Skhosana, one of those held at the facility, told local broadcaster Newzroom Afrika it was \"common practice\" for patients to be chained.\n\"They chain us as punishment [and] when you gain entry,\" he said.\nDespite this, Skhosana, who was a drug user, said the facility helped him get clean and overcome his addiction.\nAnother person, who was not named, said his experience with the facility left him needing help mentally.\nThe couple charged a monthly fee of 3,000 rand ($182; Â£137) to house the patients, of which almost a half would go to the church.\nFourteen of those found at the centre have since been taken to hospital for further medical treatment, police said.\nOfficials said 132 have been reunited with their families.\nThe couple is expected to appear in a local court on Monday.\nThe South African men trying to end violence against women: 'Every man needs to play a part'\nTwo Mexicans arrested as police uncover big meth lab on South African farm\nGrim discoveries of murdered women spark fear in South Africa\nfor more news from the African continent.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "7f18009306b0ebc3499aedf9", "title": "Watch Japan’s Cyberattacks Are an AI Warning - Bloomberg.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPSkVUN2V3eXlvM0Z0SHdIZXloY0hObjVabGRwelphTkc4UHA5RDRaXzl2c0xoSU5DZVhPUjdsalM3RDRzbmJYYmxZb3hhZDJ6NXZxYjU5VW9MNlNNQVFDZkg5eXFrd3ZXZ2FWN01YOVRrZ05JX1dPRHBEYzVrVUxOUUlXaXIyM2QteGlwaUViTEFGbXpHS01ORjRCOVhKdzJDa1gw?oc=5", "source": "publisher_bloomberg", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:57:44+00:00", "text": "Watch Japan’s Cyberattacks Are an AI Warning - Bloomberg.com\nWatch Japan’s Cyberattacks Are an AI Warning Bloomberg.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "88da931b405d753a817d07d1", "title": "Carpenter Technology (CRS) Sets Up A Leadership Change And Dividend, Is It 39% Undervalued? - Simply Wall Street", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi2AFBVV95cUxOcE53RS1rMS1kX3VjMUlwS1VOVGRDWTg5eTRBT180SmdYVnVLSkxIdk5VWlh5NzlnbmszaDF3VGhqeTZSY1NvNFk1aklwVUNLdTBqVkQzSFdTUU0xVFNQSzZkc1NhazJiNS0tZm8zRFNseWtweDNud2NWb0VrSXA2VV9DdHRGM2JpeDZzQUpqekFDQUdqc2thVHV4NERPZFNhN0VnbFZaVmExaTJSYV9JdDJVQnZObG1qSTUtN0ZqOFh", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:57:43+00:00", "text": "Carpenter Technology (CRS) Sets Up A Leadership Change And Dividend, Is It 39% Undervalued? - Simply Wall Street\nCarpenter Technology (CRS) Sets Up A Leadership Change And Dividend, Is It 39% Undervalued? Simply Wall Street", "truncated": false}, {"id": "eab3a10be9b53c48c3417b3d", "title": "Varonis Systems Acquisition by Proofpoint 'Makes Sense' as Market Competition Intensifies, RBC Says - marketscreener.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi4wFBVV95cUxPRlhGRUJHZTFjaGRQWGl3cHBULThBUWlRMVFKbzNfRWF4MW5pM2dsR0ZOUmVreVRRWVNpUkRCeDhQUWZZWXRXWEw2LVFPaDZ6NUlXWC15WE4tN0liakZkc0t5WXpFSUdvUzBvOWNqVU5yRmdLeG4wMjZ5bWhGMlRGVUFZc3RvUlhhNlFGRkxtamw1RTY1RS1pZWstUDBlNlFTSVVwbEpPZE1HVmY2Njk0WTdHbzhxUU5ieDNRRV9RQk9", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "publis