s 40 technologies in AI, biomedicine and PV for export controls in draft revised catalog - The Annapurna Express\nChina adds 40 technologies in AI, biomedicine and PV for export controls in draft revised catalog The Annapurna Express", "truncated": false}, {"id": "044b4bea2d1a4758f81a6614", "title": "Pope pictured for first time since surgery and cancer diagnosis", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw146ej00yn7o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:36:39+00:00", "text": "Pope pictured for first time since surgery and cancer diagnosis\nPope Leo thanked medical staff as he was pictured for the first time since his lung surgery\nPope Leo XIV has been pictured celebrating Mass from hospital,\nin the first images of him released by the Vatican since he underwent lung surgery.\nThe 71-year-old pontiff was diagnosed with lung cancer after\nthe operation, which the Vatican said had been \"successful\" and proceeded without complications, at Rome's Gemelli Hospital on Tuesday afternoon.\nThe images shared on Friday showed the Chicago-born Pope wearing green vestments while standing behind a makeshift altar on the tenth floor of the hospital.\nThe head of the Roman Catholic Church \"celebrated with the medical and nursing staff\" and thanked workers for their service, the Vatican press office said.\nPope's cancer diagnosis leaves Catholics questioning what comes next\nAlso on Friday, the Pope phoned Russian President Vladimir Putin from hospital to urge a ceasefire in the Russian-occupied Ukrainian city of Oleshky, where\naccess to food and water has been cut off for thousands\n\"The fact that he accepted the call and spoke with the Pope may, I hope, be a sign that the Pope's request will indeed be carried out,\" said Cardinal Pietro Parolin, the Vatican's secretary of state.\nWithout mentioning a ceasefire, the Kremlin said: \"The Vatican's intention to help create the conditions necessary to ensure the safety of the town's population and to organise vital supplies has been supported.\"\nIt added: \"It has been agreed to co-operate on this matter.\"\nThe UN high commissioner for human rights, Volker Turk, made a similar plea to address what he described as a \"desperate\" situation in Oleshky.\nThe Pope's doctors said on Friday that tests had shown \"a steady improvement in his general condition\" since his surgery.\nHis doctors said that a chest X-ray indicated \"good recovery of the operated lung\".\nThe whole lower lobe of the Pope's right lung was removed \"to ensure the procedure was radical\", the Vatican said following the surgery.\n\"After the operation, the Pope awoke normally and returned after a brief period of observation to his room,\" it said earlier, before he spent a \"peaceful night\" at the hospital.\nThe pontiff is expected to remain at the hospital for about a week as he recovers\nThe pontiff first announced that he would be having the operation during his weekly Sunday prayers, telling the crowd in St Peter's Square that doctors had found a \"well-contained\" nodule on his lung \"at an early stage\" and advised him to have it removed.\nNodules are quite common and not necessarily cancerous, but after it was examined the medical team confirmed it was, \"as suspected by pre-operative tests\", the Vatican said. He was diagnosed with lung adenocarcinoma.\nThe Vatican has stressed that the Pope had shown no symptoms of infection or illness prior to the procedure.\nWho is Robert Prevost, the new Pope Leo XIV?\nPope diagnosed with lung cancer but had successful surgery, Vatican says", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "328f4b9fa79b09e5c632fa1c", "title": "Loyalist’s President discusses fall enrolment, a cyber attack, and the path back to the black - Quinte News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxPRVFXY3BtNkgwSk9UNzRuTHNDODdYUWk3V1F5UUp0d1NqOWxlQllrTE9FaS1fSUtkVjVscHJ3cXZidTJHMjZKNFhMWHFjZlFMNXl3cy11SnhLdXpPTWNXcmlVd2tlZ0