80,000 As Market Volatility Worsens Baystreet.ca", "truncated": false}, {"id": "96e04839a2ec138376f5b84e", "title": "Snowmass Creek Capital acquires Timber Cove Resort - hotelbusiness.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigwFBVV95cUxQczJLc2hDejhJLTgtbVZvODBPdmJ0QmJSc2hkbjZTblVwXzlidWdLTnhMT3pkZ1hnR2Yxei1mbHZPRUdlU1ZMUnI0TEtaUnkxOW5tNGhheGt5a0ZjSGxXTGZMSmJBVzNVbjlyQnJvUVE1X0dsSXdkMGJPbTFLblItWk5Saw?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:24:06+00:00", "text": "Snowmass Creek Capital acquires Timber Cove Resort - hotelbusiness.com\nSnowmass Creek Capital acquires Timber Cove Resort hotelbusiness.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "c8349ad4dce591e2903cc746", "title": "Two Sigma Halts Real Estate Unit Fundraising and Cuts Staff - Bloomberg.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxQcWhoZXhBaUFEQ255LU1MNmlvNjA0b3k2aTQ1dWZQNC04VHNRV2NZM2J2a1BIZkxsZVQ1cHdZNmxsQkduOHBnZmIxSEFFR1dCaDA5RGlnN1NGX2N4Qk9DNU1uVVozZjFkUE1MbF9qazlKTTd5RzR2Wk4yNkE3dlU2aEczbXA0bHVlOTVYS1VpRkVpa1FVRFdpYkNrUmdHdnVNeUhqU2FJMGlUVTNucU9J?oc=5", "source": "publisher_bloomberg", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:23:47+00:00", "text": "Two Sigma Halts Real Estate Unit Fundraising and Cuts Staff - Bloomberg.com\nTwo Sigma Halts Real Estate Unit Fundraising and Cuts Staff Bloomberg.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "ccd9b3f124631f65cfeffa0d", "title": "Warsh Boosts Market Expectations of Fed Rate Hold in October - Bloomberg.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqgFBVV95cUxQdHZhMDY1QkVFRU1NQ0c1NkxlNzR2cDR4NEgwbVFMSkQ3RzFSNlFYT1Q0d1BzOWpRUGtLcTg1YUk0UkxOc2tKWENkTGxkRWc5SFAwWDFMS3JxdXJfWUIyNmwzR1Z0T3B5SmF0R2hjc0lDdXppV0wzQmw2bHh0a0FZS1BsUXVJdkdyZF9YcWIxMlZ3RnMwOVZ0YlFDeHdFWE5nTXdSdlQwb2NfZw?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_business", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:23:04+00:00", "text": "Warsh Boosts Market Expectations of Fed Rate Hold in October - Bloomberg.com\nWarsh Boosts Market Expectations of Fed Rate Hold in October Bloomberg.com Fed Chair Kevin Warsh warns of AI 'shock' for economy, pledges to contain inflation ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos Analysis: Everyone expects the Fed to hold rates in October. Kevin Warsh could surprise us all CNBC Key Moments From Kevin Warsh’s Speech to the IMF WSJ Warsh Vows to Tame Inflation as A.I. Delivers ‘Shock’ to Economy The New York Times", "truncated": false}, {"id": "a5f8adb44676d30055d67e48", "title": "Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-rdf", "source": "rss_dw_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:23:00+00:00", "text": "Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama\nStudent protests in the Albanian capital, Tirana, have turned violent\nImage: Hameraldi Agolli/AP Photo/picture alliance\nThe luxury high-rises transforming Tirana's skyline are meant to project the image of a modern European capital. But at the foot of one of these buildings, Samanta, a 22-year-old master's student in economics, is in tears.\nShe removes the mask she had been wearing to protect herself from tear gas.\n\"How could I ever afford an apartment in one of these towers on a salary of €540 [$608]?\" she shouts, as she stands facing a line of police officers. \"I share the rent with people I don't even know because my family has emigrated. We're exhausted.\"\nUniversity lecture halls in Tirana stand empty as students boycott classes and take to the streets, demanding the resignation of\nAlbanians have been protesting since late May as part of a broader anti-government movement known as\nmultimillion-euro tourism development linked to Jared Kushner\n, son-in-law of US President Donald Trump, in the protected coastal area of Zvernec.\nProtesters destroyed an ATM during clashes with police during an anti-government protest by students on Thursday\nThe movement has, however, since grown into a broader challenge to Rama's government.\nOver the past three days, the student demonstrations have erupted into violent clashes. Bins, businesses,\nand banks have been set ablaze, with some completely burning out. Tear gas has filled the air.\nA total of 152 people have been arrested and 324 are under investigation over the three days of protests. Injuries have been reported among both protesters and police officers, with the police saying 71 officers have been injured in the clashes.\nThe students are angry about conditions at universities, the cost of higher education and poor employment prospects after graduation. But above all, they want the government to step down. They say they are not willing to negotiate any of their other demands with the prime minister.\n\"You didn't listen to us for four months while we protested peacefully. Now you'll listen as the city burns,\" said Samanta.\nDuring the first two days of the student protests, the prime minister remained silent.\nThen, at 8:03 a.m. local time on Thursday, Rama appeared in a video message recorded inside the fire-damaged College of Europe building, just meters from his office on Tirana's main street, the Boulevard of the Martyrs of the Nation.\nA total of 152 people have been arrested over the past three days, with injuries reported among both protesters and police officers\n\"These are the hands of an opposition that, hiding behind masked people, wants to drag\nback to a place it will never return to,\"\naddressed the protesters' central demand — his resignation. In comments to Reuters, he ruled out stepping down, saying governments are changed in elections.\nThe following day, he also accused \"foreign hands\" of seeking to prevent Albania from joining the\nThe unrest comes at a critical moment for\n. Brussels has called for calm and restraint, urging all sides to avoid further escalation and engage in dialogue.\n, the 82-year-old leader of the opposition Democratic Party and a former prime minister, rejected Rama's accusations that the opposition was behind the violence.\n\"We have no idea whether it's Greece, Iran, Serbia or someone else,\" he told a press conference, mocking Rama's claims of foreign interference. \"The Democratic Party fully supports this protest and will stand by it until the end. Resign and leave immediately!\"\nStudents against the political establishment\nFor Rigels Xhemollari of the Albanian civil society organization Qendresa Qytetare (Civic Resistance), the student revolt is the culmination of months of peaceful protests.\n\"The main reason is the prime minister's failure to respond during four months of protests and his mockery of the demonstrators. Other reasons include the economic situation,\nand successive scandals,\" Xhemollari told DW, referring to a number of corruption investigations involving senior government officials.\nalone. Protesters have also voiced their frustration with Albania's political opposition.\nThe students are demanding that the government step down, and say they are not willing to negotiate with Prime Minister Rama\n\"We want the political class of the past 35 years to go. We want a new Albania with new leaders,\" Skerdi Topalli, a 20-year-old journalism student, told DW.\nFor political analyst Mark Marku, dean of the Faculty of History and Philology at the University of Tirana, the protests mark a turning point.\n\"This is the reaction of a generation. In a society that was not responding, they woke people up and made us think about change,\" he told DW.\nBut Marku warns that even Rama's resignation and fresh elections would not necessarily bring new political leadership.\n\"Challenging the government is not an end in itself. A protest must produce a result,\" he said. \"There must be a platform, a political alternative. You cannot vote for a protest.\"\nXhemollari, meanwhile, sees Rama's resignation as the only way to end the revolt.\n\"The protest has just one political demand, and it requires a political solution: the prime minister's resignation,\" he told DW.\nXhemollari says that Albania's president should bring political parties together to form a caretaker government led by a non-partisan prime minister, paving the way for local and parliamentary elections in May 2027.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "57f38c0c923829205befe1f2", "title": "Fangda Special Steel Technology To Acquire Holding Company - TradingView", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixwFBVV95cUxPS0ZRQ19TQVlOQm5sSzhoYnJaV2VmQWNFY1dGV2xYTm4wQnNqMkVJa2xCdkp5NXp0MGI5QXNYNllKcWVRU0VQOGpFZEM3SnZHY1R0OEpVX2x4N0dNRGo2aWxNWDYtbC1mVnZUSXNQTUpMVmYxV0k1bUtZeS0wYjZ5Mzh3SnB4N3dUNXNYTkJtYjJxR2Y0VGhUR1VFS1NfaXJ6MkpYYi1qSHhZVXhXaEZjUGkzM0RQR2sxNFlKclI1U0J", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:22:59+00:00", "text": "Fangda Special Steel Technology To Acquire Holding Company - TradingView\nFangda Special Steel Technology To Acquire Holding Company TradingView", "truncated": false}, {"id": "09d51ba14e693d5b5cd537db", "title": "State Treasury says September revenues rose 22.1%, a rebound from understated Corporation Business Tax collections last year - ROI-NJ", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-gFBVV95cUxNYVNPRUR4MjN0dFdhaUdXei0yZ3JpRkt3dzJwVlhDOEJLbW1HcVE2eklFZnJXZmlqbmcwUmNpRXRXRkRFbGFyZm8wajBiUWJuMExOd0s3cUFPSVNZN25YR2hmb3JBaEVabU9MQVp4aVdIRFdMLXhXbk1TTHZYUXlSRzhJUVF6X3FwSUp0UVp2X2JoWElZallWR29MV3FDVkl1czJFeTQ2b0dxa2p3RUctQndwSkNHV25SUjRGMHBRZVh", "source": "topic_government", "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:22:53+00:00", "text": "State Treasury says September revenues rose 22.1%, a rebound from understated Corporation Business Tax collections last year - ROI-NJ\nState Treasury says September revenues rose 22.1%, a rebound from understated Corporation Business Tax collections last year ROI-NJ", "truncated": false}, {"id": "695cdefa16faa8ae42bc545a", "title": "Spri