iUHNRcmFjNFNZNFlST3RXOG5ab3R6Z2tqWHFaV3JTeFVxOTVwakVuVDJaVG5SdWR3MFdZeG1SNWREZTJUd1FBekRhSmtnVHR6ajFwcHR", "source": "sec_4:google_fallback", "published_at": "2026-10-16T13:13:15+00:00", "text": "Form 4 CHURCH & DWIGHT CO INC For: Oct 15 Filed by: Buchert Brian D - StreetInsider\nForm 4 CHURCH & DWIGHT CO INC For: Oct 15 Filed by: Buchert Brian D StreetInsider", "truncated": false}, {"id": "5bda78cefaeae14e0070946c", "title": "Spain punished by FIFA for Islamophobic chants during Egypt friendly", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/16/spain-punished-by-fifa-for-islamophobic-chants-in-egypt-friendly?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T13:13:12+00:00", "text": "Spain punished by FIFA for Islamophobic chants during Egypt friendly\nShare Spain punished by FIFA for Islamophobic chants during Egypt friendly on social media\nAn anti-discrimination message is displayed to fans in the RCDE Stadium during the match between Spain and Egypt, March 31, 2026 [Albert Gea/Reuters]\nSpain have ‌‌‌‌been fined $20,000 and ordered to partially close their stadium ⁠⁠⁠⁠for their ⁠⁠⁠⁠next friendly after supporters twice chanted Islamophobic slogans during the game against Egypt in March, FIFA said ⁠⁠⁠⁠in a statement.\nat the RCDE Stadium near Barcelona, home of LaLiga club Espanyol, ⁠⁠⁠⁠where some Spain fans chanted, “Who doesn’t jump is a Muslim” during a World Cup warm-up match which ended in a 0-0 draw.\nMan Utd veering towards crisis as Man City cloud hangs over Premier League\nMan United’s Martinez apologises for outburst after talks with Carrick\nWhat led Manchester United’s Martinez to meltdown in Madrid – all to know\nAfter the second occurrence of the chant, the stadium announcer ‌‌‌‌issued a warning and the scoreboard displayed a message against discriminatory behaviour.\nSpain winger Lamine Yamal, who is Muslim,\nat the time, describing them as disrespectful and intolerable and calling those responsible “ignorant and racist”.\nSpanish police launched an investigation the following day, while world governing ⁠⁠⁠⁠body FIFA later started\nagainst ⁠⁠⁠⁠the Spanish football federation (RFEF).\nIt argued that the word ‘Muslim’ was “neither insulting nor pejorative”, adding that the fans’ conduct should be assessed under FIFA’s Article 17, ⁠⁠⁠⁠which covers political, ideological, religious or offensive messages, rather than Article 15, which deals ⁠⁠⁠⁠with discrimination and racist abuse.\nHowever, FIFA’s disciplinary ⁠⁠⁠⁠committee rejected that argument, saying Article 15 does not require the explicit use of a slur and that a term can be discriminatory when ‌‌‌‌used in context as “an insult, taunt, or marker of inferiority”.\nFIFA fined the RFEF and ordered the closure of at least ‌‌‌‌15% ‌‌‌‌of available seats for Spain’s next friendly.\nAl Jazeera has contacted the RFEF for comment.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "7637c1915f433faabee5ce88", "title": "Stock Futures Quiet Even as Rate-Hike Fears Subside - Schaeffer's Investment Research", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxOZzhFSjF3TGN5NDJPLUdTV1FpU3Y5UkdzV0ZpS2hoNGVZUkVlRlducGNCQjNndFEyYXNGVlVGb0pUNng5SU5kU2lkQ1EyNlR4UEg4eEtES2ZiOWtfVlp6dms2eGljVnp1bXd4YVYyN0d0bGVUd3FBSkZvY3FLM2ZkazViXy1fdksxbnlHU1NMS1BTdzFyVmY1X2pZaERjOVQtNU1CWE9pQXpJandIUGx3OG1n?oc=5", "source": "lane_factor_impulse", "published_at": "2026-10-16T13:13:00+00:00", "text": "Stock Futures Quiet Even as Rate-Hike Fears Subside - Schaeffer's Investment Research\nStock Futures Quiet Even as Rate-Hike Fears Subside Schaeffer's Investment Research", "truncated": false}, {"id": "426b7c90a1db4875a9a0f350", "title": "Strata Minerals MD Peter Woods to Update on Zelica Gold Project at Sharewise Webinar on 19 October 2026 - Kalkine Media", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi5AFBVV95cUxQQWtnZ09KSkpwWXEtYkZSc1dQd2ZDZlpvQkNlUVJtU1hadDRZV0IxQ0Jua2dZb0p3REtTS3l0ZzRvVHJYdmxSY2JaNFB3bXI4MG5MQjdFU2J6ZGdZZFpacko4aE54bzdZR1Q4ZGlKYm9zQ