h slammed", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/16/pro-nazi-chants-ahead-of-ajax-match-slammed-by-croatia-leaders?traffic_source=rss", "source": "rss_aljazeera_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-16T12:42:30+00:00", "text": "Pro-Nazi chants before Hajduk Split-Ajax UEFA Europa League match slammed\nShare Pro-Nazi chants before Ajax match slammed by Croatia leaders on social media\nTorcida, supporters of Hajduk Split, on their way to Poljud Stadium before the UEFA Conference League game with Ajax [Ivana Ivanovic/Pixsell/MB Media/Getty Images]\nCroatian leaders have slammed pro-Nazi and anti-Semitic chants by Hajduk Split football fans before their UEFA Conference League match against Ajax, while Israel’s embassy voiced shock.\nGroups of Hajduk Split fans, known as the Torcida, marched through the coastal town of Split before Thursday’s match chanting: “Crush the Jews”, “Rise up Adolf (Hitler)” and “Let’s go Ustasha”, referring to the country’s World War II pro-Nazi regime, local media reported.\nMan Utd veering towards crisis as Man City cloud hangs over Premier League\nMan United’s Martinez apologises for outburst after talks with Carrick\nMan United’s Martinez takes to social media to defend his criticism of club\nWhat led Manchester United’s Martinez to meltdown in Madrid – all to know\nDozens of fans were detained before Thursday’s match for violence. During the match, Torcida fans set off flares and other pyrotechnics in the stands, forcing more than a 10-minute stoppage.\nAn investigation was opened into the pro-Nazi chants and suspects are being detained, police said.\nPresident Zoran Milanovic in a Friday statement condemned the incident as “unacceptable and shameful”.\nHe urged swift action against the perpetrators to “show that there is no place in Croatia for the glorification of Nazism and Ustasha ideology”.\nIsrael’s embassy in Zagreb said on X it was “deeply shocked by the serious antisemitic incident that took place in Split and condemns it in the strongest possible terms”.\nConservative Prime Minister Andrej Plenkovic also condemned “messages of anti-Semitism … completely at odds with the values we want to uphold in Croatian society”.\nHajduk Split, who won the game 2-1, in a statement apologised to UEFA and Ajax who “witnessed scenes which we do not want Europe to remember”, while the Croatian football federation also condemned the incident.\nCroatia’s ultra-nationalist hardcore supporters have tainted the country’s image for years, notably by chanting pro-fascist slogans and displaying Ustasha symbols.\nThe Ustasha regime killed and persecuted hundreds of thousands of ethnic Serbs, Jews, Roma and antifascist Croatians.\nCroatia were docked a point by UEFA after their fans painted a swastika on the pitch in Split in 2015, before a Euro 2016 qualifier with Italy.\nIn recent years, the country has seen a growing tolerance for its pro-Nazi past, and critics accuse authorities of failing to sanction the use of Ustasha emblems.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "6aa916150e60baa2eb820f7e", "title": "COMMENTARY: AI jitters, Trump's fading oil clout and China shock 2.0: The financial week in five charts - Reuters", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi3gFBVV95cUxPT0JUeTlGZHJqb29Dcnp1dEhpLXFEN0EwdG1IX0pzb29pampFTEhISTdSODVqdDd4a2dSRllSSy12YzBHSXR1bmZCVmJyRXFmTl9IN2tDVTkwbWFXa09hTUFhaER0U2hZMkh3YTZwaXlMZzkyUUNMUWtRUW96clBaR3JpNnVFanlyUjFqek1FWTV3TGtqbHRHWDR1RDZZZnBiRFlzdElpcEw3czFJaVkyT3pMLURLQm1FQzhxY0lJdHB", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-16T12:41:56+00:00", "text": "COMMENTARY: AI jitters, Trump's fading oil clout and China shock 2.0: The financial week in five charts - Reuters\nCOMMENTARY: AI jitters, Trump's fading oil clout and China shock 2.0: The financial week in five charts Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "61e5cb38c1a880c8d3302fa1", "title": "PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia spin-off boosts val... - Pluang", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/arti