 Imran Khan stronghold\nSchool roof collapses in northwestern Pakistan, killing at least 35 people\nAt least 34 students aged 13 or younger, as well as a teacher, were killed in the roof collapse.\nThere are conflicting reports about whether the inspections will cover both public and private schools or only private schools. The province’s education department has been given three days to report its findings, according to The Associated Press news agency.\nSchools are to be classified as safe, in need of repairs or improvements, or potentially unsafe. Various structures will be assessed, including roofs, ceilings, walls and staircases.\nPolice arrested Mohammad Khan, the owner of Al-Khair school, shortly after the roof of mud and bricks collapsed.\nThe building was structurally weak, according to Peshawar Police Chief Saeed Ahmed, who also said that Khan had told officers that recent rains had weakened the structure.\nBereaved families are demanding justice, with some of the victims’ relatives maintaining that they had warned Khan about rainwater repeatedly seeping into classrooms.\nDozens of mourners gathered outside the school on Friday to remember those who died.\nPakistan’s construction standards are widely reported to be poor and builders commonly use substandard materials.\nThe roof of a private tutoring centre in the eastern city of Lahore", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "cb6955cb233a03a6fb93c1cf", "title": "SpaceX proposing sharp increase in Starship launches from Texas - SpaceNews", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxNM2FabGJTMi1DZWE0VWljczZNTjBDMGVUT3c2UWs3ZDlNajZIamhyQ3lrSktJN0pQeTNKdUNiMGMySEx1WG5YTmswYWN4WFVOSDVIRUJlSW1qaFJqdk0xYlVXYzRBQThhR29MZTR1NjRDYUF1dXBaOERlVHRva1dQZFYwRnRsa3FEUFZjRnUyWQ?oc=5", "source": "topic_products", "published_at": "2026-10-16T12:17:47+00:00", "text": "SpaceX proposing sharp increase in Starship launches from Texas - SpaceNews\nSpaceX proposing sharp increase in Starship launches from