RPYVFLUFRKenBfZDV1QXM4Tzh0VVhWM2Nodzg3dHZhVmEwODZRN3RRblpaQQ?oc=5", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-16T10:37:50+00:00", "text": "‘We will not lift any sanctions’: EU backs Ukraine as funding pressures grow - EU Perspectives\n‘We will not lift any sanctions’: EU backs Ukraine as funding pressures grow EU Perspectives", "truncated": false}, {"id": "48e138a5e53b70d12f4b9141", "title": "South Korea considers widening naval operations towards Strait of Hormuz - The Arab Weekly", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxOZHlfbFJZaDdyZEFNejJBUE9Gclc2RmJqUEQyN1JVSUFrRHBZeU4wWmJ6d3doXzhqWnBPVnRndFo4WHJwNm9lRFkxeEV4VWEzZy1udERWN0pHZEMtSEJzNVhNSnAyTVpjMTM4dWEwZXZ1MG9ST0cyQXNlcHdrNk53M09UWGJzdEg2TkVLejdUSjVPdG9ySFpFQURzVQ?oc=5", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-16T10:37:49+00:00", "text": "South Korea considers widening naval operations towards Strait of Hormuz - The Arab Weekly\nSouth Korea considers widening naval operations towards Strait of Hormuz The Arab Weekly", "truncated": false}, {"id": "cf058019e6251aa022652567", "title": "Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-rdf", "source": "rss_dw_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T10:37:00+00:00", "text": "Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue\nAir traffic was reduced at hubs across Italy, including Milan Bergamo Airport [FILE: March 10, 2026]\nImage: Tiziano Manzoni/LaPresse/ZUMA/picture alliance\nfaced delays and cancellations on Friday because of a problem with the country's\nThe ENAV air traffic control authority ruled out foul play such as a cyberattack, and said it was forced to introduce temporary restrictions of the volume of flights after identifying a data transmission problem.\nand Milan warned of likely disruptions and advised passengers to check with their airlines.\nWhat did authorities say about the problem?\nENAV said it first identified the issue overnight. It was forced to restrict the volume of flights at around 6 a.m. (0400 GMT/UTC) as the number of scheduled services increased.\n\"We would like to inform you that this morning we guaranteed the greatest possible number of departures, including intercontinental flights,\" ENAV said.\nShorter-distance services were more likely to be interrupted.\n\"Despite the anomalies encountered on the data transmission network, we are deploying all available resources to minimize disruption and restore full operations as soon as possible,\" ENAV said. \"We confirm an operational capacity of 50% of total air traffic, ensuring maximum safety at all times, which remains the Company's top priority.\"\nENAV said it had ruled out the possibility of the disturbance being caused by \"malicious acts.\"\nRome airports operator ADR warned passengers that \"flight delays and cancellations may occur\" and advised passengers to contact their airline if uncertain. Milan airports company SEA issued a similar notice.\nIf you rely on our team for trusted reporting, please take a moment to\nselect us as your Preferred Source on Google\n, so you'll always see our verified news first.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "7433f8645088d73b53b28d78", "title": "Qatari Investors Group Q.P.S.C. Reports Earnings Results for the Half Year Ended June 30, 2026 - www.marketscreener.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi3gFBVV95cUxQV1RMZ293ZzNwS0YxdjBGMXJtbmtyaUt1Sms2eXdlemlJNXBzZWpLVzZFSlk4ZTYtemVaSDBEcWl0bVlacEh4WUJHWlNWVFNJcUtEMXI2dFB1RW80NnplQm9TUzJZVkRGZTExRkpRdG9BVjd2d0FTeW96dEZsRTB5VVhFVko3TzJZc2lfOVhlTjBjLXRYWjRGbjNqU2JiRXlYYXVyVi12VlBTNXpBU3AtaHhDai1FWnZabldKRl9uNGY", "source": "lane_print_vs_priced", "published_at": "2026-10-16T10:36:50+00:00", "text": "Qatari Investors Group Q.P.S.C. Reports Earnings Results for the Half Year Ended June 30, 2026 - www.marketscreener.com\nQatari Investors Grou