AI exports amid US rivalry Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "ba5e3aa297e873d71e56aff1", "title": "Lovell Girls Varsity Volleyball @ Powell - MaxPreps", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxQZDR5YTN2RUZCcW1kT3ZqZTlBOFhxT1FVZXRPb1lKLWVfMWhWNkt0X3FtUEwxcHhDRVJRQUZoVXNqVGRSLTBNYzNVNU55dlNUNkNwNGxFZ2QyTUhmazNLSVVvMjZyTVgyWjA3bkUyOThNTFEwZXhaV09TN2c3STFvZjduZDU3YnA4SXpWZU02T01MOUdBMFZ0U0N6Vy1md2JVWjRDMWIyUVZkRnN0dURiaHlB?oc=5", "source": "topic_fed", "published_at": "2026-10-16T08:45:57+00:00", "text": "Lovell Girls Varsity Volleyball @ Powell - MaxPreps\nLovell Girls Varsity Volleyball @ Powell MaxPreps", "truncated": false}, {"id": "ec09cceda66bc5712a716ab2", "title": "China tells Israel to stop 'forced establishment' of West Bank settlements", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq1j3wdxy48ro?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T08:45:54+00:00", "text": "China tells Israel to stop 'forced establishment' of West Bank settlements\nChina has been positioning itself as a mediator for conflicts in the Middle East\nChinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi has told Israel to stop its \"forced establishment\" of settlements in the West Bank and reverse its actions, his office said.\nThe \"Palestinian question\" is \"the greatest historical injustice of this century\", Wang told Israeli President Isaac Herzog in a face-to-face meeting on the sidelines of a conference in Azerbaijan on Thursday.\nBeijing has been a long-standing supporter of the Palestinian cause and has maintained that a \"two-state solution\" is the \"correct direction\".\nIt has also been positioning itself as a mediator for conflicts in the Middle East.\nIn 2023 Beijing brokered a deal to restore diplomatic ties between Iran and Saudi Arabia after years of hostility. Earlier this year, it was part of efforts, along with Pakistan, to propose\na ceasefire in the US-Israel war against Iran\nBeijing's efforts to tackle the war in Gaza have focused on Palestinian unity.\nIn 2024 Beijing got rival Palestinian factions to\nagree to form an interim \"national reconciliation government\"\nfor the occupied West Bank and Gaza after the war with Israel, although it was never implemented.\nNow, Wang says the \"immediate priority\" is to fully open access to Gaza and stop the continued spread of a \"humanitarian catastrophe\".\nChina is willing to work with the international community to get the parties to return to dialogue and \"seek a political solution to the conflict\", he said.\nIn a post on X, Herzog said he was \"pleased\" to meet Wang and their talk \"focused on the relations between our countries and the situation in the Middle East\".\n\"I emphasised Israel's desire for peace in the region, alongside the strategic threats to our security, first and foremost from Iran and its terror proxies,\" he wrote.\nChina maintains close ties with Iran and is the biggest buyer of Iranian oil, which had previously come under US sanctions because of Tehran's nuclear programme.\nChina itself has been accused of trying to dilute its minority populations by encouraging Han Chinese migration to Tibet, which it annexed in the 1950s, and Xinjiang. Beijing rejects those claims, saying its policies promote economic development and social stability.\nOne year into the ceasefire, people in Gaza continue to live under the regular threat of Israeli strikes, displacement and food security challenges.\nAlthough large-scale bombardment has stopped, Israel has\ncontinued strikes in Gaza almost every day\n. More than 1,400 Palestinians have been killed in Israeli strikes there in the year since the ceasefire started in October 2025, according to the territory's Hamas-run health ministry, whose figures are considered reliable by the UN.\nThe US-brokered ceasefire was the first phase of a deal to end the war in Gaza, which had been triggered by a deadly Hamas-led attack on Israel on 7 October 2023.\nBut progress into the deal's next phase has been stalled, with both Israel and Hamas accusing each other of violating the terms of their agreement.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "4c102d2b73674d493663b53b", "title": "China tells Israel to stop 'forced establishment' of West Bank settlements - BBC", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTE1lblNOOEc1RDc5Ti1Bdy1EX1p6VEQyZ3E1ZHp2TUdpRGI2QW9BVVgtSVBoQUhyazJoRWxaT0FialpnT3RyeFdvNlg3YWFJS3hwREV4eUFTTDN4Rmc?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-16T08:45:54+00:00", "text": "China tells Israel to stop 'forced establishment' of West Bank settlements - BBC\nChina tells Israel to stop 'forced establishment' of West Bank settlements BBC Chinese FM tells Herzog that Israel should stop ‘forced establishment’ of settlements The Times of Israel China tells Israel to stop ‘forced establishment’ of West Bank settlements Al Jazeera China pledges continued support for Palestinians, pushes for two-state solution The Jerusalem Post China says Israel should stop its 'forced establishment' of West Bank settlements Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "524a85b98277180691eecf79", "title": "How Are Bonds Rising Amid Surging Inflation and High Oil Prices? - tastylive", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxQMDFOcGZpck9UcHJRaVJQWm1RbVlOaHNIcVo1Qk5uM0dFWE5Qc0JsSWZvblMyenlqajdIcUFrMlQySy1JbFVISW9uM3dGWWZJQ1BXaHZPVHlyb3hIRnFnUTlUX25xWGk0V21TV1J0NmZRQnpOLXhfd3NQSVBlcVExVldIbnZHRkIwNnhMbmJ4dXRDZWg3blB6bEszZTJNUk1lWU1KVHp3?oc=5", "source": "lane_regime_state", "published_at": "2026-10-16T08:45:44+00:00", "text": "How Are Bonds Rising Amid Surging Inflation and High Oil Prices? - tastylive\nHow Are Bonds Rising Amid Surging Inflation and High Oil Prices? tastylive", "truncated": false}, {"id": "9e70a8bde6f1d5e6ca1935bc", "title": "Soma Gold lines up $1.76M credit line from its own chairman - Dealroom", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxNVm1oMnJ2dVhOVVNpckJJMWJnLVlCTVJzanIzWH