m/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxPS2lmeWFIa05OQm12UHptekctYmxBYXlpTjFTNFhFOEp0bjZmTGc5TlpaQ2RLWDhFSnlldnJENl9Vdi1GR1VsdlN1QWg4d2w2eHk4UlI4UFJvRlgxa1FxOFhKVFYzdlJ1aEVYMG0xR0QzWEpraU05dGtlM21qMWt3Tk5KYXlHWmRsUHJqaDVQUW9QeDFQNkQw?oc=5", "source": "lane_insider_flow", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:54:28+00:00", "text": "Kohl's insider sells 18,352 shares amid mixed m... - Pluang\nKohl's insider sells 18,352 shares amid mixed m... Pluang", "truncated": false}, {"id": "ee0a25caa33c0467761b31c5", "title": "Suspicious mailings to election officials, congressional offices under investigation - NPR", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxON21YSVJ3M3RlZ3lkT251WlJwTm9RUS1kMFhSRXMtLWloalgzc09aUFJUblFTdVpGUk1jQ215VGtFTDRoNmFJVGFRc01PS1lsU3pESEo5aFZaTUxfa2sybGR0cm1iSHR3ZC1XTjJVdG9NYWIwcWNrNkJMSGF3S3NVc3dnNV8tcVB3N2xZcEtVLWNOTWgzQ2xSc1dpdw?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_us", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:54:15+00:00", "text": "Suspicious mailings to election officials, congressional offices under investigation - NPR\nSuspicious mailings to election officials, congressional offices under investigation NPR Authorities investigate letters with 'suspicious substances' sent to congressional, election offices Yahoo Congressional Staff Open Letters Containing Suspicious Substances The New York Times Letters with unidentified substance sent to Sen. Klobuchar, Rep. Morrison and Minnesota secretary of state CBS News FBI reacts after Alabama secretary of state’s office gets latest suspicious package WSFA", "truncated": false}, {"id": "7fe597b800cb35ba37441cd4", "title": "Harvard’s endowment jumps 27% in fiscal 2026, lifted by SpaceX as top holding", "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/15/harvards-endowment-jumps-27percent-with-spacex-as-top-holding.html", "source": "rss_cnbc_finance", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:53:49+00:00", "text": "Harvard’s endowment jumps 27% in fiscal 2026, lifted by SpaceX as top holding\nHarvard University's endowment grew 27.1% in fiscal year 2026, the school announced Thursday.\nThe return was powered by a $2.2 billion stake in SpaceX that Harvard revealed in a regulatory filing in the second quarter.\nThe rise comes amid a push by President Donald Trump's administration to seek penalties against the 21,000-student school, and threaten to withhold funding over diversity commitments and other issues.\nStudents walk on campus at Harvard University, in Cambridge, Massachusetts, Nov. 19, 2025.\nendowment grew 27.1% in fiscal year 2026, its strongest return in five years, the school said in its\nThe endowment, which beat the S&P 500's 22.3% total return in the same period by 4.8 percentage points, now totals nearly $68 billion. The outperformance came amid actions by the\n\"While markets can easily take back what they give, that return will strengthen the endowment's capacity to support the University over time,\" Harvard's chief financial officer Ritu Kalra and treasurer Timothy Barakett wrote in the 49-page annual report. \"The University deliberately smooths distributions so that operating support does not rise and fall with the markets. Strong investment returns therefore support Harvard's work gradually, through future distributions.\"\nThe returns marked the best year for the endowment, managed by the Harvard Management Company, since 2021. Harvard's fiscal year ends on June 30.\n, Harvard unveiled a $2.2 billion stake in Elon Musk's\nrocket and satellite company. It marked the endowment's largest single holding by value, trailed by\nTaiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company\nHarvard's financial picture, though, is undermined by moves by the federal government. Federally-sponsored research revenue declined 19.5% to $509 million in fiscal 2026.\nAnd starting in the current fiscal year, \"endowment resources will face an additional constraint, with the federal excise tax on Harvard's net investment income rising nearly six-fold, from 1.4% to 8%,\" Kalra and Barakett wrote. \"We estimate the higher rate will cost roughly $300 million a year.\"\n\"[I]n a year of returns like this one,\" the federal excise tax \"would be several times larger,\" they noted.\nPresident Alan Garber acknowledged such headwinds, but said in the report that Harvard can still succeed.\n\"Together, we have the opportunity to set the University on a path to excellence that none of us can imagine today,\" he said. \"Notwithstanding the challenges and uncertainty, this is a thrilling time to be part of a great American institution devoted to Veritas.\"\nChoose CNBC as your preferred source on Google and never miss a moment from the most trusted name in business news.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "e42d5d36dafbf61145377bd0", "title": "Brian Sullivan: Why the 'real' price of oil is likely $30-$40 higher than where it is now - CNBC", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxOTDVXY1ZpZnRCd2hRSFJZM3JkNlRONmNubzdkSEt0Y093TlVfNGVlUXpLYWcxWUtBTFFTYlFhekVBVF85TDBKMmFjSGg2VWhLeFVFTXJMd0VzbnFaM2gtcnhSaVoyVC1SVXRMa2xhUHg4Wi11ZXVreTE0Y0xCN1A5TVNfVnZfdUt5dUN1YVFWSEVPX2VDTy1feDROa0J6LW83Zi1JQXdTcGdaQ0poanN2akpuTnoxanRCSUtIVHp30gH", "source": "lane_regime_state", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:53:29+00:00", "text": "Brian Sullivan: Why the 'real' price of oil is likely $30-$40 higher than where it is now - CNBC\nBrian Sullivan: Why the 'real' price of oil is likely $30-$40 higher than where it is now CNBC", "truncated": false}, {"id": "0a195895679c34c486ae4232", "title": "Iambic banks $150M from IPO to advance cancer pipeline - FirstWord Pharma", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiU0FVX3lxTE5lVHdFMGEwWXVJY0pGQ1E2MEZyVE5yU1BVdi1ONjhtUE5icGtkendONEF3NEJIUjlBWGVRUHJpaFNIbHkzUzh0WVlWUFE1aDdHQ21Z?oc=5", "source": "lane_listing_flow", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:53:18+00:00", "text": "Iambic banks $150M from IPO to advance cancer pipeline - FirstWord Pharma\nIambic banks $150M from IPO to advance cancer pipeline FirstWord Pharma", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8a9