 Finance SSI, Social Security Benefits Set To Rise Disability Scoop", "truncated": false}, {"id": "6fe19b13b6f1f59890f6067e", "title": "Oeste sets final day, Oakland loses burger and sushi options, and Berkeley's Nabolom closing after 50 years - The Oaklandside", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxNYWlRSmo3OWhwZHJaeXRDaDB6ZVlYVWd2N3B5bENCV21kNGE4UkxQN05iT3JEclNSbkloWjFwMDVsS3p3UHZSQThmOUtCT2pJTUhIbzladnMwdXFFQ3ZxU05JM2JEOXd1Mi1oUHFLWnpmN25aT1NlOUNuZV9oNUpRaVZrdFJFOU85enU4UnB2Rk5rSGpZY0pDRnpzeEhaTmM?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_business", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:00:00+00:00", "text": "Oeste sets final day, Oakland loses burger and sushi options, and Berkeley's Nabolom closing after 50 years - The Oaklandside\nOeste sets final day, Oakland loses burger and sushi options, and Berkeley's Nabolom closing after 50 years The Oaklandside After a half-century of baking, Nabolom is closing; plus one burger spot is swapping in for another, and a Sliver Pizza shutters Berkeleyside After 50 years, treasured Berkeley bakery to close San Francisco Chronicle Breakfast truck, Indian, sushi and crepe restaurants among September closures The Oaklandside", "truncated": false}, {"id": "32165ee6af8945a5bd83e423", "title": "Bringing GPT-Rosalind to academic research labs", "url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-the-rosalind-academic-plan", "source": "company_openai_blog", "published_at": "2026-10-15T19:00:00+00:00", "text": "Bringing GPT-Rosalind to academic research labs\nOctober 15, 2026 Research Product Bringing GPT‑Rosalind to academic research labs Introducing the Rosalind Academic Plan, offering eligible labs sponsored access to GPT‑Rosalind and tools for life sciences discovery. Apply for access (opens in a new window) Loading… Share We’re introducing the Rosalind Academic Plan to help more academic scientists access GPT‑Rosalind ⁠ , our dedicated life sciences model, which combines frontier reasoning with Rosalind workbench ⁠ (opens in a new window) that enables specialized tool orchestration across medicinal chemistry, genomics, wet-lab assistance, and other scientific applications. Eligible labs can receive up to 30 Business Standard seats at no cost for up to 12 months, with access to GPT‑Rosalind subject to trusted-access approval. Academic research creates knowledge that entire fields build on. Work that begins with a fundamental question about biology can eventually change how we diagnose disease, develop medicines, or grow food. But those advances depend on scientists having the resources to explore ideas, test them, and share what they learn. Accelerating scientific discovery is central to OpenAI’s mission of ensuring that artificial general intelligence benefits all of humanity. With this plan, we’re investing in the scientists doing that foundational work—helping more labs combine their expertise and judgment with AI tools built for life sciences research. Supporting the research behind future breakthroughs Many of the advances we rely on today grew out of years of basic research. The Human Genome Project helped launch modern genomics, transforming medicine, diagnostics, and biotechnology. Curiosity-driven work on bacterial immune systems led to CRISPR-Cas9, which revolutionized genome editing and is now advancing research in cancer, inherited disease, agriculture, and biotechnology. Decades of university research on mRNA also laid the groundwork for COVID-19 vaccines and a new generation of vaccines and therapies. Academic research has always laid the groundwork for advances in medicine and biotechnology. By helping more scientists combine their scientific expertise and judgment with the advanced specialized reasoning of GPT‑Rosalind, we hope to support discoveries whose benefits reach far beyond the lab. How academic labs are using GPT‑Rosalind OpenAI is committed to enabling academic researchers to pursue their scientific ambitions. Distinguished academic labs are already exploring how GPT‑Rosalind can support work ranging from protein design to understanding neurodegeneration. These examples show where researchers are applying the model within their scientific workflows. 1 of 3 “ GPT‑Rosalind helped me gather drug physicochemical parameters faster. PubChem and NCBI tools helped me work across ten drugs while refining the distinction between predicted and experimentally measured values ” Zhao Lab, UCSF “ I use GPT models throughout my research, fr", "truncated": true}, {"id": "5d284dc2be82d7b46f13ef20", "title": "Custom apparel company Custom Ink explores sale, sources say - Reuters", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQd0ZES1M0NU53cDUyTzd1YWE5SDQ5azhIRkgxZU1Zbi1YeDcyc2VOYmpuZHdRZDY5QWh5cmhESnBLeXlSR1dfeHBoOXBpM0J4YjdkelN0NlIyYVpDclNwWmtUTjVyU2VyTmdaQU43ZDlpbnduV1JQM0s1NkV4Q2ZHWnJ5Zl9fV3IxTEdmWlpVbVRVVnFhdXc2UFpLWFdVRWN0My1tRnNoVkxFRlVNR0xlUm9aUmx0UQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_strategic_review", "published_at": "2026-10-15T18:59:43+00:00", "text": "Custom apparel company Custom Ink explores sale, sources say - Reuters\nCustom apparel company Custom Ink explores sale, sources say Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "858cda994f9bae40ad8d0b07", "title": "Sydney airport security workers strike - The Age", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxNcEZfaF9ockZ4clphcXJhdmdXWktFd2hGbG5GSzdEbnN5QkZZN3NVV21McTJ3WTJ2ZXpxYkRBM1owb2NFYzZRUEE2NnhzV3BmWFFPbWN4LVBkU3o2VW1GM050dV94dG5hdWtPSmYtNTRYNldoTDBRUG1qOFgxdmJPYnUxY0JJZVo2T1UyUmVzUDA1Rkg2Q3VhaXdR?oc=5", "source": "lane_labor_stop", "published_at": "2026-10-15T18:59:39+00:00", "text": "Sydney airport security workers strike - The Age\nSydney airport security workers strike The Age", "truncated": false}, {"id": "3214db4b1f2c16e053223059", "title": "Sydney airport security workers strike - SMH.com.au", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxPM2k2ckdya3dWM1FuSFR0U3BGdmpTeERBZDdNd3k4NXlmcVlxN3RNRkxndDFQNjE3ek1VcWtaTGFCQnFUQWhUSHh5ck5aM2xwSFVSbFBVVmhiN3pUWl