ncated": false}, {"id": "06492ee51449305f9ba76e49", "title": "AutoCanada launches strategic review of collision repair centres - RENX", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxPRVdYakZzaG8zRDF6aUpOLTBrTmhEYk9zQUFfZGJLeVNZMlUwMV84WTBVU1hLTm9FRDA4ZmRtVndmMFBlNFQ4dnhnTU44MzQtemtsYmdyZTFxVXh0MXd1bWZPNVVQZzllQ2RIRGlaNjJSVjM0VDE2d292TllaT0p4MzJKQjdCOEZIQnJtR3g3Q0Nsa1pRUm1TdC0zQQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_strategic_review", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:52:59+00:00", "text": "AutoCanada launches strategic review of collision repair centres - RENX\nAutoCanada launches strategic review of collision repair centres RENX", "truncated": false}, {"id": "fd2f4943d47bdbb731b4514f", "title": "Maduro pleads not guilty to new torture-related charges in New York", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqwyrn1l74zro?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:52:44+00:00", "text": "Maduro pleads not guilty to new torture-related charges in New York\nOusted Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro and his wife, Cilia Flores, are seen in a federal court in New York in July.\nVenezuela's former leader NicolÃ¡s Maduro and his wife, Cilia Flores, appeared in court on Thursday to plead not guilty to new charges of conspiracy to commit torture.\nThe US government initially accused Maduro of narco-terrorism, drug trafficking and weapons-related offenses, before adding new charges against him and Flores last week.\nMaduro and Flores were captured in January during a US military raid, after which they were taken to New York, where they remain in jail.\nThe couple has pleaded not guilty to the allegations and both have argued to have the case thrown out on the grounds that they qualify for sovereign immunity. Their trial is scheduled for June 2027.\nIn a new indictment last week, government prosecutors alleged Maduro and Flores \"created and maintained a violent system of repression\" that saw \"thousands of Venezuelans\" killed, harassed, and tortured.\nNicolas Maduro denied the new charges brought against him by the US government, telling a court on Thursday he denied the \"false accusations and false testimony against me.\"\n\"I reject this document entirely,\" Maduro said in Spanish through a translator.\nJudge Alvin Hellerstein interrupted Maduro, and declared the court would enter a plea of not guilty for Maduro.\n\"I am completely innocent. I am not guilty,\" Flores said through a translator.\nMaduro and Flores wore beige jail uniforms and both appear to have lost weight during their detention in Brooklyn.\nThe alleged torture methods included \"electric shock, asphyxiation, rape, forced nudity, prolonged isolation, starvation, punishment cells, and psychological torture\", the indictment states.\nThe US also accused Maduro of authorising the use of torture \"against specific individuals\" and alleges US citizens were tortured under this system.\nProsecutors already have accused Maduro, his wife and son, and their accomplices of engaging in a cocaine-trafficking conspiracy and partnering with cartels designated as terrorist groups.\nMaduro previously called such charges a tool to further \"imperial\" plans for getting access to Venezuela's rich oil reserves.\nHe and his wife's lawyers have argued that Maduro is the leader of a sovereign country and therefore immune from prosecution. They contend the US taking him by force is illegal.\nFlores unsuccessfully petitioned a judge to allow her to be released on bond while she awaited trial, arguing she had heart problems and other health issues while detained at the notorious Metropolitan Detention Center in Brooklyn.\nVenezuela's ex-leader NicolÃ¡s Maduro charged with conspiracy to commit torture\n'I thought I was going to die': Jailed Venezuelan activist details brutality of prison life\nUN receives reports alleging torture of detainees in Venezuela continues", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "66c65b87ac6c9acb16a77269", "title": "PACER: Login - United States Courts (.gov)", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxQTm5kVzVfNjRLUE0ycjlQc2pXQ2ZvTWF2Tk14ZGVPS2lrUnNtUHFuRzVSNkFfal9kODZ3elBmZUNJb2RUYnoybTZuYnlvNlJXVlBSWUlmaUR4a3FQQ3lsdXlkejBwWUxWUzFlaGR2UEppS1NQR1dSMlJhZmpJdjB5ajZKZ0wzRUFMNWpiNUxGbm91LTNGdXZOelJ2T2djdnZLX1lOUW5yR3lrQ2FqQTRsLS1CWklHQWZVS0FnYWFHbnd", "source": "official_court_search", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:51:58+00:00", "text": "PACER: Login - United States Courts (.gov)\nPACER: Login United States Courts (.gov)", "truncated": false}, {"id": "23e03698df6bc78c77960663", "title": "Partnership Defends 1,500 Acre Gift, $19M Deduction - Law360", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxNUUx3RDJRWGkyQlNiNkdaelBDZFlrNmhZRzdtRlJDb0MwZWZLY3ltd2lzaG1RZTBDVGVIbmlwNl9aQ3RCZHJWT1ZocWYxT1g5UlhnU3NzNUVIbFJja1M0YktLNDVOa09wN1pRckcxYTZ6SWo2N1FhVGt0dW9YMUF3d1RIbXJ2REQ3eVVteXZKSnlXMmvSAWhBVV95cUxQSkJnNmpJcFQyRU1HRXdEMXVuVmpoQ2t3akljWURLWnltOVJ", "source": "lane_tax_fiscal", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:51:58+00:00", "text": "Partnership Defends 1,500 Acre Gift, $19M Deduction - Law360\nPartnership Defends 1,500 Acre Gift, $19M Deduction Law360", "truncated": false}, {"id": "9dfa849acd6aae6be6ce7f72", "title": "Slate Grocery REIT agrees to US$2.3B all-cash buyout by Brixmor-Everview JV - RENX", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxQNFNDQ2gtWmdKN194T0V2dHg4UXY4eTNUNUdVaHZ1S284VDVwSXEtenZUOHR5dk9JZzJ0YjNqY25nN0J6Tjl2dVJzdW1yS1M2a2xPeklpWTRMU1dHb0FtUkliQjNjeXhSdXBLX0JxTXRQT0JnRmZpZTNmcVJpZnVnR3lYcjdSMWVsb2p4TkdwWTA4bDVyVEo0TG05aDUtOUU?oc=5", "source": "lane_strategic_review", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:51:30+00:00", "text": "Slate Grocery REIT agrees to US$2.3B all-cash buyout by Brixmor-Everview JV - RENX\nSlate Grocery REIT agrees to US$2.3B all-cash buyout by Brixmor-Everview JV RENX", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d488895637c4074e2c4046b4", "title": "An Egyptian farmer found \"an unusual stone.\" It led archaeologists to pieces of statues for an ancient king. - CBS News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMieEFVX3lxTE80QzA5ekdCeXR5c0JKeG9VWmdxek50SXVSbkFCY0Q2SlR6ZkcwbVdGQjEwckdoYUxqcURhQTFabXo0OE9oR1BQMTJCdWZLZVBKV2JsajFoR3RDaXJ2cDlXZ2taZmdwWVpubWVmYm1lNmU2dkdGWENlWQ?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:51:08+00:00", "text": "An Egyptian farmer found \"an unusual stone.\" It led archaeologists to pieces of statues for an ancient king. - CBS News\nAn Egyptian farmer found \"an unusual stone.\" It led archaeologists to pieces of statues for an ancient king. CBS News Man discovers mysterious stone outside home, leading to massive 3,300-year-old Egyptian treasure FOX Weather Giant Ramesses II statues found in Behbeit El-Hagar after a villager reports a carved stone block Archaeology News Online Magazine Egypt man uncovers a stone block while working on his land. Then experts realize it belongs to a 3,000 year old king allegedly from the Bible Yahoo 2 giant Ramesses II statues, one wearing a double crown, discovered by man in Egypt Live Science", "truncated": false}, {"id": "64e921aaa04cd034456ec6d6", "title": "Russia accuses Ukraine of attacking oil refinery after Zelensky says strikes to resume", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqwyrnwd9dw1o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:50:18+00:00", "text": "Russia accuses Ukraine of attacking oil refinery after Zelensky says strikes to resume\nUkraine's President Zelensky accused the US of withdrawing intelligence-sharing about Russian strikes to place pressure on Kyiv\nSouthern and Eastern Europe correspondent\nRussia has accused Ukraine of attacking an oil refinery on Thursday after President Volodymyr Zelensky said such strikes, halted at the request of the US, would resume.\nZelensky said he had restricted attacks for three days while Russia continued striking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. \"We're done,\"\nRussian President Vladimir Putin said Kyiv had also tried to hit refineries on Wednesday - which Ukraine denied - but there had been no \"significant damage\".\nZelensky also accused the US of withdrawing intelligence-sharing to pressure Kyiv into ending attacks but Ukrainian defence sources later told the BBC some functionality on Starlink satellite services had resumed.\nThey said \"operation while on the move\", part of Starlink's military service Starshield, had been restored, although it remains unclear whether restrictions on the speed at which drones could fly while still maintaining Starlink internet connection have been fully lifted.\nOfficials were still working to clarify \"the reasons and circumstances\" behind the move, the sources added.\nIn a separate development, seven people are missing after\na drone attack set a chemical tanker on fire off Romania\n, according to naval officials. Moscow said it had hit two cargo ships with military cargo heading to Ukraine's Odesa port, without naming them.\nWhy is Starlink internet so important on the battlefield in Ukraine?\nEight crew missing after drone attack leaves tanker ablaze off Romania's coast\nThe Kremlin said Kyiv had \"attempted a large-scale attack\" on a refinery south of Moscow early on Thursday.\nAccording to Russia's defence ministry, four missiles and dozens of drones were intercepted and the falling debris caused a fire at the site in Ryazan.\nZelensky said dozens of Ukrainian cities had come under Russian attack in the past day.\nHe previously said he would agree to the \"energy ceasefire\" announced by US President Donald Trump on Sunday if Moscow also abided by it.\nBut he accused Russia of ignoring the proposed deal within hours of it being announced, with strikes leaving hundreds of thousands of Ukrainians without power. The Kremlin never said it had agreed to the deal.\nZelensky agreed that he felt betrayed by the US when asked by Piers Morgan on Wednesday night, after Washington appeared to withdraw key elements of its support.\nEuropean leaders have rallied around the Ukrainian president. Italy's Defence Minister Guido Crosetto told the BBC that the US restricting its intelligence-sharing with Kyiv would be a \"complete mistake\".\n\"Because it is a fundamental form of support. This means denying a country any chance of defending itself.\"\nHe added: \"Peace will be achieved when Putin will be convinced that there is a stalemate... that he cannot advance anymore. But if he sees a weakness on the Ukrainian front, if the United States takes its resources away, then Putin will think he can win, and so he will continue the war.\"\nZelensky met Nato chief Mark Rutte as a two-day summit of European leaders began in Brussels on Thursday. The head of the military alliance said they had discussed \"the importance of implementing an energy ceasefire as well as Nato allies' continuous support for Ukraine\".\nZelensky told the FT that Ukrainian officials had been told by US counterparts that \"if you will not stop [the strikes], we will block intelligence\".\nUkraine's military relies on US early-warning alerts of incoming Russian aerial attacks to mount air defences, limiting successful strikes, while Starlink internet links are used throughout its war effort to guide drones and protect its skies.\nThere were suggestions a technical glitch was to blame for the sudden Starlink restrictions on Tuesday evening, but owner Elon Musk appeared to deny this and suggested\n\"It was not a technical problem, it was the will,\" Zelensky told the FT.\nTrump has denied halting intelligence-sharing. Starlink's sister service Starshield is provided to Ukraine under a US defence department contract. The BBC has approached the US authorities for comment.\nZelensky has questioned Trump's relationship with Russia President, Vladimir Putin\nZelensky spoke to the FT during a visit to London on Wednesday which also included a meeting with Prime Minister Andy Burnham in Downing Street -\nwho announced the UK would speed up delivery of lightweight multirole missiles to Kyiv\nThe Ukrainian president told the newspaper he would now only halt strikes on Russian oil infrastructure - which Kyiv says are vital to cutting off revenue streams to its war machine - if the US supplied more Patriot air defence missiles.\nUkraine has suffered a shortage of the US-made defences since the outbreak of the Iran war consumed stockpiles.\nStriking a more defiant tone than recently, the Ukrainian president told the newspaper his American counterpart had an affinity for autocratic leaders like Putin.\nHe said it was not up to him to mend US-Ukrainian relations given the events of the past week: \"We didn't destroy any relationship.\"\nTensions have previously frayed between the two leaders. After returning to the White House last year, the pair shared a fiery Oval Office meeting in which Trump implied Zelensky was the main block to a peace deal.\nZelensky has since walked a careful diplomatic line, showing willingness towards US-brokered deals while stressing that the terms of any peace deal must be just.\nagreement between Russia and the US to release 300,000 tonnes of diesel to the US and global marketplace\n, struck last week, as the US effectively investing in Russia's war effort.\nTwo people were killed in Sloviansk, Donetsk, after overnight strikes, where a number of residential buildings were destroyed\nThat deal was the latest effort by Trump to lower fuel prices in the US ahead of the midterm elections, after months spent grappling with the political consequences of the Iran war, which has sent fuel costs skyrocketing.\nZelensky told the FT: \"The question will be: when will the next deal be? Maybe it will be gas. Definitely it will be gas.\"\nWith Russia continuing to strike Ukraine, Zelensky suggested the disruptions to US support was no coincidence.\nLocal officials report at least 13 people were killed across Ukraine on Wednesday in what Zelensky called a \"constant\", large-scale Russian attack. He said more than 850 drones had been launched at dozens of cities and communities.\nAt least three people were killed in the central region of Kirovohrad as it suffered its largest attack since Russia's full-scale invasion began in 2022, officials there said, with nearly 360 drones launched during a 10-hour barrage. Deaths were also reported in Donetsk, Kherson and Volyn.\n\"It is clear that Russia deliberately escalated these attacks, taking advantage of the easing of sanctions and seeing attempts to pressure Ukraine,\" Zelensky wrote on social media.\nWhy Moscow is staying tight-lipped on Trump's energy ceasefire\nStarlink restrictions in Ukraine war linked to political situation, Zelensky aide says", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "23dcf1c92ab10355bdb2a021", "title": "‘Tulsa King’ Spinoff ‘Frisco King’ Drops Official Teaser & Season 1 Premiere Date - Whiskey Riff", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQbzJkNzR6YmZhQVJKNnlHV0NaS0hESXJMdU9MaEpkOU9MY1ZwTUlIeW83Vlp6STNTUmlBVjNfdXhKYm1rVGJaeldyU3ppbEpBTERGT3JBbjk4RmJRR0dxcnZYSkh4RE5pQTJsVzZSdDJMbEk0N1NSZzdHb3dUVW4tRDdGX25faUxxbW1aUUpka3RGSnhKMkxTWXhvakM2OTJ4M0Q0NWVuQzRfTVBITHNqOF9raWpfdw?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_spinoff", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:50:15+00:00", "text": "‘Tulsa King’ Spinoff ‘Frisco King’ Drops Official Teaser & Season 1 Premiere Date - Whiskey Riff\n‘Tulsa King’ Spinoff ‘Frisco King’ Drops Official Teaser & Season 1 Premiere Date Whiskey Riff", "truncated": false}, {"id": "b58388821c5cb45856ac632b", "title": "Zocdoc acquires Sohar Health for insurance verification - MobiHealthNews", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxOeWlqb2hGVzN6eEhQbXdOc3ZIeVB3RjU5TVZtWUxtTnFYeVRqalNQWW5yeFZyY0VGNWN2WlVMWjlNa1RrcGdQUXRFbjBlWlRjTk1MOHNmS21zcEM3LUFzVEVqZUxjZEx4am5TSWtMWlBkalpDUmRDWkRobkdWVGRvYmxiU252ZmttZGhkd0w2dy0?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-15T16:49:29+00:00", "text