 "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirAFBVV95cUxPZTlOQktpU1ZfbHJqamFUaE01WERtc3N2MWxaUmZIcHp0MF9zSDI2X3A4dGtOQUUzTVZqaHhZX05nODBZQjB3ZmxPS0NQSW9kLW9lRG9Mbkd1V0hyTTJCbEVtRm1HU0V0M3BFTFVZYlZQdGVHR0hUSkFaVEZwTXhqS2FOREtod1ktTkk3MGNtRTV3UnduMVBBYXNrMndVTWYwRklBM2ZMMVg3eTZt?oc=5", "source": "lane_statement_public", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:38:53+00:00", "text": "Bridgeport family construction company announces leadership transition - Hartford Business Journal\nBridgeport family construction company announces leadership transition Hartford Business Journal", "truncated": false}, {"id": "20dfd148d1648e8dbe48e994", "title": "Frisco King: Jackson-Starring Tulsa King Spinoff Gets Official Teaser - Bleeding Cool News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPR2hJWlJhUURwQ21MOGQxaU1XenZnTk5KODFPdGtJUXBpblFUWF9iYXRuS1U2aWJPazdmajZGMHBuWFpuNGg5cEp6SXpuNlZ2VmFsVm1kdGNWN2RvZGFNbXBONlFFTVhnWS1iS0xtdEJHdDhiQkNreUZrRWk5Mzl4VnF4TlNyQ3hIUUFoT0ZiOTNIeWl1VU5KMFZxQkpCUQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_spinoff", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:38:10+00:00", "text": "Frisco King: Jackson-Starring Tulsa King Spinoff Gets Official Teaser - Bleeding Cool News\nFrisco King: Jackson-Starring Tulsa King Spinoff Gets Official Teaser Bleeding Cool News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "bc5f52fd881b50f7b4703bbf", "title": "Economists: Hot PPI shows Fed's work is not done", "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/15/pce-ppi-september-fed-reserve-rate-hike.html", "source": "rss_cnbc_economy", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:37:59+00:00", "text": "Economists: Hot PPI shows Fed's work is not done\nPersonal consumption expenditures, the Federal Reserve's preferred inflation indicator, are poised to rise again later this month.\nA hotter-than-expected inflation reading Thursday will feed into PCE, and estimates now show core PCE inflation rising 0.32%, up from 0.25% in August.\n\"On the economic data alone, there is little reason for the Fed to hesitate,\" writes Mizuho's Alex Pelle\nA customer with a loaded shopping cart of groceries at a Walmart Supercenter retail store in North Bergen, New Jersey, U.S., Nov. 21, 2025.\nWall Street estimates for the Federal Reserve's preferred inflation indicator now expect an acceleration from the level that prompted the central bank to hike rates last month.\nhotter-than-expected producer price index\ncame in at 1.3% Thursday, the biggest monthly gain since March 2022 and more than double the 0.6% consensus.\nThat drove the year-over-year increase to 6.3%, the biggest jump since December 2022. The increase was paced by a 20% rise in gasoline prices. But taking out food, energy and trade services, prices still rose a healthy 0.5%, indicating that inflation was broader than just energy.\nSeven Wall Street estimates gathered by CNBC show core personal consumption expenditures inflation for September, which will be published later this month, is forecast to rise 0.32%, up from 0.25% in August. Wall Street economists use the\n, released Wednesday, and the PPI to estimate the PCE.\n\"We see real risks the Fed will deliver another rate hike in two weeks' time even as recent Fedspeak tempered expectations for back-to-back increases,'' wrote Kathy Bostjancic, chief economist at Nationwide.\nAnalysis: Why a $2 trillion deficit and 5% Treasury yields are becoming America’s biggest economic challenge\nEconomists: Hot PPI shows Fed’s work is not done\nHow high inflation became a ‘fact of life’ in the U.S.\nWholesale prices jumped 6.3% annually in September, biggest gain since 2022\nSeveral Fed officials have argued that the Fed does not need to hurry to hike rates, though they have suggested more rate hikes are needed. As a result, Fed futures on Thursday showed just a 29% probability of a hike at the Fed meeting at the end of this month, but a 91% probability of at least one hike by December.\nA 0.32% increase in PCE would boost the year-over-year core inflation rate to 3.1%, up from 3.01% in August. Estimates ranged from a high of 0.35% from Barclays to a low of 0.29% from Oxford Economics.\n\"The picture is not benign with inflation elevated and intensifying,\" wrote Alex Pelle, senior U.S. economist at Mizuho Securities. \"On the economic data alone, there is little reason for the Fed to hesitate to continue moving the policy rate higher.\"\nFed Chairman Kevin Warsh has suggested one litmus test for not hiking is confidence that inflation will return in a timely manner to the Fed's 2% target. Both headline and core PCE inflation have been above target since 2021. They have inched steadily higher since tariffs were introduced in April 2025. The gains have accelerated since the beginning of the Iran war.\nThe Fed prefers the PCE because, compared to the CPI, it believes it more closely resembles how Americans actually spend their money and changes its weightings when consumers change their spending patterns.\nChoose CNBC as your preferred source on Google and never miss a moment from the most trusted name in business news.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "a3629cfe5f6eed954b9d1ba0", "title": "Economists: Hot PPI shows Fed's work is not done - CNBC", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiggFBVV95cUxOb01IeGE0M04zdDFRdmFsVms0cWw5Nkx4RG9YTFdtSzNLNVc2TV9vUWZFdDhDQkNWcUJSWG5FT3NPWS1KRVpoZXp2cEhPcTdFYmFJSVVnRFBaa1plWmRJanR3YS1DYUhxNzRaSnhRcVZqYXRlc1dvTVBjM3l5RlRMNlZR0gGHAUFVX3lxTFBHU3JuM3lUd1N6Q29uclNoSTJQY09yUkpTZ0d6elZLX1dLWFNZYUlpclBTTm54cDBDZ3R", "source": "rss_google_business", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:37:59+00:00", "text": "Economists: Hot PPI shows Fed's work is not done - CNBC\nEconomists: Hot PPI shows Fed's work is not done CNBC US Producer Prices Up Most Since 2022 as Energy Pain Worsens Bloomberg.com Inflation worsened last month to 3.7% in sign that prices remain elevated as midterm elections near AP News A Perfect Economic Storm The American Prospect US producer prices post largest gain in 4-1/2 years; expensive gasoline boosts retail sales Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "0ec07d3d537b5259d4ae7e49", "title": "Software Bug Hits 2026 Toyota RAV4 PHEVs, Recalled Over Power Loss Risk A software initialization error in the motor-generator control unit affects nearly 39,000 plug-in hybrid RAV4s in Canada and the U.S. - Auto123", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxPU1ZqaGlHR0FxS1p3RVZVbjRvSGZjM3VNZzB3ZFM0Q0VVZS1HT1dlNGhMUHdVMUdKOUZzWUl3X2poT3kzQ3RqTFBCcEFUNDJBZjY0LS1BYkI5LWNLQlpfbW9nNEhBUFF4aXpPcmdZd0REZlpBSng1VWNqNVRTVm1XT1l0a2LSAYoBQVVfeXFMT2NpUDVuNXZiX05MVnkyNE9YcDV0UkYzR2RRdGlLaUJZVGk0ZERab1B0YXhyMmNrMWY", "source": "lane_product_harm", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:36:38+00:00", "text": "Software Bug Hits 2026 Toyota RAV4 PHEVs, Recalled Over Power Loss Risk A software initialization error in the motor-generator control unit affects nearly 39,000 plug-in hybrid RAV4s in Canada and the U.S. - Auto123\nSoftware Bug Hits 2026 Toyota RAV4 PHEVs, Recalled Over Power Loss Risk A software initialization error in the motor-generator control unit affects nearly 39,000 plug-in hybrid RAV4s in Canada and the U.S. Auto123", "truncated": false}, {"id": "69e9aebeb89214fb6f144948", "title": "New type of sunscreen hit shelves months after FDA approval - WSB-TV", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxQZk9lMGRZS0ZZbXFRbHFiYXh0X3l4M3M3MnhVZWw5MVBwTkNnNFdhZl9JN1VQZHpKX3NXWVk4V211T1NQR3dwRlFVU2d1cGxxSThhamlmNTU1bmZGMGVjSkZNY3pCNVBVblNRaDJNS1hIVHByS3piT0Y2MHlESml5RTA3QXlCbWhWaVF1ekZuZ3hDbm5kWDJIWWFCYnQzOF9weGZEalBBQXNJaXpwcXF6aHcyZzRJV0VJazY3btIB0AF", "source": "lane_gate", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:36:24+00:00", "text": "New type of sunscreen hit shelves months after FDA approval - WSB-TV\nNew type of sunscreen hit shelves months after FDA approval WSB-TV", "truncated": false}, {"id": "23090b6d14d48d294e6ce997", "title": "New type of sunscreen hit shelves months after FDA approval - KIRO 7 News Seattle", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles