kSFptNXlZN2oxX1ZuV1pOVVhFYzl4OFMwWTRNX0ZZY054XzBtOUhmdHc4OERtaWhPR2MycnoxWm5oRXM4VQ?oc=5", "source": "official_congress_search", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:26:19+00:00", "text": "Subjects - S.1748 - 119th Congress (2025-2026): Kids Online Safety Act - Congress.gov\nSubjects - S.1748 - 119th Congress (2025-2026): Kids Online Safety Act Congress.gov", "truncated": false}, {"id": "d64e80c26203100f74bb5fe5", "title": "At least 33 pupils and teacher killed after school roof collapses in Pakistan", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cked326llddgo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:26:16+00:00", "text": "At least 33 pupils and teacher killed after school roof collapses in Pakistan\nOn the ground in Pakistan as school roof collapse kills more than 30 children\nAt least 33 pupils and a teacher have been killed after a school roof collapsed in the north-western Pakistani city of Peshawar, according to hospital officials.\nMore than a dozen others are injured, with some in a critical condition.\nEmergency services were called to the private Al-Khair school in Dir Colony at 08:48 (03:48 GMT) on Thursday after lessons had begun, rescue official Bilal Faizi told the BBC.\nThe roof of an upper-floor classroom had collapsed, he said, causing ceilings below to cave in and trap children beneath the debris.\nAnnouncing the arrest of the school's owner, police chief Mian Saeed promised a thorough inquiry into \"whether there were any violations of building codes\".\nWarning: This article contains distressing details\nAn English teacher from a nearby school said he immediately rushed to the site with other local residents when they heard sirens and the sound of ambulances.\nTogether, they pulled more than 20 children from the rubble, he said.\n\"I personally pulled out six children with my own hands. Most of them were alive and talking. But later it was found that they had passed away.\"\n\"There was a lot of blood,\" he said. \"One child said he was in a lot of pain. His tongue had dried up in his mouth, [and he was] asking for water.\"\nSohail, another local resident, said he and others tried to remove children from under the rubble \"using shovels\".\nA rescue worker said an upper-floor roof collapsed, crashing through three classrooms\nThe school building had been constructed on a temporary basis, according to emergency official Arif Khattak.\nEarlier reports suggested the destroyed classrooms were in a two-storey part of the building, but Peshawar police chief Mian Saeed later confirmed that classrooms on three floors had been brought down.\nThere were about 30 pupils in the top class, 40 in the middle and 45 on the ground floor, he said.\nIt appears that when the roof of the top-floor classroom collapsed, the falling rubble crashed through classrooms below, bringing their ceilings down too.\nSaeed said the entire structure, which had \"substandard\" roof slabs, was \"overloaded\" and beyond the limit of how much weight it could bear.\nThe school is on a very narrow street, meaning it was difficult for rescue workers to reach the site and transport the injured to hospitals.\nPeshawar's Lady Reading Hospital reported the deaths of 32 children and a teacher while Naseerullah Khan Babar Memorial Hospital reported one child dead.\nThe police chief said the building was still \"extremely dangerous\" and urged people to move away.\nThe Governor of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Faisal Karim Kundi, has ordered a safety audit of all schools in the province to \"identify potential risks and ensure that immediate corrective measures are taken wherever necessary\".\n\"We cannot allow the safety of our children to be compromised,\" he said.\nFurious family members of deceased pupils accused the school of ignoring safety concerns. \"Make an example of them, a lesson for all,\" Mohammad Zaman, a man who lost two nephews in the disaster, told Reuters news agency.\nThe roof crashed through three classrooms and buried schoolchildren in debris, police say\nfourteen children died after the roof of a private tuition centre near Lahore\nAnd in August, 14 newborn babies were killed by a fire that ripped through a neonatal unit at a hospital in the capital, Islamabad, which an inquiry found\nPakistan has locked down Imran Khan's stronghold - but it could backfire\nNo fire alarms or sprinklers at Pakistan hospital ward where 14 babies died, report finds", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "ff10d86efdf414c3596e1c5d", "title": "Meta Platforms, Inc. (META) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo! Finance Canada", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUkFVX3lxTE9NdF9xWW1RaDk2MmNFdk5acnJHSVhGM0dqcF90M081cUplRkpyVjZmakJsdS11TFhOcnVVRnM0T1RXcEo5ZzBITzA1N1BsaWVacVE?oc=5", "source": "topic_business", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:26:09+00:00", "text": "Meta Platforms, Inc. (META) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo! Finance Canada\nMeta Platforms, Inc. (META) Stock Price, News, Quote & History Yahoo! Finance Canada", "truncated": false}, {"id": "bec3b45f3499e6e261d4dd8d", "title": "‘We give back’: Zelenskyy replies to Le Pen’s pledge to cut aid - POLITICO.eu", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxOWDh0TGpqcGNoRERDeFpDUWJIOUk0V01KTE5jRXotd2s5d3pMVmxvZVhaSFhxS0Z3SkROVHkzdmZTUXZWcFcxMExvcnU0eVJULU9UcjBpbkFMNGNmcmFLSnBhOXVuS3JqczNLMm9MQlRScUlVY28yWmh1Z0Yyam5ubl9paExxaVpHS1ZfUmREOTJ3WUpwMjg3TXhlVlYwWF8y?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:26:00+00:00", "text": "‘We give back’: Zelenskyy replies to Le Pen’s pledge to cut aid - POLITICO.eu\n‘We give back’: Zelenskyy replies to Le Pen’s pledge to cut aid POLITICO.eu France’s Marine Le Pen vows ‘trial of strength’ with EU Financial Times France 'can no longer finance' Ukraine, far-right presidential frontrunner Le Pen says France 24 Le Pen finds few allies in Brussels for her EU budget 'showdown' Le Monde.fr Le Pen ready to 'debate' Zelenskyy after v