xaXRia21tcGJRMUdHYVl3TERRWGs4VElPMHJkaGlxNG45V1RHRXdMc1NGeGVxOTNzSlRjWHNDTzc1cGtyZA?oc=5", "source": "lane_cat_weather", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:00+00:00", "text": "Statewide Earthquake Drill Set for Today - NBC Palm Springs\nStatewide Earthquake Drill Set for Today NBC Palm Springs", "truncated": false}, {"id": "a4d56d187e5a9c78f5a64f22", "title": "Making your Pixel devices last longer through design, repair, and reuse", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/devices/pixel/international-repair-day-2026/", "source": "company_google_blog", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:00+00:00", "text": "Making your Pixel devices last longer through design, repair, and reuse\nMaking your Pixel devices last longer through design, repair, and reuse\nThis International Repair Day, here’s a look at how we design for longevity — from the modular engineering of our Pixel smartwatch to our global network of walk-in repair centers.\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\nThis content is generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental\nWe are designing Pixel devices and Fitbit trackers with modular parts to make repairs easier and reduce waste. You can now manage your device health, troubleshoot issues, or start a repair directly through the My Pixel app and our updated support hubs. When you are ready for an upgrade, consider our expanded certified refurbished program or trade in your old device to keep it in circulation.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\n\"Making your Pixel devices last longer\" explains how Google is prioritizing repair and sustainability.\nNew Pixel watches and Fitbit trackers use modular designs to make repairs much easier.\nYou can use the My Pixel app to troubleshoot issues or start repairs quickly.\nGoogle’s expanded trade-in and refurbished programs help keep older devices out of landfills.\nThese efforts aim to reduce electronic waste by helping your tech last much longer.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nGoogle is designing its new watches and trackers to be much easier to fix instead of just throwing them away. They’ve made it simple to find repair guides, get expert help, or even chat with an AI to troubleshoot problems. If you're ready for an upgrade, you can trade in your old device or buy a refurbished one to keep tech out of landfills. It’s all about making your gadgets last longer so you don't have to replace them as often.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nOur devices should be built to last — and easy to repair when life happens. As we celebrate International Repair Day\nwe are reflecting on how circularity shapes everything we build. Extending the lifespan of hardware is one of the most meaningful ways to reduce e-waste and maximize the value of our technology.\nHere’s a closer look at how we are making repair and reuse more accessible, dependable, and impactful.\nDesigning devices for repairability: The Pixel Watch & Fitbit Edge\nSustainable hardware begins with thoughtful engineering. For the Pixel Watch 4 and 5, our design and engineering teams established an ambitious repairability roadmap and identified common repair bottlenecks from the earliest stages of development.\nThe result is an industry-leading modular architecture that rejects the industry standard of heavily glued, unserviceable components. And according to iFixit,\nit's the most repairable smartwatch out there\n, earning a 9 out of 10 repairability score.\nAnd this week we expanded our repairable products with the new\n, our first repairable fitness tracker, featuring an internal modular architecture and a replaceable battery designed to extend the life of your device.\nMaking it easy for you to access expert Pixel support\nGreat design must be backed by fast, reliable support when you need it. Here are all the ways Pixel customers can extend the life of their devices.\noffers eligible users peace of mind with protection against cracks, spills, drops, and more.\nis a hub to find solutions. Head there to run diagnostics, chat with an AI agent to troubleshoot an issue, or easily start a repair.\nthat feature multiple repair solutions and transparent price estimates, helping you find the best option for their needs.\n, so you can quickly verify your Pixel device details and start a hassle-free repair.\nThrough our global network of walk-in service centers and authorized providers, you can access quick, certified repairs with genuine parts.\nWhen it's time for an upgrade, our Google Store Trade-In Program makes it easy to exchange eligible devices for store credit, so older devices get safely refurbished or responsibly recycled.\nExpanding our certified pre-owned program\nThe Google Certified Refurbished program keeps high-performing hardware in circulation longer, without compromising on quality or performance.\nEvery phone in the program is restored with genuine Google parts, updated with the latest Android software, packaged in 100% plastic-free materials, and backed by our full one-year warranty. To make sustainable upgrades even more accessible, we’re expanding the program on two fronts: we added the Pixel 9 series to our U.S. lineup at up to 45% off on the\n., and we launched certified refurbished devices on the\nWe'll continue to invest in sustainability, product longevity, and repair to extend the lifespan of our products. And we invite you to join us in this journey: whether you are checking your device’s health via the\n, or opting for a Certified Refurbished device.\nGet the latest news from Google in your inbox\nSign up for our newsletters with product updates, event information, special offers, and more.\nCheck your inbox to confirm your subscription.\nYour information will be used in accordance with\nWe’re supporting nature restoration through sustainable farming in Brazil.\nWhy we're backing America's existing nuclear plants\nGoogle is supporting water resilience in Chile.\nOur new health and safety tools are live in the Google Health app.\nHelping bring the world’s first large-scale, near-zero emissions steel plant online\nWe’re catalyzing megaton-scale climate impact in Brazil", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "6ac085315dbeb1bc75da7ac9", "title": "'Frisco King' Confirmed: Samuel L. Jackson's Taylor Sheridan Spin-off Is Coming Sooner Than You Think - AOL.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTE54aWprYkRJb3FWZm8zM2d5N1pEWjJlZ2lsbUVuUWRTRzlOekNTTjgyZWNwNDRpRlpGWEZlOWVyV2R5aVJsRjFQWEFqT1huUDk3QTgxYzJ6Mkg3TmdfMmUxYVQ0c0VWZGM2c0dPYUtNZ0lrS0MxTHZheElRYUt0cU0?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_spinoff", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:00+00:00", "text": "'Frisco King' Confirmed: Samuel L. Jackson's Taylor Sheridan Spin-off Is Coming Sooner Than You Think - AOL.com\n'Frisco King' Confirmed: Samuel L. Jackson's Taylor Sheridan Spin-off Is Coming Sooner Than You Think AOL.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "4f371e36f3d8c2168ffe5c93", "title": "‘Frisco King’: Samuel L. Jackson Plays “Outside The Law” In Teaser For Taylor Sheridan’s ‘Tulsa King’ Spinoff As Paramount+ Sets Winter Release - Deadline", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxNRThJZlh0SUFZc3hXUUFpNEFORnRUMHRQSGtaM1R6anJvUGRkSk5lMHI5OXJZS01TSU4wc1JKZldONXhUMjBudE14ZGpyS0pBcVlBcUdRSTZrX2tGNnJMd2Q4am9oa1hZX21OZFZkU25vOV9YMlFHWGt3MTltVE1hTl9ibFZxY3FhZUdwUVlkOTM5NFFyX01OQnhTQWxkT0ph?oc=5", "source": "lane_corporate_action_spinoff", "published_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:00+00:00", "text": "‘Frisco King’: Samuel L. Jackson Plays “Outside The Law” In Teaser For Taylor Sheridan’s ‘Tulsa King’ Spinoff As Paramount+ Sets Winter Release - Deadline\n‘Frisco King’: Samuel L. Jackson Plays “Outside The Law” In Teaser For Taylor Sheridan’s ‘Tulsa King’ Spinoff As Paramount+ Sets Winter Release Deadline", "truncated": false}, {"id": "2add8516491790ff60aa7f23", "title": "Neanderthal remains may be earliest hu