Briefly Dips Below $80,000 as Volatility Roils Markets - Bloomberg.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxOcHJKRWxqVXpOTkdLaEtTdk5EZ3lnWklNbXBPaEhvbkxoVUlKRE8wTjBkMGVfTFVqRzl1QXZ3NGczbDhKMGl3UWZHTVFkczVZdjE0YXJrRFVjbXcxSTFIVXpXQ0FQQXJ3QzhJODhSRkNQWjBoU3hMM09DYjZaQ3MwRWlIa3NwSWhvR0VvNTlBdkVaMU1fVWlwak1sd0ljWExWTnRBajVnMFV6ZUlUNFBlWG9n?oc=5", "source": "publisher_bloomberg", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:59:27+00:00", "text": "Bitcoin Briefly Dips Below $80,000 as Volatility Roils Markets - Bloomberg.com\nBitcoin Briefly Dips Below $80,000 as Volatility Roils Markets Bloomberg.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "7a31ad4488b86587b6d73793", "title": "Iambic Therapeutics stock rises 16% in Nasdaq debut after IPO - Quartz", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMibEFVX3lxTE9RWmtidG9zRzVGb1paVlc1V0MwbjJ3YWVBWmZuQlJDQ21YS1NMNC1zWE5hYUh2TkFBbmZUa19Db201LVdLRFhQQ0dwbThrbU1kRU9hVHY3LTB4VGZQY2tmcUNLNVNRdHllMUFWbw?oc=5", "source": "lane_listing_flow", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:58:34+00:00", "text": "Iambic Therapeutics stock rises 16% in Nasdaq debut after IPO - Quartz\nIambic Therapeutics stock rises 16% in Nasdaq debut after IPO Quartz", "truncated": false}, {"id": "cbe930df625285bbd7712230", "title": "Tron Files $200M ATM to Buy More TRX, and Dilution Is the Catch - Altcoin Buzz", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikgFBVV95cUxOOEdfUFRCNHcxME9RN2pVYktjbHJTNy1QSXM0Skc2Q3hMY3YzeHBqa1BLWWpRN3NuUkkzQ2NvLUpGQ3Y0enpvNWhGa1BUM1NVcHVNcnJYS2FIdXRSYWQtSFlybThmNU5iMmRsX21fZFVyMWoxS3JxczB3MWlJVDRmOW5tcUFBaXo3c1ptSl9UbGN1QQ?oc=5", "source": "lane_dilution", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:57:15+00:00", "text": "Tron Files $200M ATM to Buy More TRX, and Dilution Is the Catch - Altcoin Buzz\nTron Files $200M ATM to Buy More TRX, and Dilution Is the Catch Altcoin Buzz", "truncated": false}, {"id": "0f2f8113063864ac51405d9c", "title": "Association seeks exclusive Additional Advocate-General for SC/ST cases - The Hindu", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi2gFBVV95cUxOTGh2NFNQX1cza2pPVWlpRVVhU3hjWkRqMTVxT2dwQ2VOUlJIbno2b092S0dsTHNFLUVxd0Y1ZEk2Tmt0bTRfMk9QTGZPMHNaMjg4c19US25SOXB5WnZLNFdtMmNHbFd5c3RPMVU0TFpDQ2JkazRIWGVESlphTklwWXpsZ0g1MmpfNzBGNEZPcm5JQkZvMGpiTzlIYmk0Z1hUUEpHeTBiZjZuRnpob25VNW1yblg4b3FuWkhaU1FmVkR", "source": "lane_blast_legal", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:55:33+00:00", "text": "Association seeks exclusive Additional Advocate-General for SC/ST cases - The Hindu\nAssociation seeks exclusive Additional Advocate-General for SC/ST cases The Hindu", "truncated": false}, {"id": "c980ad7620ac6f402ad1803f", "title": "Nandy 'minded to intervene' in Sky's £1.6bn takeover of ITV entertainment arm", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm79pe5yej7no?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_business", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:55:21+00:00", "text": "Nandy 'minded to intervene' in Sky's £1.6bn takeover of ITV entertainment arm\nCulture Secretary Lisa Nandy has said she is \"minded to intervene\" in the proposed Â£1.6bn deal for Sky to buy ITV's media and entertainment division.\nNandy said there were reasonable grounds to believe the deal could affect free expression in the media and the variety of Britain's news landscape.\nSky said it would \"carefully consider\" a letter from the culture secretary and \"engage constructively\" with the review into the deal.\n\"We remain confident that bringing Sky and ITV's media and entertainment business together will create a stronger British media,\" it said.\nITV welcomed the letter and said the deal would help it \"compete with global streaming platforms, benefiting viewers, advertisers and the UK creative industries\".\nthat Sky had agreed to buy ITV's broadcasting business, including its free-to-air TV channels and the ITV X streaming service.\nThe deal does not include ITV's production arm, ITV Studios, which makes popular programmes such as Love Island and I'm a Celebrity... Get Me Out of Here.\nIt would give Sky access to millions more viewers, while bosses hope it would help both compete with streaming giants such as Netflix.\nWhat Sky buying ITV could mean for your favourite shows\nBut Nandy has told Sky and ITV that she is considering issuing a public interest intervention notice (PIIN) to the Competition and Markets Authority (CMA) and regulator Ofcom, forcing an investigation into the tie-up.\nIn a letter to both companies, she said she was minded to order the probe to address public interest considerations including:\nThe need for free expression of opinion in news media\nThe need for a range of views in news media across the UK\nThe need for a range of people controlling the media across the UK\nThe need for a wide range of programmes to be offered across the UK\nThe letter said Nandy recognised Sky News and ITV News were two of the most prominent sources of television news in the UK, with a joint 26% share of those viewing news on linear TV.\nConsumers would still have access to other sources of news such as the BBC and Channel 4, it added.\nBut Nandy believes that, over time, the tie-up could undermine the range of views available to viewers, with 86% of the linear TV news market controlled by the BBC and Sky/ITV.\nThe North of England could be particularly hard hit as well as nations of the UK other than England and those from lower socio-economic backgrounds, the letter argued.\nThis is because their main source of news is broadcast news, it added.\nSky and ITV have been given until 20 October to respond to the culture secretary's concerns.\nto protect ITV's identity, its free-to-air services and public service broadcasting obligations, and to ensure ITV News and Sky News remain distinct editorial voices.\"\nAn ITV spokesperson said: \"We welcome the publication of the secretary of state's 'minded to' issue a public interest intervention notice letter as was expected and look forward to fully co-operating in the process.\n\"This is another important milestone in the regulatory review process towards creating a UK player with the scale and resources to better compete with global streaming platforms, benefiting viewers, advertisers and the UK creative industries.\"\nNandy's intervention would be made under a new public interest consideration.\nThis would need legislation to be brought forward, given that current laws do not cover the effect of a merger on streaming or on-demand programmes.\nShe said: \"If I decide to intervene on the basis of this new public interest consideration, I will bring forward legislation... to extend the application of the public interest consideration relating to the availability of a wide range of broadcasting to on-demand programmes.\"\nDepartment for Digital, Culture, Media & Sport", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "41d5f35df5286a1c28e82a48", "title": "FOMC Polymarket Betting Odds: Fed Hold Chance Slips to 73% - 99Bitcoins", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxQcktBS3pWRXVRaVhIbjItS3ZVXzRZTFB2WmxuTUJITmJuT2JPTXBUMzR4a0VYcjJaU1BtSGMzeHFxQWJmcmNFYllqUEk4dHNRbW5nVGVfTnN1MVVhVDRsdkc0VnYzamlKZ096eUZXbW0xTVZ1SkdQdEU4MEFRbGZzT0FGamsteTAxYXc?oc=5", "source": "lane_factor_impulse", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:55:01+00:00", "text": "FOMC Polymarket Betting Odds: Fed Hold Chance Slips to 73% - 99Bitcoins\nFOMC Polymarket Betting Odds: Fed Hold Chance Slips to 73% 99Bitcoins", "truncated": false}, {"id": "97680ac93cb62d852222a24e", "title": "Lexington Hospital Data Breach Affects 67,000 - Claim Depot", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE9uTTRDa1JjeFFUeGVtSllla1RrY2VKQmt2d1RGbGRzTlYxSTVPQUROdHFTZFM1OXRVcFVmd3NHOE5lanZ6em8yMi16RUxIX0FabkFoUExGeXp5NUlOX3d6ODJ3TV9rR0VIRWY0OUNTcF9XYXk2MnQ4?oc=5", "source": "lane_blast_cyber", "published_at": "2026-10-15T14:54:20+00:00", "text": "Lexington Hospital Data Breach Affects 67,000 - Claim Depot\nLexington Hospital Data Breach Affects 67,000 Claim Depot", "truncated": false}, {"id": "65f09316d23ba61326566626",