NM3kydlBLeGNwNkozMWItT0QzRjEtYnAxRVhzMnB1Uk91emhadmJtMENYNEpndnE5c0pIWjhHc2J0WG1laEJNdW1yVTRZc2xxVnRBT3h6VG5HSHluSmd2VXpwQS1jVjdUUlREOUJnSE40UUVhQWVYSjNCNTFkSTFLX1QyN2NHV1V6WVE?oc=5", "source": "rss_ap_topnews:google_fallback", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "Brazil investigates Amazon wildfires that disrupt daily life and have fueled political attacks - AP News\nBrazil investigates Amazon wildfires that disrupt daily life and have fueled political attacks AP News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "dcaabf5e08f6a89425c24830", "title": "An intelligent new shopping cart", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/shopping/universal-cart-launch/", "source": "company_google_blog", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "An intelligent new shopping cart\nUniversal Cart launches in the U.S. today. Here are four ways it can help with holiday shopping — including organizing products from multiple stores into a single cart, tracking price drops, and more.\nSenior Director, Product Management, Consumer Shopping\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\nThis content is generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental\nGoogle’s new Universal Cart is now available in the U.S. across Search and the Gemini app to help you organize your holiday shopping. This tool saves items from multiple retailers in one place, tracks price drops, identifies relevant promo codes, and suggests the best payment methods. You can complete purchases securely through Google Pay or transfer items directly to the merchant’s site to finish your order.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nGoogle’s \"An intelligent new shopping cart\" helps you organize and track items across retailers.\nSave products from different stores in one place instead of using messy browser tabs.\nGet helpful alerts about price drops or when out-of-stock items become available again.\nThe cart suggests the best payment methods and finds promo codes to save money.\nCheck out securely using Google Pay or finish your purchase directly on merchant sites.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nGoogle’s new Universal Cart keeps all your items from different stores in one place so you don't lose track of them. It uses AI to alert you about price drops and helps you find the best ways to save money. You can even pay for everything quickly and securely right through the app. It’s basically a smarter way to shop without having to jump between a bunch of different websites.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nAs we build for the future of commerce, our focus spans two fronts: unlocking agentic capabilities that act on your behalf, and designing practical tools that give shoppers confidence and control. Google’s Universal Cart is built for that second track — mirroring how people actually shop today across Google, without losing track of their items, their savings, or the merchants they trust.\n, which we previewed earlier this year, is an intelligent shopping cart and your new hub for shopping on Google. The cart puts you in control, helping to organize your shopping, keep track of items you love from across retailers, stay on top of promos, and enjoy effortless checkout powered by the Universal Commerce Protocol (UCP). Today, Universal Cart is rolling out in the U.S. across Google Search and in the Gemini app.\nHere are four things the new Universal Cart lets you do to stay organized and shop more confidently this holiday season.\n1. Save products from multiple retailers, wherever you’re shopping on Google.\nUniversal Cart offers a more organized alternative to tabs and screenshots. The cart saves your progress across Google so you never have to start your shopping from scratch. Let’s say you save a handbag from Steve Madden to your cart in\n, and later a sweater from Quince and lipgloss from Ulta Beauty in the Gemini app. Those products will be there in your cart when you come back later so you can pick up right where you left off.\n2. Keep tabs on pricing or inventory changes for your entire list.\nThe cart is built on the 60+ billion continually refreshed product listings in Google’s Shopping Graph. This allows it to proactively work for you in the background, sending notifications about price drops or when an item comes back in stock.\n3. Identify hidden savings or points from your cart.\nThe cart’s intelligent reasoning can help anticipate your needs. Say you have a couple different credit cards, but don’t know each one’s specific benefits. The Universal Cart is built on Google Wallet so it understands your card perks and can intelligently help you choose between payment methods. It’ll also show you relevant promo codes right from the cart.\n4. Make seamless, trusted purchases when you’re ready to buy.\nIn online shopping, trust is everything. You can securely check out with Google Pay in just a few taps with many of your favorite stores right in the cart, or you can transfer your items directly to the merchant’s cart to finish buying on their site. Try these simplified checkout experiences with merchants like Nike, Sephora, Target, Ulta Beauty, Walmart, Wayfair, and many Shopify merchants. Either way, you will receive direct confirmations and customer support from the merchant, and they will remain the seller of record.\nAs the holiday season kicks into high gear, the Universal Cart is just one way we’re giving shoppers the convenience and smarts they need to make the best shopping choices.\nGet the latest news from Google in your inbox\nSign up for our newsletters with product updates, event information, special offers, and more.\nCheck your inbox to confirm your subscription.\nYour information will be used in accordance with\nSee the top style searches from people in big fashion capitals.\n400 publications are now partnering with us on our News AI pilot program.\nMore ways to connect with the web from Search\nData-backed secrets to smarter holiday shopping\n6 ways to trick-or-treat yourself to the ultimate Halloween with Search\nCheck out this year’s buzziest Halloween trends.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "a60f4a701f887ae8f46b94e0", "title": "Teaching students to think and learn through questions", "url": "https://openai.com/index/teaching-students-to-think-and-learn-through-questions", "source": "company_openai_blog", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "Teaching students to think and learn through questions\nOctober 15, 2026 Company Teaching students to think and learn through questions Loading… Share On Teachers’ Day, we celebrate those who help us learn. A good question can change the course of a lesson. It can bring an unspoken question to light, open up another way to solve a problem, or help someone recognize what they already know. Teachers do this work every day: they know their students, choose how to introduce an idea, and guide them from their first attempt to understanding. Set in a university classroom, the campaign takes a humorous look at the changing relationship between teachers and students and celebrates the role of educators in a world with AI. AI for Educators now available in Portuguese Today, we are launching the AI for Educators ⁠ (opens in a new window) course in Brazilian Portuguese on OpenAI Academy, OpenAI’s free learning platform. Designed for educators in primary, secondary, and higher education, the course shows how to use AI to plan lessons, create activities and assessments, and prepare communications while preserving educators’ pedagogical judgment. Learning through active participation, step by step Study Mode helps you explore a subject ⁠ (opens in a new window) step by step, with questions, hints, explanations, and checks for understanding. Developed in collaboration with teachers, scientists, and experts in pedagogy, the feature aims to encourage active participation and reflection on one’s own reasoning. To turn on Study Mode , select Study from the tools menu in ChatGPT. A student reviewing biology, for example, might ask: “I’m studying enzymes. Ask me one question at a time, wait for my answer, and help me identify what I need to review.” Teachers can also try Study Mode with subjects they know well, looking at whether the questions encourage reasoning and whether the explanations are appropriate for their class. In a science lesson on evaporation, for example, a teacher might ask students to investigate why clothes dry on a clothesline. After exploring the topic with Study Mode, each student writes their own explanation and a question to discuss in class, without referring back to the conversation. The teacher can use these responses to identify what needs to be revisited with the class. This Teachers’ Day, we invite you to experiment: explore the AI for Educators course, try Study Mode, and discover how these tools can be useful in different teaching contexts. Technology can open up new ways to learn, but it is teachers who know their students, ask the most important questions, and help turn curiosity into knowledge. 2026 ChatGPT Education Author OpenAI Keep reading View all Atlassian and OpenAI expand their partnership Company Oct 6, 2026 How Albertsons Companies is reimagining retail from the inside out Company Oct 1, 2026 DevDay 2026 Recap Company Sep 29, 2026", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8e9c1f946780bb19eddf57e7", "title": "Sabre announces upcoming webcast of its third quarter 2026 earnings conference call - TradingView", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi3AFBVV95cUxQZkVqSVV1cWdQaW81a2FLcEItTXYwcDJyTHJRc1p0cnl4OVVIQVB2aHhweFRJUmEzLTNzd3dLazFad05PSWJJVURNY0xRcE9VeWdaTmhfZkd5amxxSDl1WVg3SjdXNE1xVGhmN2EtSHVwY3daM0VlTnkzMU5VYlVyeFJya2NWbUhkWk52LUVNUjJ0SmJYUkNzeWM2RkNfcW1RQ3BjVXkzZTlUaDhBS2xndmdRa1BoVi0wdjZxOEpnTWN", "source": "issuer_ir_search", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "Sabre announces upcoming webcast of its third quarter 2026 earnings conference call - TradingView\nSabre announces upcoming webcast of its third quarter 2026 earnings conference call TradingView", "truncated": false}, {"id": "7d0ed3cb5cb4581ac2aae88c", "title": "TIME has named Google SynthID one of the Best Inventions of 2026.", "url": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/synthid-time-best-inventions/", "source": "company_google_blog", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "TIME has named Google SynthID one of the Best Inventions of 2026.\nTIME has named Google SynthID one of the Best Inventions of 2026.\nTIME has named Google SynthID to its annual list of\nAs generative AI makes digital media more realistic, knowing how content was made helps you navigate the web with confidence.\nGoogle SynthID embeds an invisible, durable digital watermark into AI-generated images, audio, video, and text at the moment of creation, without altering the quality. To date, SynthID has watermarked more than 180 billion images and videos and 240,000 years of audio. We also recently announced\n, bringing SynthID’s watermarking technology to synthetic biology.\nTo help people identify AI content, verification tools are built directly into Google Search, the Gemini app, and Chrome. You can also use the\nto check content from Google and our partners.\nTogether, these tools help give you more transparency and context around the content you encounter online. You can read more about this and other inventions on\nWe’re powering European scientific discovery with advanced AI compute and frontier models.\nApplying technology to understand and treat disease\nWe're making it easier to identify AI-generated content globally.\nEmbeddingGemma 2: an open, lightweight multimodal embedding model", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "67ffc0a982f5d23d65bf5b92", "title": "Data-backed secrets to smarter holiday shopping", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/shopping/holiday-shopping-when-to-buy-guide/", "source": "company_google_blog", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "Data-backed secrets to smarter holiday shopping\nData-backed secrets to smarter holiday shopping\nOur new When to Buy Guide uses Google Search and discount data to show when holiday deals peak. Learn the best times to buy fragrances, handbags, luggage, tech toys, and more so you can shop smarter this season.\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\nThis content is generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental\nUse our new \"When to Buy Guide\" to time your holiday purchases based on historical discount data. Buy fragrances early, but wait until late December for the best deals on suitcases and tech toys. Check the full guide for more tips to help you save money and avoid last-minute stress.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\n\"Data-backed secrets to smarter holiday shopping\" offers a roadmap for finding the best deals.\nBuy fragrances shortly after Black Friday to get the best prices and selection.\nSkip the Black Friday handbag rush and wait until mid-December for better deals.\nPurchase travel accessories early, but wait until late December for cheap suitcases.\nHold off on buying electronic toys until the final weeks of December for savings.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nGoogle used AI to analyze shopping trends so you can find the best holiday deals. They suggest buying perfumes early, but waiting until late December for big suitcases and tech toys. You should skip the Black Friday rush for handbags and aim for mid-December instead. These tips help you save money, but remember that prices can always change.\nSummaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nFinding the perfect holiday gift shouldn't feel like a guessing game. To take the stress out of your shopping, we analyzed historical promotional patterns, Search trends, and discount data across U.S. merchants on Google. The result is our\n, a research-backed roadmap showing when holiday discounts may hit their peak, based on data from last year.\nHere are a few tips and findings to help you shop smarter. For the full list of pricing trends and insights into our last-minute gifting habits, read the complete\n. You'll also discover which parent we shop for later, and which state claims the most last-minute shoppers.\nIf you're eyeing a perfume or cologne for someone on your list, shop early. Fragrance discounts don’t typically increase as Christmas approaches, and the volume of fragrance deals drops off sharply, so waiting until late December may not offer lower prices — and could leave you with fewer options. Strategize by buying fragrances within the first two weeks after Black Friday weekend for the best deals and inventory selection.\nReconsider the Black Friday handbag frenzy:\nIf you’re on the lookout for the perfect handbag at the best price, consider holding off on buying during Black Friday weekend. Target mid-December to balance a high discount with a decent selection of styles, or wait until late December if you just want the lowest price on remaining inventory.\nShop early for travel accessories, but later for suitcases:\nWhile travel accessories see their best deals in November, major items, such as large luggage and suitcases, don't typically hit their deepest markdowns until clearance sales in late December. With this in mind, consider buying travel accessories and packing cubes on Black Friday, but wait until late December for deep clearance discounts on large suitcases, though there may be less selection.\nUnlike traditional electronics, categories like motorized tech toys show some of their steepest markdowns emerging in the final weeks of December. If electronic toys are on your kids’ wish lists, consider holding out until the final shopping stretch to unlock surprise last-minute savings. If you wait to buy, keep an eye on holiday shipping deadlines, unless you plan on shopping in-store.\nThese trends should help you shop smarter this holiday season, but pricing and inventory can vary from year to year, so think of them as general guidance rather than absolute guarantees.\nGet the latest news from Google in your inbox\nSign up for our newsletters with product updates, event information, special offers, and more.\nCheck your inbox to confirm your subscription.\nYour information will be used in accordance with\nBoost your holiday sales with these agentic commerce updates\n3 ways to prep for your next big race with Search\nBeach vibes and temporary wallpaper are trending for back-to-school season.\nCollege students are eager to turn their dull dorm rooms into cozy spaces. Here are the Google Search trends we’re seeing.\n6 back-to-school shopping tricks every student should know\nThe latest AI news we announced in May 2026", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "19510e34840ffd896d665880", "title": "Intuit to Acquire AI-Native Revenue Management Platform Sequence - Business Wire", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxQMHEyOTBoWDNNRzJXdm9UaHFGaThUUUhqaVBJcVdXVFBsRkxvOEkySFo2TlZaeTV0djk1S3VtVm9WRXpHM3duWFFiMmlfUWhMZEV0VmJZR2lSbEpyUktteW03cjd3d3RWQ05sMC1YM21VNUc4LVJiNWxSaE9lRmJZYkI5UEFwTGxVVWtCT0U5Y3U2MkxEOXo5V3lMMWNCcTJOdUhGaUZiWDlVMEVraXlHcHhJQ09xWURMS1U4LUtB?oc", "source": "lane_corporate_action_mna", "published_at": "2026-10-15T13:00:00+00:00", "text": "Intuit to Acquire AI-Native Revenue Management Platform Sequence - Business Wire\nIntuit to Acquire AI-Native Revenue Management Platform Sequence Business Wire", "truncated": false}, {"id": "08c0693a13d4a363cb018554", "title": "\"It's just wrong in every sense.\" Rooney criticizes Cristiano Ronaldo walkout from Portugal camp (with video) - Plataforma Media", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxOOUswdDV1UG44cEpJOTBLTTdmSC14MkxNWEFCelh1MVU1RDE