older Proposes A-share Buyback - TradingView\nBiwin Storage Technology's Controlling Shareholder Proposes A-share Buyback TradingView", "truncated": false}, {"id": "620696fd2454a3db70c106b1", "title": "Symrise to Expand Fragrance Ingredient Production Capacity in India - www.marketscreener.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxQdGxoMW9SWWw3UDctbU02T21pc0QtdG14SmpZbnhoMXBRLTVzcHZybDFPakJad3NfOUdkYmxLcG5uWXBFdWRCcWFtWTBqMnhzUi0zTnNrUjZSdkNacDZNeG9rVllYUmFZZnhyMDVhRURZbnJDWGprWUxGbVJGTDZ1S2pnLUZjWDM5dHA4elczSXhFUDJTSnNrZlVHam5Md1JyWktSblM1Vk8tTTZvQ1doRFU4ZVFOMmhKUFpTcA?oc=5", "source": "lane_capacity", "published_at": "2026-10-15T10:54:00+00:00", "text": "Symrise to Expand Fragrance Ingredient Production Capacity in India - www.marketscreener.com\nSymrise to Expand Fragrance Ingredient Production Capacity in India www.marketscreener.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "75ab551af655e3bccb615250", "title": "China's ByteDance sets up AI safety team, launches global hiring drive - Reuters", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixgFBVV95cUxNUUh6d0NyZGxfYjd4bDhwRWdkT0wxOG4xUUlrQkZFZ0JMTlNJMzVUVWRHNDhyYWR2Vzh0RGRsUk9YdDhHeE92NlBPTWlnU1htMHotSVhfRGoydXVjM21UcEV6Z3dsSGtSSGhOcExMaFBud3ZVcGJDU1NNUXFUcFBCdDNwZUFfWVY4QnJjNEhaWHQ2Z01PUUt4enJJVWRxWjA5aTNVUncwSW1XcFB5c2VzYXBmR3RNZVZxNHpzd1c1bHh", "source": "topic_products", "published_at": "2026-10-15T10:52:58+00:00", "text": "China's ByteDance sets up AI safety team, launches global hiring drive - Reuters\nChina's ByteDance sets up AI safety team, launches global hiring drive Reuters", "truncated": false}, {"id": "fcc880c3653b0736df576a60", "title": "Yash Optics & Lens Reports Incident Involving Cyber-Attack On It Infrastructure - TradingView", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi4AFBVV95cUxOdDFoV05sbWtvY1F4bXExdTNaQWVDTEM4S1F2VGNKMzdwaG9RRGtaSjlNbDVTMUdyNkk2NlQyWUM1eFFiX3YyRmU1QzJhZmNFbm9oSE9zOVJjR1NXZWxNek9YeFFocWhJUzU1Um5KVUZRVnpuLW1FcmU0Wmpxc0RyWHFaaUp0eVFvT1J6QmxDZXM4Y2Zqa1l6T1hzVnF1bzc4N003dFNwcjhSbFBhNGNCZWNNMWFHZXN3NjM5c2N1MTZ", "source": "lane_blast_cyber", "published_at": "2026-10-15T10:51:58+00:00", "text": "Yash Optics & Lens Reports Incident Involving Cyber-Attack On It Infrastructure - TradingView\nYash Optics & Lens Reports Incident Involving Cyber-Attack On It Infrastructure TradingView", "truncated": false}, {"id": "966226156b3f1acacaeca92c", "title": "Obama says drift towards extremism 'not inevitable'", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crwyd7vq3xw1o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T10:51:53+00:00", "text": "Obama says drift towards extremism 'not inevitable'\nBarack Obama warned that online platforms were stoking anger and fear in people\nBarack Obama has told an audience in Glasgow that hope is worth fighting for despite big challenges facing the modern world.\nThe 44th president of the United States said online platforms had shifted in recent years to focus on content that stoked anger and fear, but he believes a drift to extremism is \"not inevitable\".\nof 12,150 people while in conversation with British journalist and author Sathnam Sanghera, part of three speaking dates in the UK.\nHe reflected on his time in the White House and examined the political and social challenges facing the US and the wider world.\nMore stories from Glasgow & West Scotland\nObama said that during his presidential campaign in 2008, when social media and technology was gaining traction, he had seen them as a beacon for hope\nBut he said the same positive forces and tools that could mobilise people around democracy or human rights could also be used by hate groups.\nHe said they \"connected people for good, but also for ill\".\n\"It turns out that the reptilian side of our brain really gets attracted to anger, fear, resentment and the sense that someone is out to get you,\" he said.\n\"So a lot of social media and a lot of our information is informed around that.\"\nBut the former president, who has already spoken in Belfast and will appear in Manchester on Thursday night, said that a drift towards extremism was \"not inevitable\".\nHe added: \"After World War Two, at least in the United States and certainly in Europe as well, the federal government said 'we're going to set up some rules because we've seen what propaganda can do in the hands of somebody like Hitler.\n\"We can see how big lies and misinformation can distort and enrage and incite violence. So we're going to hold these folks responsible'.\"\nThe former President was speaking at the OVO Hydro\nObama, who was president until 2016, said there was a \"critical balance\" that must be struck between free speech and regulation.\nBut the 65-year-old said that the world and its leaders are going to need to find mechanisms and new institutions to allow rigorous debate and disagreement while helping people sort out basic facts.\nHe said: \"If I had a blame pie for why politics is so polarised and why we're seeing a rise of populism in many places, it's because of that information that is going into our brains every day.\"\nObama said this resulted in young people feeling discouraged, and that \"it's not a healthy diet that our brains are on at the moment\".\nHe added that he feared this could become even worse with AI making it hard to distinguish between what is true and what is not, something he believes will make democracy hard to function.\nObama says people forget lessons from the past\nSpeaking about hope, Obama was asked if he still believed in a Martin Luther King Jr phrase he quoted years ago, about the arm of the moral universe being long, but ultimately bending towards justice.\nThe former president said that he still stands by the quote and argued that hope is an active \"almost theological\" choice people must make.\nHe said: \"It is a decision about how do we face and embrace this finite amount of time we have on the planet.\"\nHe told the audience he believes it is healthier for people to believe that change is possible.\n\"I think when we act on that basis, it doesn't always work out, but over time things do get better,\" he said.\nObama also said there seems to be a cycle in humanity where people forget lessons learned from the past and start to take things for granted.\n\"We start thinking 'maybe using language in public from our politicians that fosters hatred and scapegoats certain people â immigrants, Jews, or blacks or gays â that's just talk, it's humour'.\"\nHe said people forget where that can lead to, with them becoming less tolerant.\nObama told the audience that the world is going to be dealing with \"big challenges\", but he said he thinks \"we can be better\" and that making the world better remains worth fighting for.\nFormer US President Barack Obama to appear in Glasgow on UK tour\nObama receives honorary degree from Queen's University Belfast\nBarack Obama to attend COP26 summit in Glasgow", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "27a4efc404630ad3e681c5ad", "title": "With about $250M in cash at June 30, Yiren Digital (YRD) reaffirms its buyback plan. - Stock Titan", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxNNUxVb04xcVgwVTF1aGszaWRZVTJIQW9WMGFxVUhmNGpkZFBSLW80eldiak9Oa3RLT3dvVG1MbHlyLWxyOEJBekhyUS1KY2ZiZDJNWVZMSmdNemphUTZCcTZ1NDI4djZ5eXBSSjlucVYyREZUcXJJQ1hCTlUxWFZoNnNoVnZQMGNHbHA5TVZnY1gtdGg4Vll5eWkwNFM4S1BpaXowaUFNSFh0QmF3Zmttdmhn?oc=5", "source": "lane_capital_return", "published_at": "2026-10-15T10:51:29+00:00", "text": "With about $250M in cash at June 30, Yiren Digital (YRD) reaffirms its buyback plan. - Stock Titan\nWith about $250M in cash at June 30, Yiren Digital (YRD) reaffirms its buyback plan. Stock Titan", "truncated": false}, {"id": "978255db618c151b2594b6ef", "title": "Hezbollah claims confiscated explosives and denies assassination plans - AP News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxOdWk3SGZncVJjWFdxUWdjNGNOTUFpdzE1aGNlWGx1MWNwLXB2Yzh3eDlWVC1FdlZ4