nes, and the wider air transport industry - SITA\nSITA agrees to acquire Collins Aerospace Airport Solutions, reinforcing its commitment to innovation and the future of airports, airlines, and the wider air transport industry SITA", "truncated": false}, {"id": "6c4346606d3a9b26db03afb2", "title": "Is the semiconductor industry headed for an almighty crash? - The Economist", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxONG13VFVpMmRfamdQcy15WkdqVjVtOXNkZE0tbENrdHV2Vlk0QTNtXzlLR0NUcFdicXZEYlF6azZFRWZGLVRUcTgwTmwwbnBjVzhlaHh1X3RGSFB4dGtmVHNSY09ENVA2Vm9uOXhaajNodUtKOG1ibll1dXlORU10RWJ3YVViRG1qQTBhZTVqanc0VFItRThoY0IwdWpKX29RalFLTVY4aw?oc=5", "source": "topic_technology", "published_at": "2026-10-15T09:04:50+00:00", "text": "Is the semiconductor industry headed for an almighty crash? - The Economist\nIs the semiconductor industry headed for an almighty crash? The Economist", "truncated": false}, {"id": "cb7c94b8ec52b60d88b06abf", "title": "Inside the Plague Research Labs at the Heart of a Russian Mystery - The New York Times", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxQRDRVMmNodXNoa3JHQmh2b3lsMVIzSWQzSDJFOHNaYTFGRm01RW11Y3dVLXFBM3ZFNHZXSS13OXBkVXh0UndYNWk4b2hxdE00UXAtdEF4VTJEdnpWUWQ3SnR4N1VsV2ZQZFk5NFdsanhmODFOSjJZNjlQb0tydlJ1MElFcmZRQ2s?oc=5", "source": "rss_google_world", "published_at": "2026-10-15T09:04:13+00:00", "text": "Inside the Plague Research Labs at the Heart of a Russian Mystery - The New York Times\nInside the Plague Research Labs at the Heart of a Russian Mystery The New York Times Does a Russian lab worker's death carry pandemic risk? Experts say it's unlikely, with one caveat PBS Taiwan to monitor online rumors pneumonic plague outbreak spreading from Russia into China Anadolu Ajansı Russia’s frozen hinterlands have long been feared to harbor disease risks The Washington Post What the Russian plague scare taught the world Axios", "truncated": false}, {"id": "ff13d47e6df2ea37fec47b12", "title": "[Roundtop Machinery Industries FY2026 Q2 Earnings Call] Q2 After-Tax Profit Turns Negative on FX Losses; First Half Remains Profitable — Five-Axis Machine Export Controls Pose Biggest Headwind - finance.biggo.com", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiYkFVX3lxTE1idjRza3hMVl9NTnFxRHpNSEx2SUhDel81MVc0RlpLQ2kweU80QkE0bWEzblc1dGdaUkJXUmNiWlZxTm92ZnpKYVNIXzVnTkRKZHg0Z3VWb2FDU3oxc1dobnp3?oc=5", "source": "lane_access_control", "published_at": "2026-10-15T09:04:00+00:00", "text": "[Roundtop Machinery Industries FY2026 Q2 Earnings Call] Q2 After-Tax Profit Turns Negative on FX Losses; First Half Remains Profitable — Five-Axis Machine Export Controls Pose Biggest Headwind - finance.biggo.com\n[Roundtop Machinery Industries FY2026 Q2 Earnings Call] Q2 After-Tax Profit Turns Negative on FX Losses; First Half Remains Profitable — Five-Axis Machine Export Controls Pose Biggest Headwind finance.biggo.com", "truncated": false}, {"id": "05ffa2ff336e2fad92d839f5", "title": "China indicates rare earths will keep flowing to EU, regardless of U.S. trade deal expiration", "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/15/china-rare-earth-exports-europe.html", "source": "rss_cnbc_finance", "published_at": "2026-10-15T09:02:31+00:00", "text": "China indicates rare earths will keep flowing to EU, regardless of U.S. trade deal expiration\nChinese Commerce Ministry Spokesperson He Yadong said that China is willing to continue approving rare earth licenses to Europe.\nHe was responding to a CNBC question about the impact of a January deadline for the U.S.-China trade truce.\nEuropean trade commissioner Maroš Sefčovič met with Chinese Commerce Minister Wang Wentao in Beijing last week.\nEuropean Union flags flutter outside the EU Commission headquarters in Brussels, Belgium, on Feb. 1, 2023\nBEIJING — China intends to keep exporting rare earths to Europe regardless of whether a U.S. trade deal with Beijing gets extended past January.\nThe world's second-largest economy is willing to continue approving rare earth licenses to Europe, China's Commerce Ministry spokesperson He Yadong told CNBC when asked on Thursday about the impact of the upcoming U.S. deadline.\nBeijing last October tightened restrictions on all exports of rare earths — including products with even\nto the majority-owned subsidiaries of Chinese companies on an entity list, potentially affecting some\nHowever, both the U.S. and China agreed to\nat a meeting in late October 2025 between Chinese President Xi Jinping and U.S. President Donald Trump. Ahead of the leaders' latest summit last month, U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the truce was extended by two months to January.\nTrade tensions between the EU and Beijing cooled last week after European trade commissioner Maroš\nSefčovič met with Chinese Commerce Minister Wang\nto keep rare earths flowing to Europe, while asking for the bloc to support China's imports of certain products in dual-use sectors.\nEuropean Commission leaders are meeting in Brussels Thursday and Friday, and are expected to review details of the trade negotiations with China.\nChoose CNBC as your preferred source on Google and never miss a moment from the most trusted name in business news.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "ad1d4a41cc648a0257f998ce", "title": "Some Republicans in key races break with Trump over tariffs - NBC News", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxQcjYta20zcDI5RzJlVHNHYVZmVnRsRWM5U1gzTGJpMDI4M2xXQ3lhaWJPUEV5SzB1enpEaWF5dk5YaG5mQlBXcUprMVllWFdXNE5qZHBjeEVqTTZxVXJVR3hGQUswanBqeG9YU3ByNkNtdnFCUXBMOHFsdWtDNXJuakEwMG0yR0R3TTNjczZiWm1IcFpKV0FTaktrM2pmSGdD?oc=5", "source": "topic_geopolitics", "published_at": "2026-10-15T09:01:42+00:00", "text": "Some Republicans in key races break with Trump over tariffs - NBC News\nSome Republicans in key races break with Trump over tariffs NBC News", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8a89c6da6cf9cbca241acc77", "title": "Trump mocks affordability and praises high oil prices in tone-deaf rallies - MS NOW