ay Area\nLow temperatures and high oil prices could leave you with a huge energy bill this winter NBC Bay Area", "truncated": false}, {"id": "a8b85259cb3d77e30f1b8dab", "title": "Trump slaps 100% tariff on some pharmaceutical drugs via executive order - ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOVHNjYmZWRzV1Rno1QnBJdlAxR1Jjd1dGLTdTRHlUQnRUQmpCOUFJSDc0cFdCSy1heGE1SUc5R1k3WWJkZGFKZ01vYUQyaTM0bzgxSWJ5R2RVYjdQNjU2NjhVZ2lUZGtUM1Ffa0RQRjFPb2tvOFFCVXN1M1pPUnN1UTYwZVlWdXZWSkppX014QkJPQ0U4VDAzMzJGYnlKRURCemFWMVd6SVZTVGfSAbABQVVfeXFMT3pWWlhKeVJ4NHJ", "source": "lane_tax_fiscal", "published_at": "2026-10-14T22:19:15+00:00", "text": "Trump slaps 100% tariff on some pharmaceutical drugs via executive order - ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos\nTrump slaps 100% tariff on some pharmaceutical drugs via executive order ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos", "truncated": false}, {"id": "8ba3bd46be05f686c43250c3", "title": "At the Brooklyn shop in 'surreal' row with Kelly Clarkson over mechanical bird", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxvgdneplgzeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_world", "published_at": "2026-10-14T22:19:13+00:00", "text": "At the Brooklyn shop in 'surreal' row with Kelly Clarkson over mechanical bird\nWatch: What's going on between Kelly Clarkson and a Brooklyn store bird?\nOn a rainy Wednesday afternoon, a novelty toy and games store in a quiet part of New York City was seeing much busier foot traffic than usual.\nInside, the shop was packed with cameramen and customers, while passersby in this Brooklyn neighbourhood of Cobble Hill looked inside, asking: \"Where's the bird?\"\nArt of Play has found itself at the centre of a social media storm since the weekend when Grammy-winning musician Kelly Clarkson complained online that the boutique store would not let her buy a singing and dancing mechanical bird that was perched on the wall.\nThe Since U Been Gone singer claimed she was \"looked at as if I couldn't afford\" the bird - which she said had a price tag of $15,000 (Â£11,000).\n\"Y'all should go check out Art of Play in Brooklyn if you enjoy being treated like Julia Roberts' character in Pretty Woman,\" she said, referring to a scene from the 1990 romantic comedy film where Roberts' character is treated poorly by staff at a shop, who imply she cannot afford various items.\nIn a follow-up post on social media, Clarkson said the store had told her the bird cost $15,000 and that they could find her something else \"comparable\".\nArt of Play has defended how it treated the star on social media, saying the wooden bird - which is called Molly - is permanently attached to the wall and is not for sale.\nIt said that during Clarkson's five-minute visit on Saturday, an employee suggested to her that she could buy an identical bird for $15,000.\nThey also said they had offered her a different singing bird for $2,000 from a clock-making shop in Germany, which she could have purchased that day.\n\"Imagine our surprise when our small local business was suddenly attacked by eight million people who have never visited our store,\" Art of Play said.\n\"It's been a surreal experience to be the focus of such widespread outrage after just one mention by a celebrity.\"\nMolly the mechanical bird now has a price tag of $15m\nClarkson defended her decision to criticise the store on social media, saying: \"I never blast people but you my friend were an exception.\"\nWhen the BBC visited the store on Wednesday, there were more reporters than customers.\nA shopkeeper said they would not comment on the story anymore and just wanted to get back to business as usual.\nMolly still hung on the wall at the shop, this time next to a price tag of $15m.\nThe sign jokes that the sculpture is the \"world's most famous singing bird automata!\"\nThe store's owner has said he and his staff have faced threats and harassment after Clarkson's complaint, telling the BBC's US partner CBS News that the singer had endangered them.\nThis week, a man filmed himself yelling expletives outside the store, before accusing its employees of \"racially profiling\" Clarkson.\nCustomer Emily Trantanella likes Art of Play\nThe kerfuffle lingered in headlines on Wednesday as a news outlet released surveillance video from Art of Play purporting to show Clarkson's visit.\nThe grainy footage, which has no audio, is said to show her wearing a yellow shirt, a baseball cap and a backpack while browsing items, including Molly the bird.\nShe can be seen talking with an employee - apparently about the bird as she points at it - and later moving to leave the store. She comes back in to say something animatedly to the cashier.\nBut while the argument over the bird has gone viral online, some of Art of Play's customers had not heard about it before being greeted by news cameras on the premises.\nOne customer who was in town visiting his daughter said he was not familiar with the controversy.\nFor others, Clarkson's claims that those at the store had treated her rudely came as a surprise.\nKiran Ramineni, who lives next door, described Art of Play as a \"very nice small mom and pop store\" and said he had seen flocks of journalists there in recent days.\nShopgoer Emily Trantanella, 27, said: \"I feel like a pretty woman and I've always been treated very well here.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "04c63da45a38bbf41340c8ad", "title": "Appeals court lifts block on Florida law restricting social media access for teens - Florida Phoenix", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxOTEc5TlFxczZxazJtQ09Yd0pkQVlYV2RBbUV6WGVLMGRkR0tqU2k0bGtVdDFuZTZMVzRMeWhGS2JfT1ZZTjFIY2NBdllYc3V0MW9HSHpaWm9EMXFERU14dW0wVTc2WGdyU2FTT2pGVFNrajlJcGZnU1NQWkFOb0ZnQndJaVdPazlRTWQxbVBad0xHZTJFSnBuVFBMZnlZNktOUTctR1YxZWZsNm1tc2NxM2JvN2NYbHZfM2VSLTJn?oc", "source": "topic_judgments", "published_at": "2026-10-14T22:17:56+00:00", "tex