ast. - Stock Titan\nHome-loan volume rose 15.3% from a year earlier, while revenue missed the company's forecast. Stock Titan", "truncated": false}, {"id": "1d2a78946eae04d68d8840fe", "title": "Better Home & Finance Holding Company Announces Preliminary Third Quarter 2026 Results - Business Wire", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi2AFBVV95cUxNVFMwVkFOOXdueFZQM1lKTC14cm9EQmJjRU9ESWkyWUtVTG5YcnB1dXlBUHRYVzhSWWRkV3ZhMW9aM2hTeGxIZ0ZfVU1MaWJSeVQ5MFNGYUlNU2wwUXpRRGdRcV9HekhudlNPVFVOYXN6MWszamZTRW5oTHhNX0x1Yk1NT3NhWGxjRkVDVlptRDNxSDAxRXl5QXJmMkRvenkyU2hWbzRMTlBmREZWVEJ0azhRbk9IY2pQNTFMSTNZR2c", "source": "topic_corporate_announcements", "published_at": "2026-10-14T17:48:00+00:00", "text": "Better Home & Finance Holding Company Announces Preliminary Third Quarter 2026 Results - Business Wire\nBetter Home & Finance Holding Company Announces Preliminary Third Quarter 2026 Results Business Wire", "truncated": false}, {"id": "e8602edea19ee0dce7c4f25c", "title": "Drop-off charges at UK airports to be reviewed after sharp increase", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwp8gynk13rro?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "source": "rss_bbc_business", "published_at": "2026-10-14T17:46:30+00:00", "text": "Drop-off charges at UK airports to be reviewed after sharp increase\nAirport drop-off charges are to be reviewed by the government following sharp price increases in recent years.\nPrices at major UK airports have risen by a third since the summer of 2025 on average, according to one analysis, with Gatwick and Stansted drop-off charges found to be the most expensive, jumping from Â£7 to Â£10.\nSuch charges at Edinburgh Airport have risen from Â£6 to Â£8.50, while fees at Bournemouth increased from Â£5 to Â£8, the same price as Leeds Bradford and London City.\nThe Department for Transport confirmed it had committed to a review, saying it was \"vital to ensure travel remains accessible and that passengers are treated fairly\".\nThe government added it hoped airports would \"exercise restraint on rises, particularly where there are limited public transport alternatives\".\nThe RAC, which conducted the analysis in July this year, has campaigned against increases in drop-off charges. It said a review of \"kiss and fly\" fees would be \"music to the ears to drivers\".\n\"We know airport drop-off charges are a growing source of anger and frustration,\" said Rod Dennis, senior policy officer at the RAC.\n\"Four-in-five drivers we've surveyed believe they are a 'rip-off', with just one-in-10 understanding why airports charge what they do.\"\nThe RAC's research found London City Airport, which only introduced charges in 2026, was the most expensive on a per-minute basis.\nIts Â£8 charge for five minutes works out at Â£1.60 per minute. Belfast International Airport now charges Â£5 for 10 minutes in the drop-off zone, up Â£2 on last year.\nNone of the top 10 airports in the European Union charge for drop-offs, according to the RAC.\nIt argues that international airports should not charge for dropping off passengers, however, the industry said the charges were a neccesary part of the business model of airports.\nAirport drop-off fees up by a third - here are the priciest\nSupporters of such charges also say they encourage travellers to use of more environmentally friendly modes of transport.\n\"Airports outside the UK are typically publicly owned and in receipt of state subsidies and tax exemptions, while UK airports are generally privately owned and subject to the full array of commercial rates of taxation,\" said Karen Dee, chief executive of Airports UK, which represents airports.\nShe added airports offered a \"range of options for those travelling to terminals, including free drop off points\" and that \"any review\" by the government would find airports make \"excellent use of a variety of ways to manage traffic and air pollution\".\nThe Aviation Environment Federation campaign group has previously defended the fees, arguing they help reduce congestion and air pollution around airports.\nEarlier this month, the government announced extra charges for parents sitting with their children when flying would be scrapped in time for next year's summer holidays.\nPrime Minister Andy Burnham said the changes were part of a series of \"everyday fixes\" to ease cost of living pressures on households.\nHave you been affected by issues covered in this story? Share your experiences.", "truncated": false, "full_text": true}, {"id": "ed4253eefdead2d4dddf850e", "title": "Trump administration cuts ACA subsidies for 189,000 enrollees By Investing.com - Investing.com South Africa", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxNS2VIZ0M0YjlkT2ljMEFGcm9udEppNE1kSXJ0T2pXM2FzaVVLa3N6TjhENFRDeTlJTUdxZzVoZEFTMXRXR3A4UUNIWmktdFlsaUdFaWNncTl1YW5aVW4yWEtsQ0h6eUk2STdaZ0xzdHdnME9zV3dfNUoxeXJkcXFOWkNXVjJfXzJLVXVuRlliOVJWNGlUYnRjR1h6cVlqTUdLV0RhSklkX05jSlBiWVdVcnJnUFRTaTBXanBxdENR?oc", "source": "lane_subsidy", "published_at": "2026-10-14T17:46:16+00:00", "text": "Trump administration cuts ACA subsidies for 189,000 enrollees By Investing.com - Investing.com South Africa\nTrump administration cuts ACA subsidies for 189,000 enrollees By Investing.com Investing.com South Africa", "truncated": false}, {"id": "f922e8bcd66765c694cc385b", "title": "Senate passes bill to establish Federal Teaching Hospital in Manchok - Daily Post Nigeria", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPdmQ3bWViWmVNeTB6RUdpQlotUmpiMWJ3ODM1eklLaXpUczFJZW5uLUhMUmd2aGNoQWFyWm0tMWlnYXVHaVhTZnhpMDJWUWxWdWR4ek1TaEF5RFY4dXRlUXN1X0VnMU9YRzRrYU9lU0Jwdkw0NGZ3dERiQnBzWW9wMDhUaExjbERTbE8wRG03d1J6MmRMTE1PQzB0TldXVjFiMW1N?oc=5", "source": "topic_legislation", "published_at": "2026-10-14T17:45:32+00:00", "text": "Senate passes bill to establish Federal Teaching Hospital in Manchok - Daily Post Nigeria\nSenate passes bill to establish Federal Teaching Hospital in Manchok Daily Post Nigeria", "truncated": false}, {"id": "9afe9b8bc8d0f597f2be